<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.1">
<book code="PSA" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">Psalm</para>

<para style="toc1">Psalm</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="PSA 1"/>

<para style="s">BOOK I</para>

<para style="s">Psalms 1–41</para>

<para style="s">The Two Paths</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 6:20–23</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 5:3–12</char></note>Blessed <char style="add">is</char> the man </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 1:1">who does not walk in the counsel of the wicked, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 1:1">and in the path of sinners does not stand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 1:1">and in the seat of those mocking does not sit. <verse eid="PSA 1:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 1:2"/>But rather his delight <char style="add">is</char> in the law of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 1:2">and in His law he meditates day and night. <verse eid="PSA 1:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 1:3"/>And he is like a tree planted by streams of water, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 1:3">which gives its fruit in its time; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 1:3">and its leaf shall not wither, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 1:3">and all that he does, he makes prosper. <verse eid="PSA 1:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 1:4"/>Not so the wicked! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 1:4">But rather <char style="add">they are</char> like the chaff, which the wind drives away. <verse eid="PSA 1:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 1:5"/>Upon thus the wicked shall not stand in the judgment, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 1:5">nor the sinful ones in the assembly of the righteous. <verse eid="PSA 1:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 1:6"/>For YHWH knows the way of the righteous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 1:6">and the way of the wicked shall perish. <verse eid="PSA 1:6"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 1"/>

<chapter number="2" style="c" sid="PSA 2"/>

<para style="s">The Triumphant Messiah</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 2:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 4:23–31</char></note>Why do the nations rage,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">noisily assemble</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Revelation 11:18.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:1">and the peoples plot in vain? <verse eid="PSA 2:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 2:2"/>The kings of the earth take their stand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:2">and the rulers establish themselves together </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 2:2">against YHWH </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:2">and against His Anointed:<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Acts 4:25–26</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 2:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 2:3"/>“Let us tear off their bonds, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:3">and cast away from us their cords.” <verse eid="PSA 2:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 2:4"/>The One sitting in the heavens laughs; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:4">the Lord scoffs at them. <verse eid="PSA 2:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 2:5"/>Then He speaks to them in His anger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:5">and in his fury He terrifies them: <verse eid="PSA 2:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 2:6"/>“And I have installed My King on Zion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:6">the mountain of My holiness.” <verse eid="PSA 2:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 2:7"/>I will recount the decree of YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:7">He has said to Me: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 2:7">“You <char style="add">are</char> My Son; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:7">today I have begotten You. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Acts 13:33, Hebrews 1:5, and Hebrews 5:5</char></note><verse eid="PSA 2:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 2:8"/>Ask from Me and I will give the nations <char style="add">as</char> Your inheritance, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:8">and the ends of the earth <char style="add">for</char> Your possession. <verse eid="PSA 2:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 2:9"/>You will break them with a rod of iron; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:9">You will shatter them like a vessel of a potter.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">You will rule them</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">You will shepherd them</char></note>” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Revelation 2:27; see also Revelation 12:5 and Revelation 19:15.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 2:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 2:10"/>And now, O kings, be prudent; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:10">be admonished, O judges of the earth. <verse eid="PSA 2:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 2:11"/>Serve YHWH with fear, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:11">and rejoice with trembling. <verse eid="PSA 2:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 2:12"/>Kiss the Son, lest He be angry, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:12">and you⁺ perish <char style="add">in</char> the way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 2:12">when His wrath is kindled in an instant. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 2:12">Blessed <char style="add">are</char> all those taking refuge in Him. <verse eid="PSA 2:12"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 2"/>

<chapter number="3" style="c" sid="PSA 3"/>

<para style="s">Deliver Me, O LORD!</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of David, in his fleeing from the face of Absalom his son.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 3:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Samuel 15:13–29</char></note> O YHWH, how many are my adversaries! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 3:1">Many <char style="add">are</char> rising up against me! <verse eid="PSA 3:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 3:2"/>Many are saying of my soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 3:2">“There is no salvation for him in God.” </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 3:2">Selah<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Selah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Interlude</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or literary term; here and throughout the Psalms.</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 3:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 3:3"/>and You, O YHWH, are a shield behind me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 3:3">my glory, and One lifting high my head. <verse eid="PSA 3:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 3:4"/>With my voice I cry to YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 3:4">and He answers me from the mountain of His holiness. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 3:4">Selah <verse eid="PSA 3:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 3:5"/>I lie down and sleep; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 3:5">I awake, for YHWH sustains me. <verse eid="PSA 3:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 3:6"/>I shall not fear the multitudes of people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 3:6">who have set <char style="add">themselves</char> all around against me. <verse eid="PSA 3:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 3:7"/>Arise, O YHWH! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 3:7">Save me, O my God! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 3:7">O that You would strike all my enemies <char style="add">on</char> the jaw; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 3:7">may you break the teeth of the wicked! <verse eid="PSA 3:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 3:8"/>Unto YHWH <char style="add">is</char> the salvation; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 3:8">may Your blessing <char style="add">be</char> upon Your people. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 3:8">Selah <verse eid="PSA 3:8"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 3"/>

<chapter number="4" style="c" sid="PSA 4"/>

<para style="s">Answer Me When I Call!</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. With stringed instruments. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 4:1"/> In my calling out, may You answer me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 4:1">O God of my righteousness! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 4:1">In <char style="add">my</char> distress, You widened <char style="add">it</char> for me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 4:1">show me favor and hear my prayer. <verse eid="PSA 4:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 4:2"/>O sons of men, until when will my glory be shame? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 4:2">Will you⁺ love vanity, <char style="add">and</char> seek after falsehood?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">false gods</char></note> </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 4:2">Selah <verse eid="PSA 4:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 4:3"/>and know that YHWH has marked out the faithful one for Himself; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 4:3">YHWH hears in my calling to Him. <verse eid="PSA 4:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 4:4"/>Tremble and do not sin; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 4:4">speak in your⁺ heart on your⁺ bed, and be silent. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 4:4">Selah <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">In your anger do not sin</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Tremble and do not sin</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Ephesians 4:26</char></note><verse eid="PSA 4:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 4:5"/>Sacrifice the sacrifices of righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 4:5">and trust in YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 4:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 4:6"/>Many are saying, “Who will show us good?” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 4:6">Lift upon us the light of Your face, O YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 4:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 4:7"/>You have put joy in my heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 4:7">more than the time when their grain and their new wine have increased. <verse eid="PSA 4:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 4:8"/>In peace I will both lie down and will sleep, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 4:8">for You alone, O YHWH, cause me to dwell in safety. <verse eid="PSA 4:8"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 4"/>

<chapter number="5" style="c" sid="PSA 5"/>

<para style="s">Give Ear to My Words</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. With the Nehiloth. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 5:1"/> Give ear to my words, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:1">have regard <char style="add">for</char> my murmuring. <verse eid="PSA 5:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 5:2"/>Be attentive to the voice of my cry, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:2">O my King and my God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:2">for to You I pray. <verse eid="PSA 5:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 5:3"/>O YHWH, in the morning You hear my voice; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:3">in the morning I direct <char style="add">it</char> to You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:3">and I keep watch. <verse eid="PSA 5:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 5:4"/>For You <char style="add">are</char> not a God delighting in wickedness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:4">evil shall not sojourn with You. <verse eid="PSA 5:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 5:5"/>The one boasting shall not stand in Your sight; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:5">You hate all workers of iniquity. <verse eid="PSA 5:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 5:6"/>You will destroy those speaking falsehood; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:6">a man of blood and deceit YHWH abhors. <verse eid="PSA 5:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 5:7"/>But I, in the abundance of Your loving devotion,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Forms of the Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">chesed</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> are translated here and in most cases throughout the Scriptures as </char><char style="fq" closed="false">loving devotion</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; the range of meaning includes </char><char style="fq" closed="false">love</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">goodness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">kindness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">faithfulness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, and </char><char style="fq" closed="false">mercy</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, as well as </char><char style="fq" closed="false">loyalty to a covenant</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:7">will come into Your house; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 5:7">I will bow down toward the temple of Your Holiness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:7">in fear of You. <verse eid="PSA 5:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 5:8"/>O YHWH, guide me in Your righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:8">on account of my enemies; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:8">make straight Your path before my face. <verse eid="PSA 5:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 5:9"/>For there is no firmness in his mouth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:9">within them is destruction; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 5:9">their throat <char style="add">is</char> a grave being wide open; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:9">they make their tongue smooth. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they practice flattery</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Romans 3:13</char></note><verse eid="PSA 5:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 5:10"/>Declare them guilty, O God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:10">let them fall by their own devices; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 5:10">in the abundance of their transgressions drive them away, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:10">for they have rebelled against You. <verse eid="PSA 5:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 5:11"/>And let all those taking refuge in You rejoice forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:11">let them shout for joy, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 5:11">and may You cover them over; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:11">and let those loving Your name exult in You. <verse eid="PSA 5:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 5:12"/>For You will bless the righteous one, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 5:12">as a shield You will surround him with favor. <verse eid="PSA 5:12"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 5"/>

<chapter number="6" style="c" sid="PSA 6"/>

<para style="s">Do Not Rebuke Me in Your Anger</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. With stringed instruments according to Sheminith.† A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 6:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 38:1–22</char></note> O YHWH, in Your anger do not rebuke me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 6:1">and do not discipline me in Your rage. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Sheminith</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical term; here and in 1 Chronicles 15:21 and Psalm 12:1.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 6:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 6:2"/>Be gracious to me, O YHWH, for I <char style="add">am</char> weak; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 6:2">heal me, O YHWH, for my bones are disturbed. <verse eid="PSA 6:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 6:3"/>And my soul is disturbed greatly; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 6:3">and You, O YHWH, until when? <verse eid="PSA 6:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 6:4"/>Return, O YHWH, draw out my soul; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 6:4">save me for the sake of Your loving devotion. <verse eid="PSA 6:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 6:5"/>For in death <char style="add">is</char> no remembrance of You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 6:5">in Sheol, who can give thanks to You? <verse eid="PSA 6:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 6:6"/>I have grown weary in my sighing; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 6:6">I cause my bed to swim through all the night; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 6:6">with my tears I melt my couch. <verse eid="PSA 6:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 6:7"/>My eye has wasted away from grief; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 6:7">it grows old because of all afflicting me. <verse eid="PSA 6:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 6:8"/>Turn away from me, all workers of iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 6:8">for YHWH has heard the voice of my weeping. <verse eid="PSA 6:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 6:9"/>YHWH has heard my supplication; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 6:9">YHWH has received my prayer. <verse eid="PSA 6:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 6:10"/>Let all my enemies be ashamed and disturbed greatly; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 6:10">let them turn back <char style="add">and</char> be ashamed in an instant. <verse eid="PSA 6:10"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 6"/>

<chapter number="7" style="c" sid="PSA 7"/>

<para style="s">I Take Refuge in You</para>

<para style="s">A Shiggaion† of David, which he sang to YHWH, concerning the words of Cush, the Benjamite.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 7:1"/> O YHWH my God, in You I have taken refuge; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:1">keep me safe from all those pursuing me, and deliver me, <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shiggaion</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 7:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 7:2"/>lest they tear my soul like a lion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:2">tearing apart, and there is no one snatching me up. <verse eid="PSA 7:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 7:3"/>O YHWH my God, if I have done this, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:3">if there is injustice in my palms, <verse eid="PSA 7:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 7:4"/>if I have dealt with the one at peace with me<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with my ally</char></note> with evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:4">or have drawn out my enemy without cause, <verse eid="PSA 7:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 7:5"/>may the enemy pursue my soul and overtake it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:5">and let him trample my life to the ground, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:5">and let him set down my honor in the dust. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 7:5">Selah <verse eid="PSA 7:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 7:6"/>arise, O YHWH, in Your anger; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:6">lift up against the fury of my adversaries, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:6">and rouse Yourself for me; You have appointed a judgment. <verse eid="PSA 7:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 7:7"/>And let the congregation of peoples surround You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:7">and over it return in the heights. <verse eid="PSA 7:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 7:8"/>YHWH shall judge the peoples; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:8">Judge me, O YHWH, according to my righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:8">and according to my integrity within me. <verse eid="PSA 7:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 7:9"/>Please, let the evil of the wicked cease, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:9">and may you establish the righteous—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:9">even the One testing hearts and kidneys, O Righteous God. <verse eid="PSA 7:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 7:10"/>My shield <char style="add">is</char> on God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:10">the One saving the upright of heart. <verse eid="PSA 7:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 7:11"/>God <char style="add">is</char> a righteous judge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:11">and a God expressing wrath on every day. <verse eid="PSA 7:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 7:12"/>If one shall not turn back, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:12"><char style="add">then</char> He sharpens His sword; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:12">He has bent His bow and prepared <char style="add">it</char>. <verse eid="PSA 7:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 7:13"/>And for Himself He has prepared instruments of death; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:13">His arrows He makes into fiery shafts. <verse eid="PSA 7:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 7:14"/>Behold, he travails <char style="add">with</char> evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:14">and he conceives trouble, and brings forth falsehood. <verse eid="PSA 7:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 7:15"/>He has dug a pit and hollowed it out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:15">and he has fallen into a pit he has made. <verse eid="PSA 7:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 7:16"/>His trouble shall return upon his head, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:16">and on the top of his head, his violence shall come down. <verse eid="PSA 7:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 7:17"/>I will confess YHWH according to His righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 7:17">and I will sing praise <char style="add">to</char> the name of YHWH-Elyon.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">YHWH-Elyon</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">LORD Most High</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 7:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 7"/>

<chapter number="8" style="c" sid="PSA 8"/>

<para style="s">How Majestic Is Your Name!</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. According to Gittith.† A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 8:1"/> O YHWH our Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 8:1">how majestic <char style="add">is</char> Your name in all the earth, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 8:1">who have set Your splendor </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 8:1">above the heavens! <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Gittith</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; here and in Psalms 81 and 84.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 8:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 8:2"/>From the mouth of infants and sucklings </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 8:2">You have established strength, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 8:2">on account of Your adversaries, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 8:2">to still the enemy and avenger. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">You have prepared praise</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Matthew 21:16</char></note><verse eid="PSA 8:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 8:3"/>When I see Your heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 8:3">the works of Your fingers, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 8:3">the moon and the stars </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 8:3">that You have established— <verse eid="PSA 8:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 8:4"/>what <char style="add">is</char> man that You should remember him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 8:4">and the son of man, that You would attend to him? <verse eid="PSA 8:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 8:5"/>And You made him lacking a little from the angels, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 8:5">and with glory and honor You crowned him. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">than God</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">than the heavenly beings</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see also LXX.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 8:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 8:6"/>You made him to rule over the works of Your hands; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 8:6">You have placed everything under his feet: <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in 1 Corinthians 15:27 and Hebrews 2:6–8</char></note><verse eid="PSA 8:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 8:7"/>All sheep and cattle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 8:7">and also the beasts of the field, <verse eid="PSA 8:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 8:8"/>the birds of the heavens and the fish of the sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 8:8">those passing <char style="add">on</char> the paths of the seas. <verse eid="PSA 8:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 8:9"/>O YHWH, our Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 8:9">how majestic <char style="add">is</char> Your name in all the earth! <verse eid="PSA 8:9"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 8"/>

<chapter number="9" style="c" sid="PSA 9"/>

<para style="s">I Will Give Thanks to Yahweh</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. According to Muth-Labben. A Psalm of David.†</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 9:1"/> I will confess YHWH with all of my heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:1">I will recount all Your wonders. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalms 9 and 10 together follow an acrostic pattern, each stanza beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet. In the LXX they form one psalm.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 9:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 9:2"/>I will be glad and rejoice in You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:2">I will sing praise <char style="add">to</char> Your name, O Most High. <verse eid="PSA 9:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 9:3"/>In turning back my enemies </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:3">they shall stumble and shall perish from Your face. <verse eid="PSA 9:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 9:4"/>For You have done my justice and my claim; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:4">You have sat on the throne, judging <char style="add">with</char> righteousness. <verse eid="PSA 9:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 9:5"/>You have rebuked the nations; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:5">You have destroyed the wicked; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:5">their name You have wiped out forever and ever. <verse eid="PSA 9:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 9:6"/>May the enemy be finished in ruins forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:6">and You have uprooted cities; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:6">let their remembrance perish with them! <verse eid="PSA 9:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 9:7"/>And YHWH shall sit forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:7">He has established His throne for the judgment. <verse eid="PSA 9:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 9:8"/>And He will judge the world in righteousness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:8">He shall make judgment <char style="add">for</char> the peoples in uprightness. <verse eid="PSA 9:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 9:9"/>And YHWH will be a secure height for the oppressed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:9">a secure height in times of distress. <verse eid="PSA 9:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 9:10"/>And they will put their trust in You—those knowing Your name—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:10">for You have not forsaken those seeking You, O YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 9:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 9:11"/>Sing praise to YHWH, the One sitting <char style="add">in</char> Zion; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:11">declare His deeds among the peoples. <verse eid="PSA 9:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 9:12"/>For the One seeking out the blood remembers them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:12">He does not forget the cry of the afflicted. <verse eid="PSA 9:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 9:13"/>Show favor to me, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:13">see my affliction from those hating me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 9:13">raise me high from the gates of death, <verse eid="PSA 9:13"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 9:14"/>so that I may recount all Your praises </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 9:14">in the gates of the daughter of Zion. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:14">I will rejoice in Your salvation. <verse eid="PSA 9:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 9:15"/>The nations have sunk down into the pit they have made; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:15">in the net that they hid, their foot is caught. <verse eid="PSA 9:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 9:16"/>YHWH is known by the justice He has done; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:16">by the work of his own hands the wicked one is snared. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 9:16">Higgaion Selah<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Higgaion Selah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">quiet interlude</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term.</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 9:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 9:17"/>the wicked shall return to Sheol—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:17">all the nations forgetting God. <verse eid="PSA 9:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 9:18"/>For the needy will not be forgotten forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:18"><char style="add">nor</char> the hope of the poor perish to the <char style="add">end</char>. <verse eid="PSA 9:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 9:19"/>Arise, O YHWH! Do not let man prevail; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:19">let the nations be judged before Your face. <verse eid="PSA 9:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 9:20"/>Put fear on them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 9:20">O YHWH; let the nations know they <char style="add">are</char> mortal. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 9:20">Selah <verse eid="PSA 9:20"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 9"/>

<chapter number="10" style="c" sid="PSA 10"/>

<para style="s">The Perils of the Pilgrim</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 10:1"/>Why, O YHWH, do You stand far off? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:1">Do You hide in times of distress? <verse eid="PSA 10:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 10:2"/>In <char style="add">his</char> arrogance, the wicked hotly pursue the afflicted; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:2">may they be caught in the schemes that they have devised! <verse eid="PSA 10:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 10:3"/>For the wicked one boasts over the desire of his heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:3">and he blesses a dishonest gainer; he has despised YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 10:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 10:4"/>The wicked one, in the height of his face, does not inquire; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:4">there is no God <char style="add">in</char> any of his thoughts. <verse eid="PSA 10:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 10:5"/>His paths are firm at every time; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:5">Your judgments <char style="add">are</char> on high before him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:5"><char style="add">and</char> all his adversaries, he sneers at them. <verse eid="PSA 10:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 10:6"/>He has said in his heart, “I shall not be moved—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:6">from generation to generation—to whom <char style="add">will be</char> no adversity.” <verse eid="PSA 10:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 10:7"/>His mouth is full of cursing and deceit<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">full of an oath</char></note> and oppression; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:7">under his tongue <char style="add">are</char> trouble and iniquity. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">bitterness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Romans 3:14</char></note><verse eid="PSA 10:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 10:8"/>He sits in an ambush of the villages; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:8">in the hidden places he kills the innocent one; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:8">his eyes look stealthily on the helpless. <verse eid="PSA 10:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 10:9"/>He lies in wait in the hidden place, like a lion in his lair; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:9">he lies in wait to catch the afflicted one; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:9">he catches the afflicted one by drawing him into his net. <verse eid="PSA 10:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 10:10"/>He is crushed; he bows down,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He crouche; he lies low</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:10">and the hapless one falls by his strength. <verse eid="PSA 10:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 10:11"/>He has said in his heart, “God has forgotten; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:11">He hides His face; He will not see <char style="add">it</char> forever.” <verse eid="PSA 10:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 10:12"/>Arise, O YHWH! O God, lift up Your hand! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:12">You must not forget the afflicted ones. <verse eid="PSA 10:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 10:13"/>Upon what does the wicked spurn God? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:13">He has said in his heart, “You will not call <char style="add">me</char> to account.” <verse eid="PSA 10:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 10:14"/>Indeed you You have seen; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:14">You regard trouble and grief, to give <char style="add">it</char> into Your hand. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 10:14">The hapless one leaves himself to You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:14">for You are the One helping the fatherless. <verse eid="PSA 10:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 10:15"/>Break the arm of the wicked and evildoer! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:15">Seek out his wickedness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:15"><char style="add">until</char> none is found. <verse eid="PSA 10:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 10:16"/>YHWH <char style="add">is</char> King forever and ever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:16">the nations have perished from His land. <verse eid="PSA 10:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 10:17"/>The desire of the afflicted ones You have heard, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:17">You will make firm their hearts; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 10:17">You will incline Your ear, <verse eid="PSA 10:17"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 10:18"/>to do justice for the fatherless and oppressed; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 10:18">he shall not continue anymore to terrorize—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 10:18">the man from the earth, <verse eid="PSA 10:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 10"/>

<chapter number="11" style="c" sid="PSA 11"/>

<para style="s">In Yahweh I Take Refuge</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 11:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Habakkuk 1:12–17</char></note> In YHWH I have taken refuge. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 11:1">How can you⁺ say to my soul, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 11:1">“Flee to your⁺ mountain a bird! <verse eid="PSA 11:1"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 11:2"/>For, behold, the wicked tread the bow; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 11:2">they make ready their arrow upon the string, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 11:2">to shoot in the darkness at those upright in heart. <verse eid="PSA 11:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 11:3"/>If the foundations are thrown down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 11:3">the righteous—what can he do?” <verse eid="PSA 11:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 11:4"/>YHWH <char style="add">is</char> is in His holy temple; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 11:4">YHWH—in the heavens <char style="add">is</char> His throne. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 11:4">His eyes are watching, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 11:4">His eyelids examine the sons of man. <verse eid="PSA 11:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 11:5"/>YHWH tests the righteous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 11:5">and His soul hates the wicked one and the lover of violence. <verse eid="PSA 11:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 11:6"/>May He rain <char style="add">down</char> coals upon the wicked, fire and brimstone; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 11:6">and a burning wind <char style="add">is</char> the portion of their cup. <verse eid="PSA 11:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 11:7"/>For YHWH <char style="add">is</char> righteous; He loves righteousness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 11:7">the upright one will see His face. <verse eid="PSA 11:7"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 11"/>

<chapter number="12" style="c" sid="PSA 12"/>

<para style="s">The Godly Are No More</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. According to Sheminith.† A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 12:1"/> Help, O YHWH! For the godly one ceases <char style="add">to be</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 12:1">for the faithful ones disappear from the sons of man. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Sheminith</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical term; here and in 1 Chronicles 15:21 and Psalm 6:1.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 12:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 12:2"/>Vanity they speak, each man with his neighbor; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 12:2"><char style="add">with</char> lips of flattery with a double heart they speak. <verse eid="PSA 12:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 12:3"/>May YHWH cut off all lips of flattery, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 12:3">a tongue speaking great <char style="add">things</char>— <verse eid="PSA 12:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 12:4"/>those who have said, “By our tongues we will prevail; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 12:4">our lips <char style="add">are</char> with us; who <char style="add">is</char> lord over us?” <verse eid="PSA 12:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 12:5"/>“From the oppression of the poor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 12:5">from the groaning of the needy, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 12:5">now I shall arise,” says YHWH. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 12:5">“I will set in safety <char style="add">him who</char> breathes for it.” <verse eid="PSA 12:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 12:6"/>The words of YHWH <char style="add">are</char> pure words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 12:6">silver refined in a furnace of earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 12:6">purified sevenfold.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">silver refined in a furnace, gold purified sevenfold</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 12:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 12:7"/>You, O YHWH, shall keep them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 12:7">You will guard them from this generation forever. <verse eid="PSA 12:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 12:8"/>On every side the wicked walk, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 12:8">as vileness is exalted by the sons of man. <verse eid="PSA 12:8"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 12"/>

<chapter number="13" style="c" sid="PSA 13"/>

<para style="s">How Long, O LORD?</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 13:1"/> Until when, O YHWH? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 13:1">Will You forget me forever? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 13:1">Until when will You hide Your face from me? <verse eid="PSA 13:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 13:2"/>Until when shall I set counsel in my soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 13:2"><char style="add">and</char> sorrow in my heart daily? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 13:2">Until when will my enemy be raised high over me? <verse eid="PSA 13:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 13:3"/>Look attentively; answer me, O YHWH my God! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 13:3">Give light to my eyes, lest I sleep in death, <verse eid="PSA 13:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 13:4"/>lest my enemy say, “I have prevailed against him.” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 13:4">My adversaries rejoice because I am shaken. <verse eid="PSA 13:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 13:5"/>Yet I have trusted in Your loving devotion; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 13:5">My heart will rejoice in Your salvation. <verse eid="PSA 13:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 13:6"/>I will sing to YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 13:6">because He has dealt bountifully with me. <verse eid="PSA 13:6"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 13"/>

<chapter number="14" style="c" sid="PSA 14"/>

<para style="s">The Fool Says There Is No God</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 14:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Romans 3:9–20</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Isaiah 59:1–17</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 53:1–6</char></note> The fool<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The Hebrew words rendered </char><char style="fq" closed="false">fool</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> throughout the Psalms denote one who is morally deficient.</char></note> says in his heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 14:1">“There is no God.” </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 14:1">They are corrupt; they have done abominable deeds; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 14:1">there is no one doing good. <verse eid="PSA 14:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 14:2"/>YHWH looks down from the heavens </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 14:2">upon the sons of man, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 14:2">to see, is there one understanding, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 14:2">seeking God? <verse eid="PSA 14:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 14:3"/>All have turned aside, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 14:3">together they have become corrupt;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">worthless</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 14:3">there is no one doing good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 14:3">not even one.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 3:10–12</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 14:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 14:4"/>All those working iniquity, have they not know? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 14:4">They devour my people they have eaten bread; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 14:4">on YHWH they do not call. <verse eid="PSA 14:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 14:5"/>There they tremble with dread, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 14:5">for God <char style="add">is</char> in the generation of the righteous. <verse eid="PSA 14:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 14:6"/>The counsel of the poor you⁺ have shamed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 14:6">for YHWH <char style="add">is</char> his place of refuge. <verse eid="PSA 14:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 14:7"/>Who gives from Zion the salvation of Israel? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 14:7">In YHWH turning back the captivity of His people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 14:7">let Jacob rejoice; let Israel be glad! <verse eid="PSA 14:7"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 14"/>

<chapter number="15" style="c" sid="PSA 15"/>

<para style="s">Who may Dwell on Your Holy Mountain?</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 15:1"/> O YHWH, who may sojourn in Your tent? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 15:1">Who may dwell in the mountain of Your Holiness? <verse eid="PSA 15:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 15:2"/>The one walking blamelessly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 15:2">and doing righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 15:2">and speaking truth in his heart. <verse eid="PSA 15:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 15:3"/>He does not have slander upon his tongue, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 15:3">and he has not done evil to his neighbor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 15:3">and a reproach he has not taken up against his neighbor. <verse eid="PSA 15:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 15:4"/>A rejected one is despised in his eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 15:4">and those fearful of YHWH he honors—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 15:4">one <char style="add">who</char> swears to endure evil, and not changing. <verse eid="PSA 15:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 15:5"/>His silver he has not given in usury, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 15:5">and he does not take a bribe against the innocent. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 15:5">The one doing these <char style="add">things</char> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 15:5">is not shaken forever. <verse eid="PSA 15:5"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 15"/>

<chapter number="16" style="c" sid="PSA 16"/>

<para style="s">The Presence of Yahweh</para>

<para style="s">A Miktam† of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 16:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 2:14–36</char></note> Preserve me, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:1">for I take refuge in You. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Miktam</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalm 16 and Psalms 56–60.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 16:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 16:2"/>I said to YHWH, “You <char style="add">are</char> my Lord. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:2">My goodness <char style="add">is</char> nothing apart from You.” <verse eid="PSA 16:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 16:3"/>As for the holy ones who <char style="add">are</char> in the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:3">they and the excellent ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:3">all my delight <char style="add">is</char> in them. <verse eid="PSA 16:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 16:4"/>May their sorrows be multiplied, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:4">those who hurry <char style="add">after</char> another! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 16:4">I will not pour out their drink offerings of blood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:4">and I will not lift up their names upon my lips. <verse eid="PSA 16:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 16:5"/>YHWH, <char style="add">is</char> the portion of my share, and my cup; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:5">You <char style="add">are</char> the One upholding my lot. <verse eid="PSA 16:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 16:6"/>The lines have fallen to me in the pleasant <char style="add">places</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:6">indeed, a pleasing inheritance <char style="add">is</char> unto me. <verse eid="PSA 16:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 16:7"/>I will bless YHWH, who counsels me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:7">even <char style="add">in</char> the nights, my kidneys instruct me.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">my conscience instructs me</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 16:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 16:8"/>I have set YHWH before me continually; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:8">because <char style="add">He is</char> at my right hand, I will not be shaken. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I foresaw</char></note><verse eid="PSA 16:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 16:9"/>Therefore my heart is glad and my glory rejoices; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:9">my flesh also will dwell securely.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">will dwell in hope</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 16:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 16:10"/>For You will not abandon my soul to Sheol, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:10">and You will not give Your Holy one to see corruption. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Acts 13:35</char></note><verse eid="PSA 16:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 16:11"/>You make known to me the path of life; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:11">fullness of joys <char style="add">is</char> with Your face,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Acts 2:25–28</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 16:11">pleasant <char style="add">things</char> <char style="add">are</char> at Your right hand forever. <verse eid="PSA 16:11"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 16"/>

<chapter number="17" style="c" sid="PSA 17"/>

<para style="s">Hear My Righteous Plea</para>

<para style="s">A Prayer of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 17:1"/> Hear, O YHWH, a just cause; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:1">attend to my cry; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 17:1">give ear to my prayer </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:1">without lips of deceit. <verse eid="PSA 17:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 17:2"/>From before Your face, let my judgment come forth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:2">may Your eyes see uprightness. <verse eid="PSA 17:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 17:3"/>You have tested my heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:3">You have inspected in the night. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 17:3">You have refined me without Your finding, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:3"><char style="add">for</char> I have purposed <char style="add">that</char> my mouth shall not transgress. <verse eid="PSA 17:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 17:4"/>As for the works of men, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:4">by the word of Your lips </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:4">I have kept myself <char style="add">from</char> the ways of a violent one. <verse eid="PSA 17:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 17:5"/>To uphold my steps on Your paths, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:5">my footsteps are not shaken. <verse eid="PSA 17:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 17:6"/>I call on You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:6">for You will answer me, O God! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 17:6">Incline Your ear to me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:6">hear my word. <verse eid="PSA 17:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 17:7"/>Set apart Your loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:7">You who save those taking refuge from the assailants—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:7">with Your right hand. <verse eid="PSA 17:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 17:8"/>May you guard me as the pupil, the daughter of Your eye; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:8">hide me in the shadow of Your wings, <verse eid="PSA 17:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 17:9"/>from wicked ones who would ruin me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:9">my enemies in soul go around against me. <verse eid="PSA 17:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 17:10"/>Their fat they have closed up; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:10">their mouths they speak with pride. <verse eid="PSA 17:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 17:11"/>In our steps now they have surrounded us; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:11">they have set their eyes to cast <char style="add">us</char> to the ground. <verse eid="PSA 17:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 17:12"/>His likeness <char style="add">is</char> as a lion longing to tear, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:12">and like a young lion lurking in hidden places. <verse eid="PSA 17:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 17:13"/>Arise, O YHWH! Go before his face; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:13">cast him down, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 17:13"><char style="add">and</char> rescue my soul from the wicked by your sword, <verse eid="PSA 17:13"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 17:14"/>from men by Your hand, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 17:14">from men of the world—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:14">their portion <char style="add">is</char> in this life. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 17:14">And Your treasured ones, You fill their belly;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">May what You have stored up for the wicked fill their bellies</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:14">they are satisfied <char style="add">with</char> sons, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:14">and they leave their remainder to their children. <verse eid="PSA 17:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 17:15"/>I, in righteousness, will see Your face; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 17:15">in <char style="add">my</char> waking, I will be satisfied <char style="add">with</char> Your form. <verse eid="PSA 17:15"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 17"/>

<chapter number="18" style="c" sid="PSA 18"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Is My Rock</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. Of the servant of YHWH, David, who spoke to YHWH the words of this song on the day that YHWH snatched him from the hand of all his enemies, from the hand of Saul. 1 And he said:</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 18:2"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Samuel 22:1–51</char></note>YHWH <char style="add">is</char> my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:2">My God <char style="add">is</char> my rock—I take refuge in Him—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 18:2">my protection, and the horn of my salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:2">my high place. <verse eid="PSA 18:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 18:3"/>I will call upon YHWH, to be praised, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:3">and I shall be saved from my enemies. <verse eid="PSA 18:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 18:4"/>The cords of Death surrounded me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:4">and the torrents of Belial terrified me. <verse eid="PSA 18:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 18:5"/>The cords of Sheol surrounded me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:5">the snares of Death confronted me. <verse eid="PSA 18:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 18:6"/>In the distress unto me, I called to YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:6">and to my God I cried for help. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 18:6">From His temple He heard my voice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:6">and my cry for help came before His face into His ears. <verse eid="PSA 18:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 18:7"/>And the earth shook and quaked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:7">and the foundations of the hills trembled; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:7">and they were shaken because of the burning from Him. <verse eid="PSA 18:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 18:8"/>Smoke went up from His nostril, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:8">and a devouring fire from His mouth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:8">coals were kindled from it. <verse eid="PSA 18:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 18:9"/>And He stretched apart the heavens and came down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:9">and a dark cloud <char style="add">was</char> under His feet. <verse eid="PSA 18:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 18:10"/>And He rode upon a cherub and flew, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:10">and He took flight upon the wings of the wind. <verse eid="PSA 18:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 18:11"/>He made darkness His covering, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:11">His canopy around Him—darkness of waters <char style="add">and</char> thick clouds of vapors. <verse eid="PSA 18:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 18:12"/>From the brightness before Him </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:12">His thick clouds passed on, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:12">hail and coals of fire. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">bolts of lightning</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 13</char></note><verse eid="PSA 18:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 18:13"/>And YHWH thundered in the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:13">and the Most High gave forth His voice—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:13">hail and coals of fire.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Most Hebrew manuscripts; some Hebrew manuscripts and LXX do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">—hail and coals of fire</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see 2 Samuel 22:14.</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 18:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 18:14"/>And He sent out His arrows and scattered them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:14">and He hurled lightning and routed them. <verse eid="PSA 18:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 18:15"/>And the channels of the sea were seen. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:15">And the foundations of the world were uncovered, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 18:15">from Your rebuke, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:15">from the blast of the breath of Your nostril. <verse eid="PSA 18:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 18:16"/>He sent from above, he took hold of me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:16">He drew me out from the many waters. <verse eid="PSA 18:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 18:17"/>He snatched me away from my strong enemy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:17">and from those hating me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:17">for they were stronger than I. <verse eid="PSA 18:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 18:18"/>They confronted me in the day of my calamity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:18">and YHWH was as a support for me. <verse eid="PSA 18:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 18:19"/>And He brought me out into a broad place; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:19">He pulled me out, because He took delight in me. <verse eid="PSA 18:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 18:20"/>YHWH rewarded me according to my righteousness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:20">according to the cleanness of my hands, He returned <char style="add">it</char> to me. <verse eid="PSA 18:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 18:21"/>For I have kept the ways of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:21">and I have not acted wickedly against my God. <verse eid="PSA 18:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 18:22"/>For all His ordinances <char style="add">are</char> before me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:22">and I did not turn aside His statutes from me. <verse eid="PSA 18:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 18:23"/>And I was blameless before Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:23">and I guarded myself from my iniquity. <verse eid="PSA 18:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 18:24"/>And YHWH has returned to me according to my righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:24">according to the cleanness of my hands before His eyes. <verse eid="PSA 18:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 18:25"/>With the faithful one, You show Yourself faithful; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:25">with a blameless man, You show Yourself blameless; <verse eid="PSA 18:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 18:26"/>with the purified one, You show Yourself pure; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:26">and with the crooked one, You show Yourself shrewd. <verse eid="PSA 18:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 18:27"/>For You will save a lowly people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:27">but the eyes of those rising high You bring low. <verse eid="PSA 18:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 18:28"/>For You light my lamp; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:28">YHWH my God makes my darkness shine bright. <verse eid="PSA 18:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 18:29"/>For with You I can run <char style="add">against</char> a troop, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:29">and with my God I can leap a wall. <verse eid="PSA 18:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 18:30"/>God—His way <char style="add">is</char> perfect—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:30">the word of YHWH is refined; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:30">He <char style="add">is</char> a shield for all those taking refuge in Him. <verse eid="PSA 18:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 18:31"/>For who <char style="add">is</char> God, apart from YHWH? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:31">And who <char style="add">is</char> the Rock, except our God?— <verse eid="PSA 18:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 18:32"/>The God girding me with strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:32">and making perfect my way. <verse eid="PSA 18:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 18:33"/>Setting my feet like does, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:33">even on the heights He makes me stand. <verse eid="PSA 18:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 18:34"/>He trains my hands for the battle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:34">and my arms can bend down a bow of bronze. <verse eid="PSA 18:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 18:35"/>And You gave to me the shield of Your salvation; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:35">and Your right hand supports me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:35">and Your gentleness makes me great. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and Your help exalts me</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and You stoop down to make me great</char></note><verse eid="PSA 18:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 18:36"/>You made wide my path under me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:36">and my ankles have not slipped. <verse eid="PSA 18:36"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 18:37"/>I pursued my enemies and overtook them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:37">and I did not turn back until they were consumed. <verse eid="PSA 18:37"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 18:38"/>I wounded them, and they were not able to rise; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:38">they have fallen under my feet. <verse eid="PSA 18:38"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 18:39"/>And You girded me with strength for the battle; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:39">those rising against me You bent down underneath me. <verse eid="PSA 18:39"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 18:40"/>And my enemies, You have given to me the neck; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:40">and those hating me, I cut them off! <verse eid="PSA 18:40"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 18:41"/>They cried for help, and no one saved them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:41">upon YHWH, and He did not answer them. <verse eid="PSA 18:41"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 18:42"/>And I beat them as dust upon the face of the wind; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:42">like mud in the streets I trampled them.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.42 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Some Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, and Syriac (see also 2 Samuel 22:43); MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I poured emptied out</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 18:42"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 18:43"/>You rescued me from the disputes of people; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:43">You set me as the head of nations; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:43">a people I have not known shall serve me. <verse eid="PSA 18:43"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 18:44"/>At the hearing of the ear, they listen to me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:44">the sons of a foreigner feign obedience before me. <verse eid="PSA 18:44"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 18:45"/>The sons of a foreigner fade away, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:45">and they come trembling from their strongholds. <verse eid="PSA 18:45"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 18:46"/>YHWH lives! And blessed <char style="add">be</char> my Rock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:46">and the God of my salvation be exalted— <verse eid="PSA 18:46"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 18:47"/>the God giving vengeance to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:47">and subduing the peoples under me, <verse eid="PSA 18:47"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 18:48"/>causing me to escape from my enemies, even above, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 18:48">those who rise against me—You lift me up. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:48">From the man of violence, You have snatched me. <verse eid="PSA 18:48"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="PSA 18:49"/>Upon thus, I will confess You among the nations, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:49">and to Your name I will sing praise. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.49 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 15:9</char></note><verse eid="PSA 18:49"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="PSA 18:50"/>He is making great the salvation of His king </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:50">and showing loving devotion to His anointed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 18:50">of David and to his seed, even to forever. <verse eid="PSA 18:50"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 18"/>

<chapter number="19" style="c" sid="PSA 19"/>

<para style="s">The Heavens Declare the Glory of God</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 19:1"/> The heavens are recounting the glory of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:1">and the firmament is declaring the work of and His hands. <verse eid="PSA 19:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 19:2"/>Day after day it pours forth speech, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:2">and night after night it shows forth knowledge. <verse eid="PSA 19:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 19:3"/>Without speech and without words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:3">their voice not being heard,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">There is no speech or language where their voice is not heard</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 19:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 19:4"/>their voice has gone out into all the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:4">and their words to the end of the world.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">their line</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 19:4">He has placed a tent in them </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:4">for the sun, <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 10:18</char></note><verse eid="PSA 19:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 19:5"/>and it <char style="add">is</char> like a bridegroom going forth from his chamber, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:5">rejoicing like a strong man to run the path. <verse eid="PSA 19:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 19:6"/>From one end of the heavens <char style="add">is</char> his going forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:6">and his circuit <char style="add">is</char> upon their ends, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:6">and there is nothing being hidden from his heat. <verse eid="PSA 19:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 19:7"/>The law of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> perfect, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:7">refreshing the soul; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 19:7">the testimony of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> sure, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:7">making wise the simple. <verse eid="PSA 19:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 19:8"/>The statutes of YHWH <char style="add">are</char> straight, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:8">making glad the heart; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 19:8">the commandment of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> pure, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:8">bringing light to the eyes. <verse eid="PSA 19:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 19:9"/>The fear of YHWH is pure, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:9">standing forever; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 19:9">the judgments of YHWH <char style="add">are</char> true, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:9">being righteous altogether, <verse eid="PSA 19:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 19:10"/>being desired above gold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:10">and much above pure gold, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 19:10">and sweeter than honey </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:10">and flowing honey from the honeycomb. <verse eid="PSA 19:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 19:11"/>Indeed, Your servant is warned by them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:11">in keeping them <char style="add">is</char> great reward. <verse eid="PSA 19:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 19:12"/>Who can discern <char style="add">his</char> errors? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:12">From the hidden cleanse me. <verse eid="PSA 19:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 19:13"/>Also, hold back Your servant from proud <char style="add">things</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:13">may they not rule over me. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 19:13">Then I shall be complete, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:13">and cleansed of great transgression. <verse eid="PSA 19:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 19:14"/>The words of my mouth </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:14">and the meditation of my heart, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 19:14">let them be for favor before Your face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 19:14">O YHWH, my Rock and my Redeemer. <verse eid="PSA 19:14"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 19"/>

<chapter number="20" style="c" sid="PSA 20"/>

<para style="s">The Day of Trouble</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 20:1"/> May YHWH answer you in the day of distress; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 20:1">may the name of the God of Jacob set you on high. <verse eid="PSA 20:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 20:2"/>May He send help for you from the Holy Place, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 20:2">and from Zion may He support you. <verse eid="PSA 20:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 20:3"/>May He remember all your gifts, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 20:3">and anoint your burnt offering. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 20:3">Selah <verse eid="PSA 20:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 20:4"/>may He give to you according to your heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 20:4">and fulfill all your counsel. <verse eid="PSA 20:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 20:5"/>We will rejoice in your salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 20:5">and we will raise a banner in the name of our God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 20:5">may YHWH fulfill all your petitions. <verse eid="PSA 20:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 20:6"/>Now I know that YHWH brings salvation <char style="add">for</char> His anointed; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 20:6">He will answer him from His holy heaven, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 20:6">with the saving might of His right hand. <verse eid="PSA 20:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 20:7"/>These in the chariots, and these in the horses, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 20:7">but we, in the name of YHWH our God, will remember. <verse eid="PSA 20:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 20:8"/>They have bowed down and fallen, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 20:8">and we have risen and stand upright. <verse eid="PSA 20:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 20:9"/>O YHWH, save<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">give victory to</char></note> the king! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 20:9">Answer us on the day we call. <verse eid="PSA 20:9"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 20"/>

<chapter number="21" style="c" sid="PSA 21"/>

<para style="s">After the Battle</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 21:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Proverbs 21:1–31</char></note> O YHWH, in Your strength the king rejoices! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:1">And in Your salvation, how greatly he exults! <verse eid="PSA 21:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 21:2"/>The desire of his heart You have given to him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:2">and the request of his lips you have not withheld. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 21:2">Selah <verse eid="PSA 21:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 21:3"/>for You put before him the blessings of goodness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:3">You set upon his head a crown of pure gold. <verse eid="PSA 21:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 21:4"/>Life he has asked from You, <char style="add">and</char> You gave <char style="add">it</char> to him—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:4">length of days, forever and ever. <verse eid="PSA 21:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 21:5"/>Great <char style="add">is</char> his glory in Your salvation; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:5">splendor and majesty You have placed upon him. <verse eid="PSA 21:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 21:6"/>For You set <char style="add">for</char> him blessings forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:6">You make him rejoice with gladness before Your face. <verse eid="PSA 21:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 21:7"/>For the king trusts in YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:7">and in the loving devotion of the Most High </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:7">he shall not be shaken. <verse eid="PSA 21:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 21:8"/>Your hand will find all Your enemies; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:8">Your right hand will find those hating You. <verse eid="PSA 21:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 21:9"/>You will place them as <char style="add">in</char> a furnace of fire </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:9">at the time of Your presence; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 21:9">YHWH in His anger will swallow them up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:9">and the fire will devour them. <verse eid="PSA 21:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 21:10"/>Their fruit You will destroy from the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:10">and their seed from among the sons of men. <verse eid="PSA 21:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 21:11"/>For they stretched out against you <char style="add">for</char> evil. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:11">They devised a plot; they will not prevail. <verse eid="PSA 21:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 21:12"/>For You set them <char style="add">to the</char> shoulder; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:12">You prepare Your bowstrings against their faces. <verse eid="PSA 21:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 21:13"/>Be exalted, O YHWH, in Your strength; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 21:13">we will sing and praise Your might. <verse eid="PSA 21:13"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 21"/>

<chapter number="22" style="c" sid="PSA 22"/>

<para style="s">The Psalm of the Cross</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. According to “The Doe of the Dawn.” A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 22:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 19:16–30</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 23:26–43</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Mark 15:21–41</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 27:32–56</char></note> My God, my God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:1">why have You forsaken me,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Matthew 27:46 and Mark 15:34</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 22:1">far away from my salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:1"><char style="add">from</char> the words of my roaring? <verse eid="PSA 22:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 22:2"/>O my God, I cry out by day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:2">and You do not answer, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 22:2">and by night, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:2">and <char style="add">there is</char> no quiet for me. <verse eid="PSA 22:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 22:3"/>And You <char style="add">are</char> holy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:3">sitting <char style="add">amid</char> the praises of Israel. <verse eid="PSA 22:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 22:4"/>In You our fathers trusted; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:4">they trusted, and You delivered them. <verse eid="PSA 22:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 22:5"/>To You they cried, and they were given escape; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:5">in You they trusted, and they were not put to shame. <verse eid="PSA 22:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 22:6"/>And I <char style="add">am</char> a worm, and not a man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:6">the scorn of men, and despised by the people. <verse eid="PSA 22:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 22:7"/>All seeing me mock at me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:7">they gape with the lip; they shake the head: <verse eid="PSA 22:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 22:8"/>“Roll to YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:8">let Him deliver him </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 22:8"><char style="add">and</char> snatch him away, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:8">if indeed He delights in him.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He trusts in YHWH</char></note>” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Matthew 27:43</char></note><verse eid="PSA 22:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 22:9"/>Yet You brought me forth from the womb; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:9">You made me trust upon the breasts of my mother. <verse eid="PSA 22:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 22:10"/>Upon You I was cast forth from the womb; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:10">from the belly of my mother, You <char style="add">are</char> my God. <verse eid="PSA 22:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 22:11"/>You should not be far from me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:11">for distress <char style="add">is</char> near, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:11"><char style="add">and</char> because <char style="add">there is</char> no one to help. <verse eid="PSA 22:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 22:12"/>Many <char style="add">strong</char> bulls have surrounded me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:12">mighty ones of Bashan have encircled Me. <verse eid="PSA 22:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 22:13"/>They open against me their mouths, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:13">a lion tearing and roaring. <verse eid="PSA 22:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 22:14"/>I am poured out like water, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:14">and all of my bones are separated; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 22:14">my heart has become like wax, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:14"><char style="add">and</char> has melted in the midst of my bowels. <verse eid="PSA 22:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 22:15"/>My strength is dried up like a potsherd, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:15">and my tongue clings <char style="add">to</char> my jaws; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:15">and in the dust of death You lay me. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> MT; or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">My mouth</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, a possible reading of the original Hebrew text </char></note><verse eid="PSA 22:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 22:16"/>For dogs have surrounded me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:16">the swarm of the wicked has encircled me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:16">piercing my hands and my feet.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> DSS, LXX, Vulgate, and Syriac; most MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">like a lion at my hands and feet</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 22:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 22:17"/>I can count all my bones; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:17">they glare; they look at me. <verse eid="PSA 22:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 22:18"/>They divide out my garments for themselves, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:18">and over my clothing they cast lots. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in John 19:24; see also Matthew 27:35, Mark 15:24, and Luke 23:34</char></note><verse eid="PSA 22:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 22:19"/>But You, O YHWH, do not be far away! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:19">O my strength, may You hurry to help me. <verse eid="PSA 22:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 22:20"/>Snatch my soul from the sword, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:20">my only one from the hand of the dog! <verse eid="PSA 22:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 22:21"/>Save me from the mouth of the lion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:21">and from the horns of the wild oxen answer me. <verse eid="PSA 22:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 22:22"/>I will declare Your name to my brothers; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:22">in the midst of the assembly I will praise You. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I will sing Your praises in the assembly</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Hebrews 2:12.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 22:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 22:23"/>Those fearing YHWH, praise Him! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:23">All the seed of Jacob, honor Him! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:23">And fear Him, all the seed of Israel! <verse eid="PSA 22:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 22:24"/>For He has not despised </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:24">and has not detested the affliction of the afflicted, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 22:24">and He has not hidden His face from him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:24">and in his crying out to Him, He has heard. <verse eid="PSA 22:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 22:25"/>From You <char style="add">is</char> my praise in the great assembly; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:25">my vows I will complete in front of those who fear Him. <verse eid="PSA 22:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 22:26"/>The afflicted ones shall eat and be satisfied; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:26">those seeking Him shall praise YHWH. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:26">May your⁺ hearts live forever! <verse eid="PSA 22:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 22:27"/>They will remember and will turn to YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:27">all the ends of the earth; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 22:27">and before Your face they will bow down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:27">all the clans of the nations. <verse eid="PSA 22:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 22:28"/>For unto YHWH <char style="add">is</char> the kingship, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:28">and He rules over the nations. <verse eid="PSA 22:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 22:29"/>All the fat ones of the earth shall eat and bow low; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:29">before His face will bow all those going down <char style="add">to</char> the dust, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:29">even the one unable able to keep alive his soul. <verse eid="PSA 22:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 22:30"/>A seed shall serve Him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:30">it will be recounted of the Lord to the generation. <verse eid="PSA 22:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 22:31"/>They shall come and declare His righteousness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:31">to a people to be born, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 22:31">that which He has done! <verse eid="PSA 22:31"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 22"/>

<chapter number="23" style="c" sid="PSA 23"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Is My Shepherd</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 23:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 10:1–21</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Ezekiel 34:11–24</char></note> YHWH <char style="add">is</char> my shepherd;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Revelation 7:17.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 23:1">I shall not lack. <verse eid="PSA 23:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 23:2"/>In pastures green He makes me to lie down; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 23:2">beside waters of resting He guides me. <verse eid="PSA 23:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 23:3"/>He restores my soul; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 23:3">He guides me in the paths of righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 23:3">for the sake of His name. <verse eid="PSA 23:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 23:4"/>Even though I may walk in the valley of the shadow of death,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the valley of deep darkness</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 23:4">I will fear no evil, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 23:4">for You <char style="add">are</char> with me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 23:4">Your rod and Your staff, they comfort me. <verse eid="PSA 23:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 23:5"/>You arrange a table before me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 23:5">in front of my enemies; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 23:5">You anoint my head with the oil; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 23:5">my cup overflows. <verse eid="PSA 23:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 23:6"/>Surely goodness and mercy will pursue me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 23:6">all the days of my life, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 23:6">and I will dwell in the house of YHWH </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 23:6">for the length of days. <verse eid="PSA 23:6"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 23"/>

<chapter number="24" style="c" sid="PSA 24"/>

<para style="s">The Earth Is Yahweh’s</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 24:1"/> Unto YHWH <char style="add">is</char> the earth and its fullness,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in 1 Corinthians 10:26</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:1">the world and those dwelling in it. <verse eid="PSA 24:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 24:2"/>For He has founded it upon the seas, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:2">and upon the rivers He established it. <verse eid="PSA 24:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 24:3"/>Who will ascend onto the hill of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:3">or who will stand in His holy place? <verse eid="PSA 24:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 24:4"/>The one clean of hands and pure of heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:4">who has not lifted up his soul to vanity,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to falsehood</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to an idol</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:4">and has not sworn by deceit. <verse eid="PSA 24:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 24:5"/>He will lift up a blessing from YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:5">and righteousness from the God of his salvation. <verse eid="PSA 24:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 24:6"/>This <char style="add">is</char> the generation of those seeking Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:6">those seeking Your face, <char style="add">O God</char> of Jacob.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX, Syriac, and two Hebrew manuscripts; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">who seek your face, O Jacob</char></note> </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 24:6">Selah <verse eid="PSA 24:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 24:7"/>lift up, O gates, your⁺ heads, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:7">and be lifted up, O ancient doors, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:7">and the King of Glory shall come in! <verse eid="PSA 24:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 24:8"/>Who <char style="add">is</char> this King of Glory? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:8">YHWH strong and mighty, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:8">YHWH mighty <char style="add">in</char> battle! <verse eid="PSA 24:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 24:9"/>Lift up, O gates, your⁺ heads, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:9">and be lifted up, O ancient doors, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:9">and the King of glory shall come <char style="add">in</char>! <verse eid="PSA 24:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 24:10"/>Who is this King of glory? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:10">YHWH of Hosts, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 24:10">He <char style="add">is</char> the King of Glory! </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 24:10">Selah <verse eid="PSA 24:10"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 24"/>

<chapter number="25" style="c" sid="PSA 25"/>

<para style="s">To You I lift Up My Soul</para>

<para style="s">of David.†</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 25:1"/> Unto You, O YHWH, I lift up my soul. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">25.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> This psalm is an acrostic poem, each verse beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 25:1"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 25:2"/>My God, in You I trust. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 25:2">Do not let me be put to shame; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:2">do not let my enemies rejoice over me. <verse eid="PSA 25:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 25:3"/>Indeed, all those waiting on You will not be put to shame; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:3">those who act treacherously without cause will be ashamed. <verse eid="PSA 25:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 25:4"/>May You show me Your ways, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:4">may You teach me Your paths. <verse eid="PSA 25:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 25:5"/>Make me to walk in Your truth and teach me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:5">for You <char style="add">are</char> the God of my salvation; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:5">on You I wait all the day. <verse eid="PSA 25:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 25:6"/>Remember Your mercies, O YHWH, and Your loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:6">for they <char style="add">are</char> from of old. <verse eid="PSA 25:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 25:7"/>May You not remember the sins of my youth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:7">and my transgressions; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 25:7">according to Your loving devotion, may You remember me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:7">for the sake of Your goodness, O YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 25:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 25:8"/>Good and upright <char style="add">is</char> YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:8">upon thus, He directs sinful ones in the way. <verse eid="PSA 25:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 25:9"/>He guides the humble ones in justice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:9">and He teaches the humble ones His way. <verse eid="PSA 25:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 25:10"/>All the paths of YHWH <char style="add">are</char> loving devotion and truth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:10">to those keeping His covenant and His decrees. <verse eid="PSA 25:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 25:11"/>And for the sake of Your name, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:11">may You pardon my iniquity, though it <char style="add">is</char> great. <verse eid="PSA 25:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 25:12"/>Who <char style="add">is</char> this man, the one fearing YHWH? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:12">He will direct him in the way he must choose. <verse eid="PSA 25:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 25:13"/>His soul shall dwell in goodness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:13">and his seed shall possess the land. <verse eid="PSA 25:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 25:14"/>The counsel of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> with those fearing Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:14">and He makes known to them His covenant. <verse eid="PSA 25:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 25:15"/>My eyes <char style="add">are</char> continually toward YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:15">for He brings out my feet from a net. <verse eid="PSA 25:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 25:16"/>May You turn to me and show favor to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:16">for I <char style="add">am</char> lonely and afflicted. <verse eid="PSA 25:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 25:17"/>The troubles of my heart have enlarged; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:17">may You bring me out from my distress. <verse eid="PSA 25:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 25:18"/>Look on my affliction and my trouble, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:18">and lift all my sins. <verse eid="PSA 25:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 25:19"/>See my enemies!—For they are many, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:19">and with violent hatred they hate me. <verse eid="PSA 25:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 25:20"/>Guard my soul and deliver me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:20">let me not be put to shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:20">for I take refuge in You. <verse eid="PSA 25:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 25:21"/>May integrity and uprightness keep me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:21">for I wait for You.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">25.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for my hope is in You</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for I wait for You, O Lord</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 25:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 25:22"/>May You redeem Israel, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 25:22">from all his distress. <verse eid="PSA 25:22"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 25"/>

<chapter number="26" style="c" sid="PSA 26"/>

<para style="s">Vindicate Me, O LORD</para>

<para style="s">Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 26:1"/> Judge me, O YHWH! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 26:1">For I have walked in my integrity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 26:1">and I have trusted in YHWH without slipping. <verse eid="PSA 26:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 26:2"/>Examine me, O YHWH, and test me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 26:2">refine my kidneys and my heart. <verse eid="PSA 26:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 26:3"/>For Your loving devotion <char style="add">is</char> before my eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 26:3">and I have walked in Your truth. <verse eid="PSA 26:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 26:4"/>I do not sit with men of vanity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 26:4">and with dissemblers I will not go in. <verse eid="PSA 26:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 26:5"/>I hate the assembly of evildoers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 26:5">and with the wicked I do not sit. <verse eid="PSA 26:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 26:6"/>I wash my hands in innocence, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 26:6">and I go about Your altar, O YHWH, <verse eid="PSA 26:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 26:7"/>to sound with a voice of thanksgiving, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 26:7">and to recount all Your wonders. <verse eid="PSA 26:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 26:8"/>O YHWH, I love the habitation of Your house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 26:8">and the place of the dwelling of Your glory. <verse eid="PSA 26:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 26:9"/>Do not gather my soul with sinners, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 26:9">and my life with men of blood, <verse eid="PSA 26:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 26:10"/>in whose hands <char style="add">is</char> a scheme, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 26:10">and <char style="add">whose</char> right hand is filled <char style="add">with</char> a bribe. <verse eid="PSA 26:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 26:11"/>And I, in my integrity, walk; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 26:11">redeem me and be merciful to me. <verse eid="PSA 26:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 26:12"/>My foot stands on level ground; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 26:12">in the assemblies I will bless YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 26:12"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 26"/>

<chapter number="27" style="c" sid="PSA 27"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Is My Salvation</para>

<para style="s">Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 27:1"/> YHWH <char style="add">is</char> my light and my salvation—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:1">of whom shall I be afraid? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 27:1">YHWH <char style="add">is</char> the strength of my life—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:1">of whom shall I be in dread? <verse eid="PSA 27:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 27:2"/>In the coming near <char style="add">of</char> the wicked against me, for the eating of my flesh, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:2">my adversaries and my enemies to me, they stumble and fall. <verse eid="PSA 27:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 27:3"/>Though a host may encamp against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:3">my heart will not fear; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 27:3">though war should rise up against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:3">in this I will keep my trust. <verse eid="PSA 27:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 27:4"/>One <char style="add">thing</char> I have asked from YHWH—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:4">it do I seek—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 27:4">that I may dwell in the house of YHWH </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:4">all the days of my life, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 27:4">to look on the beauty of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:4">and to inquire in His temple. <verse eid="PSA 27:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 27:5"/>For He will hide me in His shelter </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:5">in the day of evil; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 27:5">He will conceal me under the cover of His tent; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:5">upon a rock He will set me high. <verse eid="PSA 27:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 27:6"/>And now my head will be held high </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:6">over my enemies all around me, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 27:6">and I will offer in His tent sacrifices of shouting; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:6">I will sing and make music to YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 27:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 27:7"/>Hear, O YHWH, my voice <char style="add">when</char> I call, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:7">and be merciful to me and answer me. <verse eid="PSA 27:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 27:8"/>You have said <char style="add">to</char> my heart “Seek My face.” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:8">Your face, O YHWH, I will seek. <verse eid="PSA 27:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 27:9"/>Do not hide Your face from me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:9">do not stretch Your servant away in anger! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 27:9">You have been my help—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:9">do not leave me and do not forsake me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:9">O God of my salvation. <verse eid="PSA 27:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 27:10"/>Though my father and my mother have forsaken me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:10">yet YHWH will gather me <char style="add">in</char>. <verse eid="PSA 27:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 27:11"/>Teach me Your way, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:11">and lead me on a level path, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:11">on account of my enemies. <verse eid="PSA 27:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 27:12"/>Do not give me up to the desires of my adversaries, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:12">for false witnesses have risen against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:12">and they breathe out violence. <verse eid="PSA 27:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 27:13"/>Still I believed to look </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:13">on the goodness of YHWH </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:13">in the land of the living. <verse eid="PSA 27:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 27:14"/>Wait for YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 27:14">be strong and let your heart be courageous. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 27:14">And wait for YHWH! <verse eid="PSA 27:14"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 27"/>

<chapter number="28" style="c" sid="PSA 28"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Is My Strength</para>

<para style="s">Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 28:1"/> To You, O YHWH, I call out. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:1">O my Rock, do not be deaf to me, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 28:1">lest You be silent to me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:1">and I be likened with those descending to the Pit. <verse eid="PSA 28:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 28:2"/>May You hear the voice of my supplications, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:2">in my crying out to You, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 28:2">in my lifting up my hands </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:2">toward Your holy sanctuary.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Your innermost sanctuary</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Your Most Holy Place</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 28:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 28:3"/>Do not drag me away with the wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:3">and with the workers of iniquity, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 28:3">those speaking peace with their neighbors, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:3">and evil <char style="add">is</char> in their heart. <verse eid="PSA 28:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 28:4"/>Give to them according to their doing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:4">and according to the evil of their deeds! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 28:4">According to the work of their hands, give to them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:4">return their dealing to them! <verse eid="PSA 28:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 28:5"/>For they do not have regard toward the works of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:5">and toward the deed of His hands; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 28:5">He shall overthrow them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:5">and not rebuild them. <verse eid="PSA 28:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 28:6"/>Blessed <char style="add">be</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:6">for He has heard the voice of my supplications. <verse eid="PSA 28:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 28:7"/>YHWH <char style="add">is</char> my strength and my shield; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:7">in Him my heart trusts, and I am helped; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 28:7">so my heart rejoices, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:7">and with my song I will give thanks to Him. <verse eid="PSA 28:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 28:8"/>YHWH <char style="add">is</char> the strength for them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:8">and He <char style="add">is</char> a stronghold of salvation <char style="add">for</char> His anointed. <verse eid="PSA 28:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 28:9"/>May You save Your people and bless Your inheritance, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 28:9">and shepherd them and carry them, even to forever. <verse eid="PSA 28:9"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 28"/>

<chapter number="29" style="c" sid="PSA 29"/>

<para style="s">Ascribe Glory to Yahweh</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 29:1"/> Ascribe to YHWH, O sons of the mighty ones.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">29.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">O sons of God</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">O heavenly beings</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 29:1">Ascribe to YHWH glory and strength. <verse eid="PSA 29:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 29:2"/>Ascribe to YHWH the glory of His name; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 29:2">bow down before YHWH in the splendor of holiness.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">29.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in holy attire</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 29:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 29:3"/>The voice of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> upon the waters; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 29:3">the God of glory thunders—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 29:3">YHWH <char style="add">is</char> over many waters. <verse eid="PSA 29:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 29:4"/>The voice of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> with power, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 29:4">the voice of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> with majesty. <verse eid="PSA 29:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 29:5"/>The voice of YHWH breaks the cedars, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 29:5">and YHWH shatters the cedars of Lebanon. <verse eid="PSA 29:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 29:6"/>He makes Lebanon skip like a calf, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 29:6">and Sirion<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">29.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Mount Hermon</char></note> like the son of a wild ox. <verse eid="PSA 29:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 29:7"/>The voice of YHWH is hewing </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 29:7">flames of fire. <verse eid="PSA 29:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 29:8"/>The voice of YHWH causes the wilderness to writhe; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 29:8">YHWH causes the wilderness of Kadesh to writhe. <verse eid="PSA 29:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 29:9"/>The voice of YHWH twists the oaks,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">29.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">makes the deer to calve</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 29:9">and strips bare the forests—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 29:9">and in His temple all of it is saying, “Glory!” <verse eid="PSA 29:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 29:10"/>YHWH has sat over the flood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 29:10">and YHWH sits as King forever. <verse eid="PSA 29:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 29:11"/>YHWH gives strength to His people; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 29:11">YHWH blesses His people with peace. <verse eid="PSA 29:11"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 29"/>

<chapter number="30" style="c" sid="PSA 30"/>

<para style="s">You Turned My Mourning into Dancing</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm. A song for the dedication of the house of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 30:1"/> I will exalt You, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:1">for You have drawn me up, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 30:1">and You did not let my enemies </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:1">rejoice over me. <verse eid="PSA 30:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 30:2"/>O YHWH my God, I cried for help to You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:2">and You healed me. <verse eid="PSA 30:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 30:3"/>O YHWH, You have brought up my soul from Sheol; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:3">from my going down <char style="add">to</char> the Pit, You have kept me alive. <verse eid="PSA 30:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 30:4"/>Make music to YHWH, His faithful ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:4">and praise His holy name.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and praise the memorial of His holiness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Exodus 3:15.</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 30:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 30:5"/>For a moment <char style="add">is</char> His anger; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:5">for a lifetime <char style="add">is</char> His favor. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 30:5">In the night lodges weeping, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:5">and in the morning, joy. <verse eid="PSA 30:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 30:6"/>And I said in my prosperity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:6">“I will not be shaken forever.” <verse eid="PSA 30:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 30:7"/>O YHWH, by Your favor </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:7">You made my mountain stand strong; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 30:7">You have hidden Your face—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:7">I was dismayed. <verse eid="PSA 30:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 30:8"/>To You, O YHWH, I called out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:8">and to my Lord I made supplication. <verse eid="PSA 30:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 30:9"/>“What profit <char style="add">is</char> in my blood,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in my destruction</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:9">in my going down to the Pit?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">30.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to corruption</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 30:9">Will the dust confess You? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:9">Will it declare Your truth? <verse eid="PSA 30:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 30:10"/>Hear, O YHWH, and have mercy on me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:10">O YHWH, be the One giving help to me.” <verse eid="PSA 30:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 30:11"/>You have turned my mourning to dancing for me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:11">You have opened my sackcloth and clothed me with gladness, <verse eid="PSA 30:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 30:12"/>so that <char style="add">my</char> glory will sing praise to you, and not be silent. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 30:12">O YHWH, my God, I will give thanks to You forever. <verse eid="PSA 30:12"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 30"/>

<chapter number="31" style="c" sid="PSA 31"/>

<para style="s">Into Your Hands I Commit My Spirit</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 31:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 23:44–49</char></note> In You, O YHWH, I have taken refuge; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:1">do not let me be ashamed forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:1">in Your righteousness, deliver me! <verse eid="PSA 31:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 31:2"/>Incline Your ear to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:2">and quickly deliver me. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 31:2">Be for me as a rock of refuge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:2">as a house of strongholds to save me. <verse eid="PSA 31:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 31:3"/>For You <char style="add">are</char> my rock and my stronghold; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:3">and for the sake of Your name, You will lead me and guide me. <verse eid="PSA 31:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 31:4"/>You will bring me out from the net that they have hidden for me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:4">because You <char style="add">are</char> my refuge. <verse eid="PSA 31:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 31:5"/>Into Your hand I commit my spirit; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:5">You have redeemed me, O YHWH, God of truth. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">31.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Luke 23:46</char></note><verse eid="PSA 31:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 31:6"/>I have hated<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">31.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> MT; one Hebrew manuscript, LXX, and Syriac </char><char style="fq" closed="false">You hate</char></note> those serving worthless idols; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:6">and I toward YHWH place my trust. <verse eid="PSA 31:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 31:7"/>I will rejoice and be glad in Your loving devotion—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:7">in that You have seen my affliction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:7"><char style="add">and</char> you knew of the distress of my soul. <verse eid="PSA 31:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 31:8"/>And You did not shut me up in the hand of the enemy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:8">You set my feet on a broad place. <verse eid="PSA 31:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 31:9"/>Show favor to me, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:9">for there is distress for me! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 31:9">My eye, my soul, and my belly </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:9">have wasted away with grief. <verse eid="PSA 31:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 31:10"/>For my life has been consumed with grief, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:10">and my years with groaning; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 31:10">my strength fails in my iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:10">and my bones are wasting away. <verse eid="PSA 31:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 31:11"/>Among all my enemies I am an object of scorn, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:11">even to my neighbors, and a source of dread, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 31:11">exceedingly to those who know me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:11">those seeing me in the street flee from me! <verse eid="PSA 31:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 31:12"/>I have been forgotten like a dead man from the heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:12">I am perishing like a vessel. <verse eid="PSA 31:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 31:13"/>For I have heard the slander of many, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:13">terror from round about, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 31:13">in their taking counsel together against me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:13">they have plotted to take my life. <verse eid="PSA 31:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 31:14"/>Yet I have trusted in You, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:14">I say, “You <char style="add">are</char> My God.” <verse eid="PSA 31:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 31:15"/>In Your hand <char style="add">are</char> my times; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:15">deliver me from the hand of my enemies, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:15">and from those pursuing me. <verse eid="PSA 31:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 31:16"/>Cause Your face to shine upon Your servant; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:16">save me in Your loving devotion. <verse eid="PSA 31:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 31:17"/>O YHWH, do not let me be ashamed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:17">for I have called to You. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 31:17">Let the wicked be ashamed; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:17">let them be silent in Sheol. <verse eid="PSA 31:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 31:18"/>Let the lips of falsehood become dumb, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:18">those speaking against the righteous <char style="add">with</char> arrogance, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:18">with pride and contempt. <verse eid="PSA 31:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 31:19"/>How great <char style="add">is</char> Your goodness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:19">which You have laid up for those fearing You, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 31:19"><char style="add">which</char> you have prepared for those taking refuge in You </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:19">before the sons of man! <verse eid="PSA 31:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 31:20"/>You shall hide them in the hidden place of Your presence, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:20">from the plots of man; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 31:20">you shall store them in a shelter, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:20">from the strife of tongues. <verse eid="PSA 31:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 31:21"/>Blessed <char style="add">be</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:21">for He has made marvelous His loving devotion to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:21">in a city <char style="add">under</char> siege. <verse eid="PSA 31:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 31:22"/>For I said in my haste, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:22">“I am cut off from before Your eyes!” </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 31:22">Surely You heard the voice of my supplications, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:22">in my crying out to You. <verse eid="PSA 31:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 31:23"/>Love YHWH, all you His holy ones! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:23">YHWH is watching the faithful </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:23">and recompensing the worker of pride in excess. <verse eid="PSA 31:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 31:24"/>Hold firm, and He shall strengthen your⁺ heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 31:24">all those waiting for YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 31:24"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 31"/>

<chapter number="32" style="c" sid="PSA 32"/>

<para style="s">The Joy of Forgiveness</para>

<para style="s">Of David. A Maskil.†</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 32:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Romans 4:1–12</char></note> Blessed <char style="add">is he</char> with transgression lifted, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:1">with sin is covered.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">32.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Maskil</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">32.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Blessed is he whose lawless acts are forgiven, whose sins are covered</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Romans 4:7</char></note><verse eid="PSA 32:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 32:2"/>Blessed <char style="add">is</char> the man </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:2">for whom YHWH does not reckon iniquity,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">32.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Blessed is the man whose sin the LORD does not count against him</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Romans 4:8</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:2">and in his spirit <char style="add">is</char> no deceit. <verse eid="PSA 32:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 32:3"/>When I remained silent, my bones were worn out </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:3">by my groaning all the day. <verse eid="PSA 32:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 32:4"/>For day and night </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:4">Your hand was heavy upon me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 32:4">my juice was overturned,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">32.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">my vitality was turned</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">my strength was drained</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:4"><char style="add">as</char> in the drought of summer. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 32:4">Selah <verse eid="PSA 32:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 32:5"/>I made known to You my sin, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:5">and my iniquity I did not hide; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 32:5">I said, “I will make confession over my transgressions to YHWH,” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:5">and You forgave the guilt of my sin. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 32:5">Selah <verse eid="PSA 32:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 32:6"/>upon thus, let every godly one pray to You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:6">in a time to find; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 32:6">even with a flood of great waters toward him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:6">they shall not touch him. <verse eid="PSA 32:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 32:7"/>You <char style="add">are</char> a hiding <char style="add">place</char> unto me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:7">from distress you keep me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:7">with shouts of deliverance, You will surround me. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 32:7">Selah <verse eid="PSA 32:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 32:8"/>I will instruct you and direct you in the way that you should go; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:8"><char style="add">with</char> My eye I will give counsel concerning you. <verse eid="PSA 32:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 32:9"/>You⁺ should not be like a horse, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:9">like a mule without understanding, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 32:9">with bit and bridle to curb its ornaments, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:9"><char style="add">that</char> there is no coming near to you. <verse eid="PSA 32:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 32:10"/>Many <char style="add">are</char> the pains of the wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:10">and the one trusting in YHWH, loving devotion shall surround him. <verse eid="PSA 32:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 32:11"/>Be glad in YHWH and rejoice, O righteous ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 32:11">and shout for joy, all upright of heart! <verse eid="PSA 32:11"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 32"/>

<chapter number="33" style="c" sid="PSA 33"/>

<para style="s">Praise to the Creator</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 33:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 148:1–14</char></note>Give a ringing cry, O righteous ones, in YHWH! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:1">Beautiful <char style="add">is</char> the praise for the upright. <verse eid="PSA 33:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 33:2"/>Give thanks to YHWH with the harp; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:2">with an instrument of ten <char style="add">strings</char>, make music to Him. <verse eid="PSA 33:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 33:3"/>Sing to Him a new song; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:3">play skillfully with a shout of joy. <verse eid="PSA 33:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 33:4"/>For straight <char style="add">is</char> the word of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:4">and all His work is trustworthy. <verse eid="PSA 33:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 33:5"/>He loves righteousness and justice; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:5">the earth is full of the loving devotion of YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 33:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 33:6"/>By the word of YHWH the heavens were made, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:6">and by the breath of His mouth all their host. <verse eid="PSA 33:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 33:7"/>He gathers together the waters of the sea as a heap; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:7">He lays up the depths in storehouses. <verse eid="PSA 33:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 33:8"/>Let them be afraid of YHWH, all the earth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:8">let all those dwelling in the world stand in awe of Him! <verse eid="PSA 33:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 33:9"/>For He has spoken, and it came to pass; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:9">He has commanded, and it stood firm. <verse eid="PSA 33:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 33:10"/>YHWH breaks apart the counsel of nations; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:10">He has diasllowed the plans of the peoples. <verse eid="PSA 33:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 33:11"/>The counsel of YHWH stands forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:11">the plans of His heart from generation and <char style="add">to</char> generation. <verse eid="PSA 33:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 33:12"/>Blessed <char style="add">is</char> the nation for whom YHWH <char style="add">is</char> its God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:12">the people He has chosen as the inheritance for Him. <verse eid="PSA 33:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 33:13"/>From the heavens, YHWH looks; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:13">He sees all the sons of man. <verse eid="PSA 33:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 33:14"/>From the fixed place of His sitting, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:14">He gazes toward all those dwelling <char style="add">on</char> the earth. <verse eid="PSA 33:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 33:15"/>He fashions their hearts together; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:15">He attends to all their works. <verse eid="PSA 33:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 33:16"/>No king is saved by the abundance of <char style="add">his</char> strength; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:16">a mighty man is not delivered by the abundance of <char style="add">his</char> power. <verse eid="PSA 33:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 33:17"/><char style="add">His</char> horse <char style="add">is</char> a false <char style="add">thing</char> for salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:17">and in the abundance of its strength it cannot provide escape. <verse eid="PSA 33:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 33:18"/>Behold, the eye of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> toward those who fear Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:18">to those waiting on His loving devotion, <verse eid="PSA 33:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 33:19"/>to snatch their soul from death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:19">and to keep them alive in famine. <verse eid="PSA 33:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 33:20"/>Our soul waits for YHWH—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:20">He <char style="add">is</char> our help and our shield. <verse eid="PSA 33:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 33:21"/>For in Him our heart shall rejoice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:21">because we have trusted in His holy Name. <verse eid="PSA 33:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 33:22"/>May Your loving devotion, O YHWH, be upon us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 33:22">as we do wait for You. <verse eid="PSA 33:22"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 33"/>

<chapter number="34" style="c" sid="PSA 34"/>

<para style="s">Taste and See That Yahweh Is Good</para>

<para style="s">Of David, in his changing his behavior before Abimelech,† and he drove him off, and he went.†</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 34:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Samuel 21:8–15</char></note> I will bless YHWH at every time; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:1">His praise <char style="add">is</char> continually in my mouth. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">34.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Abimelech</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is another name for </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Achish</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see 1 Samuel 21–29 and 1 Kings 2:39.</char></note><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">34.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> This psalm is an acrostic poem, each verse beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 34:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 34:2"/>In YHWH my soul boasts; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:2">let the humble hear and be glad. <verse eid="PSA 34:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 34:3"/>Magnify YHWH with me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:3">and let us exalt His name together. <verse eid="PSA 34:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 34:4"/>I sought YHWH, and He answered me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:4">and He snatched me up from all my fears. <verse eid="PSA 34:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 34:5"/>They looked toward Him, and they shone, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:5">and their faces were not ashamed. <verse eid="PSA 34:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 34:6"/>This poor one called out, and YHWH heard, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:6">and from all his troubles He saved him. <verse eid="PSA 34:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 34:7"/>The angel of YHWH encamps all around those who fear Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:7">and he rescues them. <verse eid="PSA 34:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 34:8"/>Taste and see that YHWH <char style="add">is</char> good; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:8">blessed <char style="add">is</char> the man <char style="add">who</char> takes refuge in Him. <verse eid="PSA 34:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 34:9"/>Fear YHWH, His holy ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:9">for There is no lack for those fearing Him. <verse eid="PSA 34:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 34:10"/>The young lions are in want and are hungry, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:10">and those seeking YHWH shall not lack any good <char style="add">thing</char>. <verse eid="PSA 34:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 34:11"/>Come, <char style="add">my</char> sons, listen to me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:11">the fear of YHWH I will teach you⁺. <verse eid="PSA 34:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 34:12"/>Who <char style="add">is</char> the man desiring life, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:12">loving days, that he may see good? <verse eid="PSA 34:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 34:13"/>Keep your tongue from evil </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:13">and your lips from speaking deceit. <verse eid="PSA 34:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 34:14"/>Turn away from evil and do good; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:14">seek peace and pursue it. <verse eid="PSA 34:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 34:15"/>The eyes of YHWH <char style="add">are</char> toward the righteous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:15">and His ears are inclined to their cry. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">34.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to their prayer</char></note><verse eid="PSA 34:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 34:16"/>The face of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> against those doing evil,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">34.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in 1 Peter 3:10–12</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:16">to cut off from the earth their memory. <verse eid="PSA 34:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 34:17"/>They cry out, and YHWH hears, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:17">and He delivers them from all their troubles. <verse eid="PSA 34:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 34:18"/>Near <char style="add">is</char> YHWH to the broken of heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:18">and He saves those crushed in spirit. <verse eid="PSA 34:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 34:19"/>Many <char style="add">are</char> <char style="add">are</char> the afflictions of a righteous one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:19">but from them all YHWH delivers him. <verse eid="PSA 34:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 34:20"/>He guards all his bones; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:20">not one of them is broken. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">34.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in John 19:36</char></note><verse eid="PSA 34:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 34:21"/>Evil will kill the wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:21">and those hating a righteous one will be held guilty. <verse eid="PSA 34:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 34:22"/>YHWH redeems the soul of His servants, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 34:22">and not any of those taking refuge in Him will be condemned. <verse eid="PSA 34:22"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 34"/>

<chapter number="35" style="c" sid="PSA 35"/>

<para style="s">Contend with My Opponents, O LORD</para>

<para style="s">Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 35:1"/> Contend, O YHWH, with my opponents; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:1">fight with those fighting me! <verse eid="PSA 35:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 35:2"/>Take hold of shield and buckler, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:2">and rise in help of me, <verse eid="PSA 35:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 35:3"/>and draw out the spear and javelin<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">35.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and close the way</char></note> against those pursuing me! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:3">Say to my soul, “I <char style="add">am</char> your salvation.” <verse eid="PSA 35:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 35:4"/>Let them be shamed and dishonored, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:4">those seeking my soul; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 35:4">let them be turned back and confounded, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:4">those planning evil for me! <verse eid="PSA 35:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 35:5"/>Let them be like chaff before the wind, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:5">and the angel of YHWH driving <char style="add">them</char> away. <verse eid="PSA 35:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 35:6"/>Let their path be darkness and slickness—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:6">and let the angel of YHWH pursue them! <verse eid="PSA 35:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 35:7"/>For without cause, they have hidden a pit for me—their net; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:7">they have dug one for my soul without cause. <verse eid="PSA 35:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 35:8"/>Let destruction come upon him <char style="add">that</char> he shall not know, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:8">and the net that he has hidden, let it catch him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:8">the destruction, let him fall into it! <verse eid="PSA 35:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 35:9"/>And my soul will rejoice in YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:9">it will exult in His salvation. <verse eid="PSA 35:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 35:10"/>All my bones will say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:10">“O YHWH, who <char style="add">is</char> like You?—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 35:10">Snatching the afflicted from the one stronger than he, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:10">and the afflicted one and the needy one from the one plundering him.” <verse eid="PSA 35:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 35:11"/>Violent witnesses rise up; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:11">those whom I do not know; they interrogate me. <verse eid="PSA 35:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 35:12"/>They repay me evil in place of good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:12"><char style="add">to</char> the bereavement of my soul. <verse eid="PSA 35:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 35:13"/>And I—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:13">in their sickness my clothing <char style="add">is</char> sackcloth; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 35:13">I humbled my soul with fasting, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:13">and my prayer returned upon my bosom. <verse eid="PSA 35:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 35:14"/>As for a friend </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:14">or brother to me—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 35:14">I went about as one mourning; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:14">in grief as for my mother, I bowed down. <verse eid="PSA 35:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 35:15"/>And in my stumbling, they were glad and gathered themselves together; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:15">attackers they gathered together against me, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 35:15">and ones I did not know, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:15">they tore and did not cease., <verse eid="PSA 35:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 35:16"/>Like godless mockers at a feast,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">35.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Like a godless circle of mockers,</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:16">they gnashed at me with their teeth. <verse eid="PSA 35:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 35:17"/>O Lord, how long will you look on? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:17">Turn back my soul from their ravages, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:17">my only one from the young lions! <verse eid="PSA 35:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 35:18"/>I will give You thanks in the great assembly; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:18">among a mighty people I will praise You. <verse eid="PSA 35:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 35:19"/>Do not let my enemies rejoice over me <char style="add">in</char> deception; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:19">those hating me for no reason wink the eye. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">35.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See John 15:25.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 35:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 35:20"/>For they do not speak peace, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:20">and against the quiet of the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:20">they devise words of deceit. <verse eid="PSA 35:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 35:21"/>And they opened wide against me their mouths; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:21">they said, “Aha, aha! Our eyes have seen <char style="add">it</char>!” <verse eid="PSA 35:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 35:22"/>You have seen it, O YHWH; do not be silent! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:22">O Lord, do not be far from me! <verse eid="PSA 35:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 35:23"/>Rouse Yourself, and awaken to my judgment, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:23">my God and my Lord, to my cause! <verse eid="PSA 35:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 35:24"/>Judge for me according to Your righteousness, O YHWH my God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:24">and do not let them rejoice over me. <verse eid="PSA 35:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 35:25"/>Do not let them say in their heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:25">“Aha, our desire!” </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 35:25">Do not let them say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:25">“We have swallowed him up!” <verse eid="PSA 35:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 35:26"/>Let them be put to shame and brought to confusion </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:26">together, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:26">those being glad at my distress; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 35:26">may they be clothed with shame and dishonor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:26">those magnifying themselves over me! <verse eid="PSA 35:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 35:27"/>Let them shout for joy and be glad, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:27">those desiring my vindication, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 35:27">and let them say continually, “Let YHWH be magnified, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:27">the One delighting in the welfare of His servant!” <verse eid="PSA 35:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 35:28"/>And my tongue shall utter Your righteousness—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 35:28">Your praise all the day. <verse eid="PSA 35:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 35"/>

<chapter number="36" style="c" sid="PSA 36"/>

<para style="s">The Transgression of the Wicked</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. Of the servant of YHWH, of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 36:1"/> Of the transgression of the wicked </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:1"><char style="add">is</char> within my heart; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 36:1">there is no dread of God </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:1">before his eyes.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">36.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 3:18</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 36:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 36:2"/>For he is flattering to himself in his own eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:2">having found his iniquity to be hated. <verse eid="PSA 36:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 36:3"/>The words of his mouth <char style="add">are</char> wickedness and deceit; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:3">he has ceased to be prudent and do good. <verse eid="PSA 36:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 36:4"/>He devises iniquity upon his bed; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:4">he stands himself on a path <char style="add">that is</char> not good; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:4">he does not reject evil. <verse eid="PSA 36:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 36:5"/>O YHWH, Your loving devotion <char style="add">is</char> into the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:5">Your faithfulness as far as the clouds. <verse eid="PSA 36:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 36:6"/>Your righteousness <char style="add">is</char> like the mountains of Might, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:6">Your ordinances the great deep; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:6">You keep safe man and beast, O YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 36:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 36:7"/>How precious <char style="add">is</char> Your loving devotion, O God! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:7">Even the sons of man take refuge </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:7">under the shadow of Your wings. <verse eid="PSA 36:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 36:8"/>They are filled from the fatness of Your house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:8">and You let them drink <char style="add">from</char> the stream of Your delights. <verse eid="PSA 36:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 36:9"/>For with You <char style="add">is</char> the fountain of life; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:9">in Your light we see light. <verse eid="PSA 36:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 36:10"/>Draw out Your loving devotion to those knowing You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:10">and Your righteousness to the upright of heart. <verse eid="PSA 36:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 36:11"/>Do not let the foot of pride come against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:11">and the hand of the wicked, do not let it drive me away. <verse eid="PSA 36:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 36:12"/>There the workers of iniquity do fall! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 36:12">They have been cast down, and are not able to rise. <verse eid="PSA 36:12"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 36"/>

<chapter number="37" style="c" sid="PSA 37"/>

<para style="s">Delight Yourself in Yahweh</para>

<para style="s">Of David.†</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 37:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Kings 2:1–9</char></note> You should not fret ove those doing evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:1">and do not be jealous of the workers of iniquity. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">37.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> This psalm is an acrostic poem, each stanza beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 37:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 37:2"/>For like the grass, soon they are cut off, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:2">and like the green of the herb they shall wither. <verse eid="PSA 37:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 37:3"/>Trust in YHWH and do good; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:3">dwell in the land and graze in faithfulness. <verse eid="PSA 37:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 37:4"/>And delight yourself in YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:4">and He will give to you the desires of your heart. <verse eid="PSA 37:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 37:5"/>Roll upon YHWH your way; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:5">trust in Him, and He will act. <verse eid="PSA 37:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 37:6"/>And He will bring forth your righteousness like the dawn, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:6">and your justice like the noonday sun. <verse eid="PSA 37:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 37:7"/>Be still before YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:7">and wait patiently for Him; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 37:7">do not fret over the one succeeding in his path, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:7">over the man making schemes. <verse eid="PSA 37:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 37:8"/>Cease from anger, and leave <char style="add">behind</char> wrath; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:8">you should not burn—<char style="add">it</char> only causes harm. <verse eid="PSA 37:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 37:9"/>For those doing evil will be cut off, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:9">and those waiting on YHWH, they will inherit the land. <verse eid="PSA 37:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 37:10"/>And in yet a little while, the wicked man <char style="add">is</char> no more; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:10">and you will look for his place, and it <char style="add">is</char> no more. <verse eid="PSA 37:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 37:11"/>And the meek will inherit the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:11">and they will delight in the abundance of peace. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">37.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the earth</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Matthew 5:5.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 37:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 37:12"/>The wicked man is plotting against the righteous one </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:12">and is gnashing his teeth at him. <verse eid="PSA 37:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 37:13"/>The Lord laughs at him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:13">for He sees that his day is coming. <verse eid="PSA 37:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 37:14"/>The wicked have drawn out the sword </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:14">and have bent their bows, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 37:14">to cast down the poor and needy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:14"><char style="add">and</char> to slay those upright in the path. <verse eid="PSA 37:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 37:15"/>Their sword will come <char style="add">into</char> their own heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:15">and their bows will be broken. <verse eid="PSA 37:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 37:16"/>Better <char style="add">is</char> the little of the righteous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:16">than the riches of many wicked. <verse eid="PSA 37:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 37:17"/>For the arms of the wicked will be broken, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:17">and YHWH upholds the righteous. <verse eid="PSA 37:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 37:18"/>YHWH Knows the days of the blameless, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:18">and their inheritance will be forever. <verse eid="PSA 37:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 37:19"/>They will not be ashamed in a time of evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:19">and in days of famine they will be satisfied. <verse eid="PSA 37:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 37:20"/>But the wicked will perish, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:20">and the enemies of YHWH; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 37:20">like the splendor of the meadows they will be consumed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:20"><char style="add">and</char> with the smoke they will be consumed. <verse eid="PSA 37:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 37:21"/>The wicked borrows and does not repay, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:21">and the righteous one is gracious and giving. <verse eid="PSA 37:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 37:22"/>For those being blessed by Him will inherit the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:22">and those being cursed by Him will be cut off. <verse eid="PSA 37:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 37:23"/>By YHWH the steps of a man are established, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:23">and in his way He delights. <verse eid="PSA 37:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 37:24"/>Though he falls, he will not be cast down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:24">for YHWH is upholding his hand.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">37.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">is upholding him with His hand</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 37:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 37:25"/>I have been young, and I am old; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:25">and I have not seen the righteous forsaken, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:25">and his seed seeking bread. <verse eid="PSA 37:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 37:26"/>All the day, he is gracious and lending, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:26">and his seed are a blessing. <verse eid="PSA 37:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 37:27"/>Turn away from evil and do good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:27">and you will dwell forever. <verse eid="PSA 37:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 37:28"/>For YHWH loves justice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:28">and He will not forsake His holy ones; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 37:28">forever they are preserved, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:28">and the seed of the wicked will be cut off. <verse eid="PSA 37:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 37:29"/>The righteous will inherit the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:29">and they will dwell forever in it. <verse eid="PSA 37:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 37:30"/>The mouth of the righteous utters wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:30">and his tongue speaks justice. <verse eid="PSA 37:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 37:31"/>The law of his God <char style="add">is</char> in his heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:31">his steps do not slip. <verse eid="PSA 37:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 37:32"/>The wicked is keeping watch on the righteous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:32">and he is seeking to kill him. <verse eid="PSA 37:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 37:33"/>YHWH will not leave him in his hand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:33">and will not declare him wicked in his being judged. <verse eid="PSA 37:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 37:34"/>Wait on YHWH and keep His way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:34">and He will exalt you <char style="add">so as</char> to possess the land; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 37:34">in the cutting off <char style="add">of</char> the wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:34">you will see <char style="add">it</char>. <verse eid="PSA 37:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 37:35"/>I have seen a wicked, ruthless one </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:35">spread out like a luxuriant native tree. <verse eid="PSA 37:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 37:36"/>And he passed away, and behold, he was no more; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:36">and indeed I sought him, and he could not be found. <verse eid="PSA 37:36"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 37:37"/>Observe a blameless one, and see an upright one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:37">for the end of the man <char style="add">is</char> well-being.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">37.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for there is a future for the man of peace</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 37:37"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 37:38"/>But those transgressing will be destroyed together; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:38">the end for the wicked man is cut off. <verse eid="PSA 37:38"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 37:39"/>And the salvation of the righteous <char style="add">is</char> from YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:39">He <char style="add">is</char> their stronghold in time of distress. <verse eid="PSA 37:39"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 37:40"/>And YHWH helps them and rescues them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:40">He shall rescue them from the wicked and save them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 37:40">because they have taken refuge in Him. <verse eid="PSA 37:40"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 37"/>

<chapter number="38" style="c" sid="PSA 38"/>

<para style="s">Do Not Rebuke Me in Your Anger</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of David, for remembrance.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 38:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 6:1–10</char></note> O YHWH, do not rebuke me in Your wrath </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:1">and chastise me in Your fury. <verse eid="PSA 38:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 38:2"/>For Your arrows descend into me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:2">and Your hand comes down on me. <verse eid="PSA 38:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 38:3"/>No soundness <char style="add">is</char> in my flesh </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:3">before the face of Your anger; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 38:3">no peace <char style="add">is</char> in my bones </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:3">before the face of my sin. <verse eid="PSA 38:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 38:4"/>For my iniquities have passed over my head; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:4">like a heavy burden, they are heavy for me. <verse eid="PSA 38:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 38:5"/>My wounds are foul and festering, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:5">before the face of my foolishness. <verse eid="PSA 38:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 38:6"/>I am bent, I am bowed down even to excess; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:6">all the day I go about mourning. <verse eid="PSA 38:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 38:7"/>For my loins are full of burning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:7">and there is no soundness in my flesh. <verse eid="PSA 38:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 38:8"/>I am numb and crushed, even to excess; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:8">I roar from the groaning of my heart. <verse eid="PSA 38:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 38:9"/>O Lord, all my desire <char style="add">is</char> before You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:9">and my groaning is not hidden from You. <verse eid="PSA 38:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 38:10"/>My heart pounds, my strength has forsaken me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:10">and the light of my eyes—even they <char style="add">are</char> not with me. <verse eid="PSA 38:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 38:11"/>My beloved and my friends stand away from my plague; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:11">my neighbors stand far off. <verse eid="PSA 38:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 38:12"/>And those seeking my soul lay snares, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:12">and those searching out my harm speak; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:12">they ponder destruction and treachery all the day. <verse eid="PSA 38:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 38:13"/>And I <char style="add">am</char> like a deaf one <char style="add">who</char> does not hear </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:13">and like a mute one <char style="add">who</char> does not open his mouth. <verse eid="PSA 38:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 38:14"/>And I am like a man who is not hearing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:14">and in his mouth <char style="add">are</char> no rebukes, <verse eid="PSA 38:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 38:15"/>because for You, O YHWH, I have waited; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:15">You will answer, O Lord my God. <verse eid="PSA 38:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 38:16"/>For I said, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:16">“Lest they rejoice over me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 38:16">in the slipping of my foot </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:16">they magnify themselves against me.” <verse eid="PSA 38:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 38:17"/>For I am ready to fall, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:17">and my sorrow <char style="add">is</char> before me continually. <verse eid="PSA 38:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 38:18"/>For I declare my iniquity; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:18">I am anxious over my sin. <verse eid="PSA 38:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 38:19"/>And my enemies without cause are many, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:19">and those hating me without cause have been multiplied.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> One DSS manuscript; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">My enemies are vigorous and many</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">38.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See John 15:25</char></note><verse eid="PSA 38:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 38:20"/>And those repaying evil for good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:20">they oppose me, because of my pursuing good. <verse eid="PSA 38:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 38:21"/>Do not forsake me, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:21">O my God, do not be far from me! <verse eid="PSA 38:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 38:22"/>Hurry to help me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 38:22">O Lord, my salvation. <verse eid="PSA 38:22"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 38"/>

<chapter number="39" style="c" sid="PSA 39"/>

<para style="s">I Will Watch My Ways</para>

<para style="s">To the one directing. For Jeduthun. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 39:1"/> I said, “I will guard my ways </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:1">from sinning with my tongue; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 39:1">I will guard my mouth with a muzzle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:1">as long as a wicked one is before me.” <verse eid="PSA 39:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 39:2"/>I was mute <char style="add">in</char> silence, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:2">I kept silent from good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:2">and my sorrow was stirred up. <verse eid="PSA 39:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 39:3"/>My heart became hot within me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:3">in my musing, a fire was kindled; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 39:3">I have spoken with my tongue: <verse eid="PSA 39:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 39:4"/>“Cause me to know, O YHWH, my end, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:4">and the measure of my days—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:4">what <char style="add">is</char> it?—<char style="add">That</char> I may know how fleeting I <char style="add">am</char>. <verse eid="PSA 39:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 39:5"/>Behold, <char style="add">as</char> handbreadths have made my days, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:5">and my lifetime as nothing before You. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 39:5">Truly each one <char style="add">is</char> a vapor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:5">each man is stationary. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 39:5">Selah <verse eid="PSA 39:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 39:6"/>surely like a shadow every man goes about; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:6">surely in vain they are in commotion; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 39:6">he heaps up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:6">and does not know who will gather them. <verse eid="PSA 39:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 39:7"/>And now, what am I waiting, O Lord? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:7">My hope, it <char style="add">is</char> in You. <verse eid="PSA 39:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 39:8"/>May You deliver me from all my transgressions; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:8">do not make me the reproach of the fool! <verse eid="PSA 39:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 39:9"/>I have become mute, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:9">and cannot open my mouth—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:9">O that You would act! <verse eid="PSA 39:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 39:10"/>Turn Your plague away from me! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:10">By the blow of Your hand I am consumed. <verse eid="PSA 39:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 39:11"/>With rebukes over iniquity, You discipline a man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:11">the things he desires you melt away like a moth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:11">surely every man <char style="add">is</char> a vapor. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 39:11">Selah <verse eid="PSA 39:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 39:12"/>hear my prayer, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:12">and turn your ear to my cry; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 39:12">at my tears may You not be silent! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:12">For I <char style="add">am</char> a sojourner with You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:12">a sojourner like all my fathers. <verse eid="PSA 39:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 39:13"/>Turn Your gaze from me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:13">that I might be made glad, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 39:13">before I go <char style="add">on</char> and am no more.” <verse eid="PSA 39:13"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 39"/>

<chapter number="40" style="c" sid="PSA 40"/>

<para style="s">I Waited Patiently for Yahweh</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 40:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Hebrews 10:1–18</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 70:1–5</char></note> I have waited patiently <char style="add">for</char>, YHWH! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:1">And He inclined to me and heard my cry. <verse eid="PSA 40:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 40:2"/>And He brought me up from the pit of desolation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:2">from the mud of the mire; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 40:2">and He raised up my feet upon a rock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:2"><char style="add">and</char> has made firm my steps. <verse eid="PSA 40:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 40:3"/>And He put in my mouth a new song—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:3">praise to our God. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 40:3">Many will see <char style="add">it</char> and will fear, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:3">and they will trust in YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 40:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 40:4"/>Blessed <char style="add">is</char> the man </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:4">who makes YHWH his refuge, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 40:4">and does not turn toward the proud, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:4">and those turning aside to falsehood!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">those turning aside to false gods</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">those running after lies</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 40:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 40:5"/>Much You have done, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:5">O YHWH my God, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 40:5">and wonderful are your thoughts toward us—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:5">none can compare to You! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 40:5">Were I to declare and speak, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:5">they are vast beyond numbering. <verse eid="PSA 40:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 40:6"/>In sacrifice and offering You did not take delight, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:6">You have opened the ears for me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 40:6">burnt offering and sin offering </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:6">You did not require. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">but a body You prepared for me</char></note><verse eid="PSA 40:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 40:7"/>Then I said, “Behold, I have come—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:7">in the roll of the book it is written of me. <verse eid="PSA 40:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 40:8"/>I have delighted to do Your will, O my God,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">40.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Hebrews 10:5–7</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:8">and Your law <char style="add">is</char> in the midst of my heart.” <verse eid="PSA 40:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 40:9"/>I have proclaimed tidings of righteousness in the great assembly; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:9">behold, I do not restrain my lips, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:9">O YHWH, You have known. <verse eid="PSA 40:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 40:10"/>Your righteousness I have not kept hidden in the midst of my heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:10">Your faithfulness and Your salvation I have declared; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 40:10">I have not concealed Your loving devotion and Your truth </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:10">from the great assembly. <verse eid="PSA 40:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 40:11"/>You, O YHWH, do not withhold Your mercies from me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:11">may Your loving devotion and Your truth continually guard me. <verse eid="PSA 40:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 40:12"/>For evils have surrounded against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:12">until there is no numbering <char style="add">them</char>; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 40:12">my iniquities have overtaken me, and I am not able to see; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:12">they are vast <char style="add">beyond</char> the hairs of my head, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:12">and my heart has left me. <verse eid="PSA 40:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 40:13"/>Take pleasure, O YHWH, to deliver me! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:13">O YHWH, may You hurry to help me! <verse eid="PSA 40:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 40:14"/>Let them be put to shame and confounded together, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:14">those seeking my soul, to snatch it away! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 40:14">Let them be driven back </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:14">and humiliated, those delighting in my harm! <verse eid="PSA 40:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 40:15"/>Let them be desolate for a reward of their shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:15">those saying to me, “Aha, aha!” <verse eid="PSA 40:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 40:16"/>All those seeking You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:16">may they rejoice and be glad in You; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 40:16">let those loving Your salvation say continually, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:16">“YHWH be magnified!” <verse eid="PSA 40:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 40:17"/>And I <char style="add">am</char> poor and needy; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:17">may the Lord think of me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 40:17">You <char style="add">are</char> my help and my deliverer—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 40:17">O my God, do not delay! <verse eid="PSA 40:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 40"/>

<chapter number="41" style="c" sid="PSA 41"/>

<para style="s">Victory over Betrayal</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 41:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 13:18–30</char></note> Blessed <char style="add">is</char> he who acts wisely toward the poor; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:1">in a day of evil, YHWH will rescue him. <verse eid="PSA 41:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 41:2"/>YHWH will guard him and keep him alive; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:2">he will be blessed in the land, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 41:2">and You will not deliver him </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:2">to the will of his enemies. <verse eid="PSA 41:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 41:3"/>YHWH will support him on <char style="add">his</char> couch of illness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:3">You turn over all his bed in his sickness. <verse eid="PSA 41:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 41:4"/>I said, “O YHWH, be gracious to me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:4">heal my soul, for I have sinned against You.” <verse eid="PSA 41:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 41:5"/>My enemies speak evil against me: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:5">“When will he die and his name perish?” <verse eid="PSA 41:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 41:6"/>And if one comes to see <char style="add">me</char>, he speaks emptiness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:6">his heart gathers iniquity for himself; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:6">he goes out—at the street he speaks. <verse eid="PSA 41:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 41:7"/>All those hating me, they whisper together against me; against me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:7">they devise evil to me: <verse eid="PSA 41:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 41:8"/>“Let a thing of destruction be poured into him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:8">and <char style="add">he</char> who lies down shall not rise up again.” <verse eid="PSA 41:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 41:9"/>Even a man of my welfare, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:9">he in whom I trusted, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 41:9"><char style="add">who</char> ate my bread, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:9">has lifted up the heel against me. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">41.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in John 13:18</char></note><verse eid="PSA 41:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 41:10"/>But You, O YHWH, show favor to me and raise me up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:10">that I may repay them! <verse eid="PSA 41:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 41:11"/>By this I know that You have delighted in me: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:11">That my enemy will not shout over me. <verse eid="PSA 41:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 41:12"/>And I, in my integrity, may You take hold of me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:12">and set me before Your face forever. <verse eid="PSA 41:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 41:13"/>Blessed <char style="add">be</char> YHWH, God of Israel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 41:13">from forever and even to forever! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 41:13">Amen and Amen. <verse eid="PSA 41:13"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 41"/>

<chapter number="42" style="c" sid="PSA 42"/>

<para style="s">BOOK II</para>

<para style="s">Psalms 42–72</para>

<para style="s">As the Deer Pants for the Water</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Maskil of the sons of Korah.†</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 42:1"/> As the deer pants for streams of water, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:1">so my soul pants for You, O God. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> In many Hebrew manuscripts Psalms 42 and 43 constitute one psalm. </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Maskil</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 42:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 42:2"/>My soul thirsts for God, for the living God. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:2">When shall I come and appear before the face of God?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">42.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and see the face of God?</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 42:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 42:3"/>My tears have been to me <char style="add">as</char> bread, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:3">day and night, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 42:3">in the saying to me all the day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:3">“Where <char style="add">is</char> your God?” <verse eid="PSA 42:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 42:4"/>These <char style="add">things</char> I remember, and I pour out my soul within myself: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:4">How I crossed over with the throng; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 42:4">I moved with them up to the house of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:4">with the voice of shouting and praise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:4">with a multitude keeping the feast. <verse eid="PSA 42:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 42:5"/>Why are you cast down, O my soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:5">and in commotion within me? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 42:5">Wait for God, for still I will praise Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:5">for the salvation of His face. <verse eid="PSA 42:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 42:6"/>O My God, my soul is downcast within me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:6">upon thus I remember You, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 42:6">from the land of the Jordan and Hermon, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:6">from the mount of Mizar. <verse eid="PSA 42:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 42:7"/>Deep is calling to deep, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:7">at the voice of Your waterfalls, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 42:7"><char style="add">and</char> all Your breakers and waves </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:7">have passed over me. <verse eid="PSA 42:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 42:8"/>By day, YHWH commands His loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:8">and in the night His song <char style="add">is</char> with me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:8">a prayer to the God of my life. <verse eid="PSA 42:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 42:9"/>I will say to God my rock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:9">“Why have You forgotten me? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 42:9">Why must I walk in mourning </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:9">in the oppression of the enemy?” <verse eid="PSA 42:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 42:10"/>With a shattering in my bones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:10">my enemies taunt me, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 42:10">in their saying to me all the day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:10">“Where <char style="add">is</char> your God?” <verse eid="PSA 42:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 42:11"/>Why are you cast down, O my soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:11">and why are you in commotion within me? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 42:11">Wait for God, for still I will praise Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 42:11">the salvation of my face, and my God. <verse eid="PSA 42:11"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 42"/>

<chapter number="43" style="c" sid="PSA 43"/>

<para style="s">Send Out Your Light</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 43:1"/>Judge for me, O God, and plead my cause! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 43:1">From a nation unfaithful, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 43:1">from a man of deceit and injustice, may You deliver me. <verse eid="PSA 43:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 43:2"/>For You <char style="add">are</char> the God of my strength. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 43:2">Why have You rejected me? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 43:2">Why must I walk in mourning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 43:2">in the oppression of the enemy? <verse eid="PSA 43:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 43:3"/>Send forth Your light and Your truth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 43:3">they shall guide me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 43:3">let them bring me to Your holy mountain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 43:3">and to Your dwelling place! <verse eid="PSA 43:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 43:4"/>And I will come to the altar of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 43:4">to God, the joy of my rejoicing; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 43:4">and I will praise you with the harp, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 43:4">O God, my God. <verse eid="PSA 43:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 43:5"/>Why are you cast down, O my soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 43:5">and why are you disquieted within me? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 43:5">Wait for God, for still I will praise Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 43:5">the salvation of my face, and my God. <verse eid="PSA 43:5"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 43"/>

<chapter number="44" style="c" sid="PSA 44"/>

<para style="s">Redeem Us, O God</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. Of the sons of Korah. A Maskil.†</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 44:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Romans 8:35–39</char></note> O God, with our ears we have heard; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:1">our fathers have recounted to us </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 44:1">the work You did in their days, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:1">in the days of old. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">44.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Maskil</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 44:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 44:2"/>You, with Your hand, dispossessed the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:2">and You planted them; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 44:2">You afflicted the peoples </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:2">and sent them forth. <verse eid="PSA 44:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 44:3"/>For they did not gain possession of the land by their sword, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:3">and their arm did not bring salvation to them; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 44:3">but <char style="add">it was</char> Your right hand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:3">and Your arm, and the light of Your face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:3">because You delighted in them. <verse eid="PSA 44:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 44:4"/>You are my King, O God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:4">Command deliverances for Jacob. <verse eid="PSA 44:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 44:5"/>Through You we push back our adversaries; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:5">by Your name we trample those rising against us. <verse eid="PSA 44:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 44:6"/>For not in my bow do I trust, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:6">and my sword will not save me.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">44.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">will not give me victory</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; similarly in verse 7</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 44:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 44:7"/>For You have saved us from our adversaries, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:7">and those hating us, You have put to shame. <verse eid="PSA 44:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 44:8"/>In God we have boasted all the day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:8">and we will praise Your name forever. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 44:8">Selah <verse eid="PSA 44:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 44:9"/>yet You have rejected us and put us to shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:9">and You do not go forth with our armies. <verse eid="PSA 44:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 44:10"/>You make us turn back from the adversary, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:10">and those hating us have taken plunder for themselves. <verse eid="PSA 44:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 44:11"/>You have appoint us for food like sheep, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:11">and among the nations You have scattered us. <verse eid="PSA 44:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 44:12"/>You sell Your people with no profit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:12">and You do not gain increase by their price. <verse eid="PSA 44:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 44:13"/>You make us a reproach to our neighbors, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:13">a mockery and derision to those around us. <verse eid="PSA 44:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 44:14"/>You make us a byword among the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:14">a shaking of the head<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">44.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a laughingstock</char></note> among the peoples. <verse eid="PSA 44:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 44:15"/>All the day, my disgrace <char style="add">is</char> before me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:15">and the shame of my face has covered me, <verse eid="PSA 44:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 44:16"/>at the voice of a reproacher and reviler, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:16">from the face of the enemy and avenger. <verse eid="PSA 44:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 44:17"/>All this has come upon us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:17">and we have not forgotten You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:17">and we have not dealt falsely with Your covenant. <verse eid="PSA 44:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 44:18"/>Our heart has not turned back, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:18"><char style="add">nor</char> our steps turned aside from Your path. <verse eid="PSA 44:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 44:19"/>Yet You have crushed us in the place of jackals,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">44.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">serpents</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">dragons</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:19">and You have covered over us with the shadow of death. <verse eid="PSA 44:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 44:20"/>If we had forgotten the name of our God </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:20">or spread out our hands to a strange god, <verse eid="PSA 44:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 44:21"/>would not God search this out? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:21">For He knows the secrets of the heart. <verse eid="PSA 44:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 44:22"/>Yet for Your sake we are killed all the day; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:22">we are reckoned as sheep for the slaughter. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">44.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 8:36</char></note><verse eid="PSA 44:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 44:23"/>Rouse Yourself! Why do You sleep, O Lord? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:23">Awake! Do not reject <char style="add">us</char> forever. <verse eid="PSA 44:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 44:24"/>Why do You hide Your face? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:24">You forget our affliction and our oppression. <verse eid="PSA 44:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 44:25"/>For our soul is bowed down to the dust; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:25">our belly has clung to the ground. <verse eid="PSA 44:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 44:26"/>Rise up as helper to us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 44:26">and redeem us for the sake of Your loving devotion! <verse eid="PSA 44:26"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 44"/>

<chapter number="45" style="c" sid="PSA 45"/>

<para style="s">My Heart Is Stirred by a Noble Theme</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. According to “The Lilies.” Of the sons of Korah. A Maskil.† A song of love.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 45:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 72:1–20</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Chronicles 1:1–13</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Kings 3:1–15</char></note> My heart is stirred by a good word; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:1">I am telling my works, O king;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Maskil</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:1">my tongue <char style="add">is</char> the pen of a swift scribe. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">King</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; here and throughout Psalm 45</char></note><verse eid="PSA 45:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 45:2"/>You are beautiful above the sons of man; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:2">favor is poured out from your lips; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:2">upon thus God has blessed you forever. <verse eid="PSA 45:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 45:3"/>Gird your sword upon the thigh, O mighty one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:3"><char style="add">with</char> your majesty and splendor! <verse eid="PSA 45:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 45:4"/>And <char style="add">in</char> your splendor prosper! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:4">Ride forth upon a word of truth and gentleness <char style="add">and</char> justice; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:4">and your right hand will teach you fearful <char style="add">things</char>. <verse eid="PSA 45:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 45:5"/>Your arrows <char style="add">are</char> sharp—the peoples fall under you—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:5">in the heart of the enemies of the king. <verse eid="PSA 45:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 45:6"/>Your throne, O God, <char style="add">is</char> forever and ever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:6">a scepter of uprightness <char style="add">is</char> the scepter of your kingdom. <verse eid="PSA 45:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 45:7"/>You have loved righteousness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:7">and hated wickedness; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 45:7">upon thus, God, your God </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:7">has anointed you with the oil of joy above your companions. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">45.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Hebrews 1:8–9</char></note><verse eid="PSA 45:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 45:8"/>All your garments <char style="add">are</char> with myrrh and aloes <char style="add">and</char> cassia; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:8">from the palaces of ivory, the harps have made you glad. <verse eid="PSA 45:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 45:9"/>Daughters of kings <char style="add">are</char> among your precious ones; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:9">the queen stands at your right hand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:9">in gold of Ophir. <verse eid="PSA 45:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 45:10"/>Hear, O daughter, and see; and incline your ear, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:10">and forget your people and the house of your father. <verse eid="PSA 45:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 45:11"/>For the king himself desires your beauty, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:11">because he <char style="add">is</char> your lord—and bow to him— <verse eid="PSA 45:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 45:12"/>and the daughter of Tyre, with a gift; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:12">the rich among the people, will seek your face. <verse eid="PSA 45:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 45:13"/>All glorious <char style="add">is</char> the daughter of the king inside; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:13">her clothing <char style="add">is</char> with weavings of gold. <verse eid="PSA 45:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 45:14"/>In various colors she is brought to the king; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:14">the virgins following her, companions of hers, shall be brought to you. <verse eid="PSA 45:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 45:15"/>They are brought along with joy and rejoicing; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:15">they shall come into the palace of the king. <verse eid="PSA 45:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 45:16"/>In place of your fathers shall be your sons, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:16">whom you shall make to <char style="add">be</char> princes in all the earth. <verse eid="PSA 45:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 45:17"/>I will cause your name to be remembered through all generations; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 45:17">upon thus the people will praise you forever and ever. <verse eid="PSA 45:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 45"/>

<chapter number="46" style="c" sid="PSA 46"/>

<para style="s">God Is Our Refuge and Strength</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. Of the sons of Korah. According to Alamoth.† A Song.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 46:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Chronicles 32:1–8</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Kings 18:13–16</char></note> God <char style="add">is</char> unto us a place of refuge and strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:1">a help in distress surely to be found. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">46.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Alamoth</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; here and in 1 Chronicles 15:20.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 46:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 46:2"/>Upon thus we will not fear, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:2">with the changing of the earth, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 46:2">and with the shaking of the mountains </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:2">into the heart of the seas— <verse eid="PSA 46:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 46:3"/>its waters roar and foam, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:3"><char style="add">and</char> the mountains quake in its rising. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 46:3">Selah <verse eid="PSA 46:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 46:4"/><char style="add">there is</char> a river whose streams make glad the city of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:4">the Holy Place of the dwelling of the Most High. <verse eid="PSA 46:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 46:5"/>God <char style="add">is</char> within her; she will not be shaken; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:5">God will help her at the turn of the morning. <verse eid="PSA 46:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 46:6"/>The nations raged, the kingdoms were shaken; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:6">He has given forth with His voice; the earth melts. <verse eid="PSA 46:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 46:7"/>YHWH of Hosts <char style="add">is</char> with us; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:7">a secure height for us <char style="add">is</char> the God of Jacob. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 46:7">Selah <verse eid="PSA 46:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 46:8"/>Come, see the works of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:8">who has set devastation upon the earth. <verse eid="PSA 46:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 46:9"/>He makes wars cease to the end of the earth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:9">the bow He breaks, and the spear He cuts apart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:9">the shields<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">46.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">chariots</char></note> He burns in the fire. <verse eid="PSA 46:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 46:10"/>“Be still and know that I <char style="add">am</char> God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:10">I will be exalted among the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:10">I will be exalted over the earth.” <verse eid="PSA 46:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 46:11"/>YHWH of Hosts <char style="add">is</char> with us; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 46:11">a secure height for us <char style="add">is</char> the God of Jacob. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 46:11">Selah <verse eid="PSA 46:11"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 46"/>

<chapter number="47" style="c" sid="PSA 47"/>

<para style="s">Clap Your Hands, All You Peoples</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. Of the sons of Korah. A Psalm.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 47:1"/> All <char style="add">you</char> peoples, clap your hands; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 47:1">shout unto God, with a voice of a ringing cry! <verse eid="PSA 47:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 47:2"/>For YHWH-Elyon<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">47.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">YHWH-Elyon</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">LORD Most High</char></note> <char style="add">is</char> to be feared; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 47:2"><char style="add">He is</char> the great King over all the earth. <verse eid="PSA 47:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 47:3"/>He turns back the peoples under us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 47:3">and the nations under our feet. <verse eid="PSA 47:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 47:4"/>He chose for us our inheritance, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 47:4">the excellence of Jacob, whom He loves. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 47:4">Selah <verse eid="PSA 47:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 47:5"/>God has gone up with a shout, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 47:5">YHWH with the voice of a shofar. <verse eid="PSA 47:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 47:6"/>Sing praises to God, sing praises! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 47:6">Sing praises to our King, sing praises! <verse eid="PSA 47:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 47:7"/>For the King of all the earth <char style="add">is</char> God—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 47:7">sing praises <char style="add">with</char> skill!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">47.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">sing a Maskil of praise</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">sing praises with understanding</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 47:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 47:8"/>God reigns over the nations; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 47:8">God sits upon the throne of His holiness. <verse eid="PSA 47:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 47:9"/>The princes of the peoples have gathered together, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 47:9">the people of the God of Abraham; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 47:9">for the shields of the earth <char style="add">are</char> unto God—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 47:9"><char style="add">He is</char> greatly to be exalted. <verse eid="PSA 47:9"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 47"/>

<chapter number="48" style="c" sid="PSA 48"/>

<para style="s">Broken Bondage</para>

<para style="s">A song. A Psalm of the sons of Korah.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 48:1"/> Great <char style="add">is</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:1">and greatly to be praised, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 48:1">in the city of our God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:1">the mountain of His holiness. <verse eid="PSA 48:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 48:2"/>Beautiful <char style="add">in</char> elevation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:2">the joy of all the earth, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 48:2">like the peaks of Zaphon<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the far north</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; the most sacred mountain of the Canaanites was </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Zaphon</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char></note> <char style="add">is</char> Mount Zion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:2">the city of the great King. <verse eid="PSA 48:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 48:3"/>God <char style="add">is</char> in her citadels, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:3">known as a secure height. <verse eid="PSA 48:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 48:4"/>For behold, the kings assembled; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:4">they passed over together. <verse eid="PSA 48:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 48:5"/>They saw, so they were astonished; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:5">they were in dismay, and they hurried away. <verse eid="PSA 48:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 48:6"/>Trembling took hold of them there, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:6"><char style="add">and</char> writhing like a woman in labor. <verse eid="PSA 48:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 48:7"/>With a wind of the east </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:7">you broke apart the ships of Tarshish.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the fleet of trading ships</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 48:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 48:8"/>According to what we have heard, so we have seen, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:8">in the city of YHWH of Hosts, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 48:8">in the city of our God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:8">God will establish her even to forever! </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 48:8">Selah <verse eid="PSA 48:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 48:9"/>we have reflected, O God, <char style="add">on</char> Your loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:9">within Your temple. <verse eid="PSA 48:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 48:10"/>According to Your name, O God, so Your praise </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:10"><char style="add">is</char> unto the ends of the earth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:10">Your right hand is full of righteousness. <verse eid="PSA 48:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 48:11"/>Let Mount Zion be glad; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:11">let the daughters<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the villages</char></note> of Judah rejoice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:11">on account of Your judgments! <verse eid="PSA 48:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 48:12"/>Go around Zion and encircle her, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:12"><char style="add">and</char> count her towers. <verse eid="PSA 48:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 48:13"/>Set your⁺ heart toward her bulwark, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:13">pass between her citadels, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:13">so that you⁺ may recount <char style="add">it</char> to the following generation. <verse eid="PSA 48:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 48:14"/>For this <char style="add">is</char> God, Our God, forever and ever! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 48:14">He will lead us over death.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">48.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He will guide us even until death</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 48:14"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 48"/>

<chapter number="49" style="c" sid="PSA 49"/>

<para style="s">The Evanescence of Wealth</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. Of the sons of Korah. A Psalm.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 49:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Ecclesiastes 5:8–20</char></note> Hear this, all <char style="add">you</char> peoples; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:1">give ear, all <char style="add">you</char> dwellers of the world, <verse eid="PSA 49:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 49:2"/>both sons of a man and sons of a <char style="add">great</char> man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:2">the rich and the poor together! <verse eid="PSA 49:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 49:3"/>My mouth will speak wisdom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:3">and a declaration of my heart, understanding. <verse eid="PSA 49:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 49:4"/>I will incline my ear to a proverb; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:4">I will open up my riddle with the harp. <verse eid="PSA 49:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 49:5"/>Why should I fear in the days of evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:5">the perversion <char style="add">that</char> surrounds me <char style="add">at</char> my heels, <verse eid="PSA 49:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 49:6"/>those trusting in their wealth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:6">and <char style="add">who</char> boast in the abundance of their riches? <verse eid="PSA 49:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 49:7"/>A brother surely cannot ransom a man,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">49.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">redeem another</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:7">and he cannot give to God his redemption price. <verse eid="PSA 49:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 49:8"/>For costly <char style="add">is</char> the ransom of their soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:8">and it shall cease forever, <verse eid="PSA 49:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 49:9"/>that he might live on forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:9"><char style="add">and</char> not see the Pit. <verse eid="PSA 49:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 49:10"/>For he sees wise men die; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:10">the fool and the senseless one perish together, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:10">and they leave their wealth for others. <verse eid="PSA 49:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 49:11"/>Their inward thoughts<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">49.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX, Syriac, and Aramaic Targum </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Their graves</char></note> <char style="add">are</char> their homes forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:11">their dwelling places from generation to generation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:11">they proclaimed over the lands their own names. <verse eid="PSA 49:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 49:12"/>And man in <char style="add">his</char> wealth does not remain; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:12">he becomes like the beasts that perish. <verse eid="PSA 49:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 49:13"/>This <char style="add">is</char> their path of folly<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">49.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the fate of the foolish</char></note> for them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:13">and after them in their sayings they took delight. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 49:13">Selah <verse eid="PSA 49:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 49:14"/>like sheep they are appointed for Sheol, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:14"><char style="add">and</char> death will be their shepherd; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 49:14">the upright will rule over them in the morning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:14">and their form shall be consumed <char style="add">in</char> Sheol—the habitation for him. <verse eid="PSA 49:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 49:15"/>Surely God will redeem my soul from the hand of Sheol, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:15">for He shall take me. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 49:15">Selah <verse eid="PSA 49:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 49:16"/>do not be afraid when a man becomes rich, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:16">when the glory of his house increases. <verse eid="PSA 49:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 49:17"/>For in his death he will take of it all nothing; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:17">his glory will not go down after him, <verse eid="PSA 49:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 49:18"/>though his soul, in his living, he blesses, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:18">and they praise you when you do well for yourself. <verse eid="PSA 49:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 49:19"/>He will come to the generation of his fathers; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:19">even to forever they shall not see light. <verse eid="PSA 49:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 49:20"/>A man in <char style="add">his</char> splendor does not understand; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 49:20">he is like the beasts that perish! <verse eid="PSA 49:20"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 49"/>

<chapter number="50" style="c" sid="PSA 50"/>

<para style="s">The Mighty One Calls</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of Asaph.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 50:1"/> God of gods, YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:1">speaks and calls the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:1">from the rising of the sun to the going down. <verse eid="PSA 50:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 50:2"/>From Zion, the perfection of beauty, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:2">God shines forth. <verse eid="PSA 50:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 50:3"/>Our God comes and will not be silent; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:3">before His face a fire devours, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:3">and all around Him it will storm exceedingly. <verse eid="PSA 50:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 50:4"/>He calls to the heavens from above, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:4">and to the earth, for the judging of His people: <verse eid="PSA 50:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 50:5"/>“Gather to Me My holy ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:5">those having cut a covenant with Me by sacrifice.” <verse eid="PSA 50:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 50:6"/>And let the heavens declare His righteousness—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:6">for God Himself is Judge.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">50.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for He is a God of justice</char></note> </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 50:6">Selah <verse eid="PSA 50:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 50:7"/>“Hear, O My people, and I will speak; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:7">O Israel, and I will testify against you: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:7">I <char style="add">am</char> God, your God. <verse eid="PSA 50:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 50:8"/><char style="add">It is</char> not over your sacrifices <char style="add">that</char> I rebuke you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:8">or your burnt offerings before me continually. <verse eid="PSA 50:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 50:9"/>I will not take a bull from your house </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:9"><char style="add">or</char> male goats from your folds. <verse eid="PSA 50:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 50:10"/>For every living <char style="add">thing</char> of the forest <char style="add">is</char> unto Me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:10"><char style="add">and</char> the cattle on a thousand hills. <verse eid="PSA 50:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 50:11"/>I know every bird of the mountains, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:11">and the wild beast of the field <char style="add">is</char> unto Me. <verse eid="PSA 50:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 50:12"/>If I were hungry, I would not say <char style="add">it</char> to you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:12">for the world and its fullness <char style="add">is</char> to Me. <verse eid="PSA 50:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 50:13"/>Do I eat the flesh of bulls, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:13">and do I drink the blood of goats? <verse eid="PSA 50:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 50:14"/>Make a sacrifice of thanksgiving to God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:14">and fulfill to the Most High your vows. <verse eid="PSA 50:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 50:15"/>And call on Me in the day of distress, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:15"><char style="add">and</char> I will rescue you, and you will glorify Me.” <verse eid="PSA 50:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 50:16"/>And to the wicked God says, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:16">“What to you <char style="add">is</char> to recount My statutes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:16">and to lift up My covenant upon your mouth? <verse eid="PSA 50:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 50:17"/>And you have hated instruction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:17">and cast My words behind you! <verse eid="PSA 50:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 50:18"/>If you see a thief, then you are pleased with him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:18">and your portion <char style="add">is</char> with those committing adultery. <verse eid="PSA 50:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 50:19"/>With your mouth you send forth evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:19">and your tongue weaves deceit. <verse eid="PSA 50:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 50:20"/>You sit against your brother and speak; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:20">against the son of your mother you place fault. <verse eid="PSA 50:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 50:21"/>These <char style="add">things</char> you have done, and I kept silent; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:21">you thought I was just<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">50.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">you thought the ‘I AM’ was</char></note> like you. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 50:21">I will rebuke you </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:21">and set in array before your eyes.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">50.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and accuse you to your face</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 50:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 50:22"/>Understand this, please, <char style="add">you</char> forgetting God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:22">lest I tear <char style="add">you</char> in pieces, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:22">and there is no one to deliver! <verse eid="PSA 50:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 50:23"/>The one making a sacrifice of thanksgiving honors Me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:23">and he <char style="add">who</char> sets <char style="add">his</char> path, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 50:23">I will make to look on the salvation of God.” <verse eid="PSA 50:23"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 50"/>

<chapter number="51" style="c" sid="PSA 51"/>

<para style="s">Create in Me a Clean Heart, O God</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Psalm of David, in the coming of Nathan the prophet to him after that he had gone in to Bathsheba.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 51:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Samuel 12:1–12</char></note> Have mercy on me<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">51.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Be gracious to me</char></note> O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:1">according to Your loving devotion; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 51:1">according to the abundance of Your compassion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:1">wipe out my transgressions. <verse eid="PSA 51:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 51:2"/>Wash me thoroughly from my iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:2">and cleanse me from my sin. <verse eid="PSA 51:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 51:3"/>For I know my transgressions, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:3">and my sin <char style="add">is</char> before me continually. <verse eid="PSA 51:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 51:4"/>Against You, You alone, have I sinned, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:4">and have done the evil in your eyes, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 51:4">so that You are right when You speak, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:4">and You are pure when You judge. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">51.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and victorious when You judge</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Romans 3:4</char></note><verse eid="PSA 51:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 51:5"/>Behold, in iniquity I was brought forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:5">and in sin my mother conceived me. <verse eid="PSA 51:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 51:6"/>Behold, You take delight <char style="add">in</char> truth in the inner parts; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:6">in the inmost place You teach me wisdom. <verse eid="PSA 51:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 51:7"/>Cleanse my sin with hyssop, and I will be clean; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:7">wash me, and I will be whiter than snow. <verse eid="PSA 51:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 51:8"/>Make me hear joy and gladness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:8">let the bones You have crushed rejoice. <verse eid="PSA 51:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 51:9"/>May You hide Your face from my sins, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:9">and wipe out all my iniquities. <verse eid="PSA 51:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 51:10"/>Create a clean heart in me, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:10">and renew a right spirit within me. <verse eid="PSA 51:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 51:11"/>Do not cast me away from before Your face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:11">and do not take away from me Your Holy Spirit. <verse eid="PSA 51:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 51:12"/>Restore to me the joy of Your salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:12">and uphold me <char style="add">by a</char> willing spirit. <verse eid="PSA 51:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 51:13"/>I will teach transgressors Your ways, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:13">and sinners will return to You. <verse eid="PSA 51:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 51:14"/>Deliver me from bloodguilt, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:14">the God of my salvation; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:14">my tongue will sing of Your righteousness. <verse eid="PSA 51:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 51:15"/>O Lord, open my lips, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:15">and my mouth will declare Your praise. <verse eid="PSA 51:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 51:16"/>For You do not take delight <char style="add">in</char> sacrifice, or I would give <char style="add">it</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:16"><char style="add">with</char> a burnt offering You are not pleased. <verse eid="PSA 51:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 51:17"/>The sacrifices of God <char style="add">are</char> a broken spirit. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:17">A heart broken and crushed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:17">O God, You will not despise. <verse eid="PSA 51:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 51:18"/>By Your pleasure, do good to Zion; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:18">may You build up the walls of Jerusalem. <verse eid="PSA 51:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 51:19"/>Then You will delight <char style="add">in</char> the sacrifices of righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:19">a burnt offering and whole <char style="add">sacrifice</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 51:19">then they will offer bulls upon Your altar. <verse eid="PSA 51:19"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 51"/>

<chapter number="52" style="c" sid="PSA 52"/>

<para style="s">Why Do You Boast of Evil?</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Maskil† of David, in the coming of Doeg the Edomite, when he announced to Saul and said to him, “David has gone to the house of Ahimelech.”</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 52:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Samuel 22:6–23</char></note> Why do you boast in evil, O mighty man? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 52:1">The loving devotion of God <char style="add">is</char> all the day. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">52.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Maskil</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 52:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 52:2"/>Your tongue devises destruction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 52:2">like a sharp razor working deceit. <verse eid="PSA 52:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 52:3"/>You love evil more than good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 52:3">lying more than speaking righteousness. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 52:3">Selah <verse eid="PSA 52:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 52:4"/>You love all devouring words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 52:4">O tongue of deceit! <verse eid="PSA 52:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 52:5"/>Even God will tear you down forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 52:5">He will take you up and pluck you out of the tent </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 52:5">and uproot you from the land of the living. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 52:5">Selah <verse eid="PSA 52:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 52:6"/>and the righteous will see and fear, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 52:6">and they shall laugh at him: <verse eid="PSA 52:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 52:7"/>“Behold the man </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 52:7">who did not set God <char style="add">as</char> his refuge, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 52:7">and <char style="add">who</char> trusted in the abundance of his wealth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 52:7"><char style="add">and</char> took strength by destruction.” <verse eid="PSA 52:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 52:8"/>And I <char style="add">am</char> green, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 52:8">like an olive tree in the house of God; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 52:8">I trust in the loving devotion of God </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 52:8">forever and ever. <verse eid="PSA 52:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 52:9"/>I will confess You forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 52:9">because You have done <char style="add">it</char>. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 52:9">And I will call on Your name, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 52:9">for <char style="add">it is</char> good before of Your holy ones. <verse eid="PSA 52:9"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 52"/>

<chapter number="53" style="c" sid="PSA 53"/>

<para style="s">The Fool Says There Is No God</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. According to Mahalath.† A Maskil† of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 53:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Romans 3:9–20</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Isaiah 59:1–17</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 14:1–7</char></note> The fool says in his heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 53:1">“There is no God.” </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 53:1">They are corrupt and have done abominable injustice; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 53:1">there is no one doing good. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">53.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Mahalath</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; see also Psalm 88:1.</char></note><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">53.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Maskil</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 53:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 53:2"/>God looks down from the heavens </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 53:2">upon the sons of man, to see: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 53:2">Is there one acting wisely, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 53:2">seeking God? <verse eid="PSA 53:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 53:3"/>All have turned back, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 53:3">together they have become corrupt;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">53.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">worthless</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 53:3">there is no one doing good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 53:3">not even one.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">53.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 3:10–12</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 53:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 53:4"/>Will they not learn, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 53:4">the workers of iniquity, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 53:4">those devouring my people they have devoured bread; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 53:4">they do not call upon God. <verse eid="PSA 53:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 53:5"/>There they feared a fear—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 53:5">there was no fear. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 53:5">For God scattered the bones </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 53:5">of the one setting camp against you; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 53:5">you have put <char style="add">them</char> to shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 53:5">for God has rejected them. <verse eid="PSA 53:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 53:6"/>Who will give from Zion the salvation of Israel? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 53:6">God, in turning back the captivity of His people,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">53.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the fortunes of His people</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 53:6">let Jacob rejoice; let Israel be glad! <verse eid="PSA 53:6"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 53"/>

<chapter number="54" style="c" sid="PSA 54"/>

<para style="s">Save Me by Your Name</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. With stringed instruments. A Maskil† of David, at the coming of the Ziphites, when they said to Saul, “Is not David hiding himself with us?”</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 54:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Samuel 23:7–29</char></note> O God, by Your name save me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 54:1">and by Your might defend me! <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">54.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Maskil</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 54:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 54:2"/>O God, hear my prayer, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 54:2">give ear to the words of my mouth. <verse eid="PSA 54:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 54:3"/>For strangers have risen up against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 54:3">and terrible ones have sought my soul; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 54:3">they have not put God before them. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 54:3">Selah <verse eid="PSA 54:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 54:4"/>behold, God <char style="add">is</char> the One giving help to me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 54:4">the Lord <char style="add">is</char> with those upholding my soul. <verse eid="PSA 54:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 54:5"/>He will return the evil to my enemies—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 54:5">in Your faithfulness put an end to them! <verse eid="PSA 54:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 54:6"/>With a freewill offering I will sacrifice to You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 54:6">I will give thanks to Your name, O YHWH, for <char style="add">it is</char> good. <verse eid="PSA 54:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 54:7"/>For from all distress He has delivered me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 54:7">and on my enemies my eye has looked. <verse eid="PSA 54:7"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 54"/>

<chapter number="55" style="c" sid="PSA 55"/>

<para style="s">Cast Your Burden upon Yahweh</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. With stringed instruments. A Maskil† of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 55:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Samuel 17:15–29</char></note> Turn your ear, O God, to my prayer, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:1">and do not hide Yourself from my supplication. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">55.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Maskil</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 55:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 55:2"/>Be attentive to me, and answer me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:2"><char style="add">for</char> I am restless in my complaint, and make a noise, <verse eid="PSA 55:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 55:3"/>from the voice of the enemy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:3">from the face of the oppression of the wicked. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 55:3">For they bring down trouble upon me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:3">and in anger they hate me. <verse eid="PSA 55:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 55:4"/>My heart is writhing within me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:4">and the terrors of death have fallen upon me. <verse eid="PSA 55:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 55:5"/>Fear and trembling have come upon me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:5">and shuddering has covered me. <verse eid="PSA 55:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 55:6"/>And I said, “Who shall give to me a wing like a dove, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:6"><char style="add">that</char> I might fly away and be at rest— <verse eid="PSA 55:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 55:7"/>behold, I would go far off wandering </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:7"><char style="add">and</char> would lodge in the wilderness. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 55:7">Selah <verse eid="PSA 55:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 55:8"/>I would hurry to shelter for myself, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:8">from the rushing wind, from the tempest.” <verse eid="PSA 55:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 55:9"/>Swallow up, O Lord, divide their tongues! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:9">For I have seen violence and strife in the city. <verse eid="PSA 55:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 55:10"/>Day and night they go around it, on its walls, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:10">and iniquity and trouble <char style="add">are</char> within it. <verse eid="PSA 55:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 55:11"/>Disasters <char style="add">are</char> within it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:11">and oppression and deceit do not depart from its streets. <verse eid="PSA 55:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 55:12"/>For <char style="add">it is</char> not an enemy <char style="add">who</char> scorns me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:12">or I could bear it; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 55:12">and not one hating me <char style="add">who</char> wielded power against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:12">or I could hide myself from him. <verse eid="PSA 55:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 55:13"/>And <char style="add">it was</char> you, a man like me in rank, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:13">my companion, and one known by me, <verse eid="PSA 55:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 55:14"/><char style="add">with</char> whom we would take sweet counsel together; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:14">in the house of God we walked with the throng. <verse eid="PSA 55:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 55:15"/>Devastation <char style="add">is</char> upon them! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:15">May they go down alive <char style="add">to</char> Sheol! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:15">For evils <char style="add">are</char> in their dwellings, within them. <verse eid="PSA 55:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 55:16"/>I will call to God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:16">and YHWH will save me. <verse eid="PSA 55:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 55:17"/>Evening and morning and noon I meditate and cry aloud, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:17">and He hears my voice. <verse eid="PSA 55:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 55:18"/>In peace He has redeemed my soul from the battle against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:18">though there were many against me. <verse eid="PSA 55:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 55:19"/>God will hear and afflict them—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:19">even He who sits of old—</para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 55:19">Selah </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 55:19">with whom there are no changes for Him. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:19">And they have not fear God. <verse eid="PSA 55:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 55:20"/>He has stretched out his hands against those united with him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:20">he has profaned his covenant. <verse eid="PSA 55:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 55:21"/>His mouth has been smoother than butter, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:21">and war <char style="add">is</char> in his heart; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 55:21">his words have been softer than oil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:21">and they <char style="add">are</char> drawn swords. <verse eid="PSA 55:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 55:22"/>Cast your burden upon YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:22">and He will sustain you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:22">He will not give a righteous one to be shaken forever. <verse eid="PSA 55:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 55:23"/>And You, O God, will bring them down </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:23">to the Pit of destruction, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 55:23">men of blood and deceit! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 55:23">They will not live even half their days. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 55:23">And I will trust in You. <verse eid="PSA 55:23"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 55"/>

<chapter number="56" style="c" sid="PSA 56"/>

<para style="s">Be Merciful to Me, O God</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing according to “A Dove of Distant Oaks.” Of David. A Miktam† in the seizing of him by the Philistines in Gath.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 56:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Samuel 21:8–15</char></note> Show favor to me, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:1">for man would swallow me up; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:1">all the day fighting, he oppresses me. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">56.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Miktam</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 16 and 56–60.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 56:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 56:2"/>My enemies swallow <char style="add">me</char> up all the day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:2">for many <char style="add">are</char> fighting against me proudly. <verse eid="PSA 56:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 56:3"/><char style="add">On</char> the day I am afraid, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:3">I will trust in You. <verse eid="PSA 56:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 56:4"/>In God—His word I praise—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:4">in God do I trust. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 56:4">I will not fear; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:4">what can flesh do to me? <verse eid="PSA 56:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 56:5"/>All the day they wrest my words; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:5">their thoughts <char style="add">are</char> all for evil against me. <verse eid="PSA 56:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 56:6"/>They gather together, they hide, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:6">they mark my steps </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:6">when they lie in wait for my soul. <verse eid="PSA 56:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 56:7"/>Over iniquity bring <char style="add">no</char> escape<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">56.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> MT does not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">no</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> for them! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:7">In <char style="add">your</char> anger, may You cast down the nations, O God! <verse eid="PSA 56:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 56:8"/>My wanderings<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">56.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">sorrows</char></note> You have counted; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:8">put my tears in Your bottle—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:8">are <char style="add">they</char> not in Your book? <verse eid="PSA 56:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 56:9"/>Then my enemies will turn back </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:9">on the day I cry out. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:9">This I have known, that God <char style="add">is</char> for me. <verse eid="PSA 56:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 56:10"/>In God whose word I do praise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:10">in YHWH whose word I praise— <verse eid="PSA 56:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 56:11"/>in God I have put my trust! I will not be afraid. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:11">What can man do to me? <verse eid="PSA 56:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 56:12"/>Your vows, O God, <char style="add">are</char> upon me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:12">I will give thank offerings to You. <verse eid="PSA 56:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 56:13"/>For You have delivered my soul from death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:13"><char style="add">Do You</char> not keep my feet from falling, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 56:13">that I may walk before God </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 56:13">in the light of the living! <verse eid="PSA 56:13"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 56"/>

<chapter number="57" style="c" sid="PSA 57"/>

<para style="s">In You My Soul Takes Refuge</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. To “Do not Destroy.” Of David. A Miktam† in his fleeing from the face of Saul in the cave.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 57:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 142:1–7</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 108:1–13</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Samuel 22:1–5</char></note> Have mercy on me, O God, have mercy on me! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:1">For in You my soul takes refuge, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 57:1">and in the shadow of Your wings I will make my refuge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:1">until the calamities have passed by. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">57.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Miktam</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 16 and 56–60.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 57:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 57:2"/>I will call out to El-Elyon,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">57.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">El-Elyon</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">God Most High</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:2">to God, who fulfills for me. <verse eid="PSA 57:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 57:3"/>He sends forth from the heavens, and saves me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:3">He rebukes the one panting after me. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 57:3">Selah </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 57:3">God sends forth </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:3">His loving devotion and His faithfulness. <verse eid="PSA 57:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 57:4"/>My soul <char style="add">is</char> in the midst of lions; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:4">I lie down <char style="add">among</char> flames—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 57:4">the sons of men, their teeth <char style="add">are</char> spears and arrows, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:4">and their tongue <char style="add">is</char> a sharp sword. <verse eid="PSA 57:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 57:5"/>Be exalted above the heavens, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:5">Your glory above all the earth! <verse eid="PSA 57:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 57:6"/>They have prepared a net for my steps; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:6">my soul is bent down; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 57:6">they have dug before me a pit—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:6">may they fall into its midst! </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 57:6">Selah <verse eid="PSA 57:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 57:7"/>my heart is steadfast, O God, my heart is steadfast; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:7">I will sing and make music. <verse eid="PSA 57:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 57:8"/>Awake, my glory!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">57.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Awake, my soul!</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:8">Awake, O harp and lyre—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:8">I will awaken the dawn! <verse eid="PSA 57:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 57:9"/>I will confess You among the peoples, O Lord; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:9">I will make music to You among the nations. <verse eid="PSA 57:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 57:10"/>For Your loving devotion reaches to the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:10">and Your faithfulness to the clouds. <verse eid="PSA 57:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 57:11"/><char style="add">Be</char> lifted high above the heavens, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 57:11"><char style="add">and</char> above all the earth Your glory! <verse eid="PSA 57:11"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 57"/>

<chapter number="58" style="c" sid="PSA 58"/>

<para style="s">God Judges the Earth</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. “Do not Destroy.” Of David. a Miktam.†</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 58:1"/> <char style="add">Is it</char> truly righteousness you⁺ speak? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:1">Do you⁺ judge uprightly, O sons of man? <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">58.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Miktam</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 16 and 56–60.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 58:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 58:2"/>Even in the heart you⁺ work iniquities; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:2">in the earth you⁺ weigh out the violence of your⁺ hands. <verse eid="PSA 58:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 58:3"/>The wicked are estranged from the womb; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:3">they have gone astray from the belly, speaking lies. <verse eid="PSA 58:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 58:4"/>Their venom <char style="add">is</char> like the venom of a snake, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:4">like the deaf cobra that stops up its ear, <verse eid="PSA 58:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 58:5"/>which will not listen to the voice of those whispering—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:5">charmers most skillfully charming. <verse eid="PSA 58:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 58:6"/>O God, may You break their teeth in their mouths; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:6">tear out the great teeth of the young lions, O YHWH! <verse eid="PSA 58:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 58:7"/>Let them flow away like waters, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:7">running continually to themselves; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 58:7">he treads the <char style="add">bow</char>—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:7">may his arrows be as though cut in pieces.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">58.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">when they are trodden down, may they wither like grass</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 58:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 58:8"/>Like a snail melting as it goes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:8">the stillborn child of a woman, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:8">may they not see the sun! <verse eid="PSA 58:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 58:9"/>Before your⁺ pots can discern the thorn, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:9">as those living, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:9">as burning wrath He sweeps <char style="add">them</char> away. <verse eid="PSA 58:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 58:10"/>The righteous one will rejoice </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:10">when he has seen vengeance; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 58:10">he will wash his feet </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:10">in the blood of the wicked. <verse eid="PSA 58:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 58:11"/>Then man will say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:11">“Surely fruit <char style="add">is</char> for the righteous; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 58:11">surely there is a God judging the earth!” <verse eid="PSA 58:11"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 58"/>

<chapter number="59" style="c" sid="PSA 59"/>

<para style="s">Deliver Me from My Enemies</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. “To Do not Destroy.” Of David. a Miktam† at the sending of men by Saul, when they watched the house in order to kill him.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 59:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Samuel 19:1–24</char></note> Snatch me from my enemies, O my God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:1">from those who rise against me, set me on <char style="add">a place up</char> high. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">59.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Miktam</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 16 and 56–60.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 59:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 59:2"/>Deliver me from the workers of iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:2">and save me from men of blood! <verse eid="PSA 59:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 59:3"/>For behold, they lie in wait for my life; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:3">the mighty ones gather against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:3">not <char style="add">for</char> my transgression and not <char style="add">for</char> my sin, O YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 59:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 59:4"/>Without <char style="add">my</char> fault, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:4">they run and prepare themselves. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:4">Awake to help me, and see! <verse eid="PSA 59:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 59:5"/>And You, O YHWH, God of Hosts, the God of Israel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:5">may You awaken to attend to all the nations! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:5">You must not be merciful to any of those acting treacherously <char style="add">with</char> wickedness. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 59:5">Selah <verse eid="PSA 59:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 59:6"/>they return at the evening; they growl like a dog, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:6">and go all around the city. <verse eid="PSA 59:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 59:7"/>Behold, they belch out with their mouths. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:7">Swords <char style="add">are</char> in their lips: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:7">“For who hears?” <verse eid="PSA 59:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 59:8"/>But You, O YHWH, laugh at them! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:8">You scoff at all the nations. <verse eid="PSA 59:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 59:9"/>O <char style="add">my</char> strength, I will keep watch for You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:9">for God <char style="add">is</char> my secure height. <verse eid="PSA 59:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 59:10"/>The God of loving devotion will meet me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:10">God will let me look on my enemies. <verse eid="PSA 59:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 59:11"/>Do not kill them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:11">lest my people forget. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 59:11">Send them staggering by Your strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:11">and bring them down! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:11">O Lord, our shield. <verse eid="PSA 59:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 59:12"/>The sin of their mouth </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:12"><char style="add">is</char> a word of their lips; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 59:12">let them be captured in their pride </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:12">and in the cursing and lies they recount. <verse eid="PSA 59:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 59:13"/>Consume <char style="add">them</char> in fury, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:13">consume <char style="add">them</char>, and they are no more! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 59:13">And let them know that God </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:13">is ruling in Jacob to the ends of the earth. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 59:13">Selah <verse eid="PSA 59:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 59:14"/>and they return in the evening; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:14">they growl like a dog, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:14">and go round about the city. <verse eid="PSA 59:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 59:15"/>They wander up and down for food; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:15">and if they are not satisfied, then they grumble. <verse eid="PSA 59:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 59:16"/>But I will sing of Your power, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:16">and I will sing out Your loving devotion in the morning. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 59:16">For You have been a high place for me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:16">and a refuge for me in the day of distress. <verse eid="PSA 59:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 59:17"/>O My strength, to You I will sing praises! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:17">For God <char style="add">is</char> my secure height, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 59:17">the God of loving devotion <char style="add">to</char> me. <verse eid="PSA 59:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 59"/>

<chapter number="60" style="c" sid="PSA 60"/>

<para style="s">Victory with God</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. According to “The Lily of the Covenant.” A Miktam† of David for teaching, in his struggling with Aram-naharaim† and with Aram-zobah,† when Joab returned and struck Edom in the Valley of Salt—twelve thousand men.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 60:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 108:1–13</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Chronicles 18:1–13</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Samuel 8:1–14</char></note> O God, You have rejected us; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:1">You have broken us; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 60:1">You have been angry; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:1">may You return to us! <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">60.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Miktam</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 16 and 56–60.</char></note><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">60.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Mesopotamia; </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Aram-naharaim</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Aram of the two rivers</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, likely the region between the Euphrates and Balih Rivers in northwestern Mesopotamia.</char></note><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">60.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the land northeast of Damascus</char></note><verse eid="PSA 60:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 60:2"/>The earth You have made quake; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:2">You have torn it open; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 60:2">may You heal its fractures, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:2">for it is tottering. <verse eid="PSA 60:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 60:3"/>You have made Your people see hardship; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:3">You have made us drink the wine of staggering. <verse eid="PSA 60:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 60:4"/>You have given a banner to those who fear You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:4">to be set prominently before the face of the bow.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">60.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">that it may be displayed because of truth</char></note> </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 60:4">Selah <verse eid="PSA 60:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 60:5"/>That Your beloved may be rescued, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:5">bring salvation <char style="add">with</char> Your right hand and answer us. <verse eid="PSA 60:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 60:6"/>God has spoken in His holiness:<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">60.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from His sanctuary</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:6">“I will rejoice; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 60:6">I will divide Shechem, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:6">and I will measure out the Valley of Succoth. <verse eid="PSA 60:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 60:7"/>Gilead <char style="add">is</char> unto Me, and Manasseh <char style="add">is</char> unto Me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:7">and Ephraim <char style="add">is</char> the helmet for My head; Judah <char style="add">is</char> My scepter; <verse eid="PSA 60:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 60:8"/>Moab <char style="add">is</char> the pot <char style="add">for</char> my washing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:8"><char style="add">and</char> upon Edom I will cast My sandal; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:8">I will give a shout over Philistia.” <verse eid="PSA 60:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 60:9"/>Who will bring me <char style="add">to</char> the city of fortification? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:9">Who will lead me to Edom? <verse eid="PSA 60:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 60:10"/>Have You not, O God, rejected us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:10">and do You not go forth, O God, with our armies? <verse eid="PSA 60:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 60:11"/>Give to us help against the enemy—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:11">for empty <char style="add">is</char> the help of man! <verse eid="PSA 60:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 60:12"/>In God we will perform <char style="add">with</char> strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 60:12">and He will trample our adversaries. <verse eid="PSA 60:12"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 60"/>

<chapter number="61" style="c" sid="PSA 61"/>

<para style="s">You Have Heard My Vows</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. On a stringed instrument. Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 61:1"/> Hear, O God, my cry; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 61:1">attend to my prayer. <verse eid="PSA 61:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 61:2"/>From the end of the earth I call out to You </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 61:2">in the feebleness of my heart; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 61:2">may You lead me to the rock </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 61:2">that is higher than I. <verse eid="PSA 61:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 61:3"/>For You have been a place of refuge for me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 61:3">a tower of strength against the face of the enemy. <verse eid="PSA 61:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 61:4"/>Let me sojourn in Your Tent forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 61:4">I will take refuge in the shelter of Your wings. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 61:4">Selah <verse eid="PSA 61:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 61:5"/>for You, O God, have listend to my vows; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 61:5">You have appointed the inheritance </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 61:5">of those fearing Your name. <verse eid="PSA 61:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 61:6"/>May You add days to the days of the king; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 61:6"><char style="add">may</char> his years <char style="add">be</char> as generation and generation. <verse eid="PSA 61:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 61:7"/>May he dwell forever before God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 61:7">may You appoint loving devotion and faithfulness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 61:7">to guard him. <verse eid="PSA 61:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 61:8"/>So I will sing praise to your name forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 61:8">that I may perform my vows, day <char style="add">by</char> day. <verse eid="PSA 61:8"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 61"/>

<chapter number="62" style="c" sid="PSA 62"/>

<para style="s">Waiting on God</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. According to Jeduthun. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 62:1"/> Only toward God <char style="add">is</char> my soul silent; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:1">from Him <char style="add">is</char> my salvation. <verse eid="PSA 62:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 62:2"/>Only He <char style="add">is</char> my Rock and my salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:2">My tower; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:2">not much will I be shaken. <verse eid="PSA 62:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 62:3"/>Until when will you⁺ plot against a man? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:3">You⁺ are destroyed, all of you⁺, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 62:3">like a wall leaning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:3">a fence being pushed down. <verse eid="PSA 62:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 62:4"/>Surely from his high position they take counsel to thrust <char style="add">him</char> down; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:4">they delight in lies—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 62:4">with their mouth they bless, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:4">and within them they curse. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 62:4">Selah <verse eid="PSA 62:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 62:5"/>Only for God be silent, O my soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:5">for from Him <char style="add">is</char> my hope. <verse eid="PSA 62:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 62:6"/>Only He <char style="add">is</char> my Rock and my salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:6">my secure height; I will not be shaken. <verse eid="PSA 62:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 62:7"/>In God <char style="add">is</char> my salvation and my glory, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:7">the Rock of my strength; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:7">my refuge <char style="add">is</char> in God. <verse eid="PSA 62:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 62:8"/>Trust in Him at all times, O people; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:8">pour out your⁺ heart before Him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:8">God <char style="add">is</char> <char style="add">is</char> a refuge for us. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 62:8">Selah <verse eid="PSA 62:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 62:9"/>Only a vapor <char style="add">are</char> the sons of a man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:9">a lie the sons of a man—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 62:9">in the scales they go up </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:9">as a vapor together. <verse eid="PSA 62:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 62:10"/>You should⁺ not trust in oppression, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:10">and do not be vain in robbery; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 62:10"><char style="add">on</char> wealth when it increases </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:10">you⁺ should not set the heart. <verse eid="PSA 62:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 62:11"/>Once God has spoken; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:11">twice I have heard this, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 62:11">that strength <char style="add">is</char> unto God, <verse eid="PSA 62:11"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 62:12"/>and unto You, O Lord, <char style="add">is</char> loving devotion. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 62:12">For You do recompense to each man </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 62:12">according to his work. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">62.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 2:6</char></note><verse eid="PSA 62:12"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 62"/>

<chapter number="63" style="c" sid="PSA 63"/>

<para style="s">Thirsting for God</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of David, in his being in the wilderness of Judah.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 63:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Samuel 15:30–37</char></note> O God, You <char style="add">are</char> my God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:1">I seek after You—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:1">my soul thirsts for You, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 63:1">my flesh longs for You—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:1">in a land dry and weary, without waters. <verse eid="PSA 63:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 63:2"/>So in the sanctuary I have seen You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:2">to behold Your power and Your glory. <verse eid="PSA 63:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 63:3"/>Because Your loving devotion <char style="add">is</char> better than life, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:3">my lips will praise You. <verse eid="PSA 63:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 63:4"/>So I will bless You in my life; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:4">in Your name I will lift up my hands. <verse eid="PSA 63:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 63:5"/>As <char style="add">with</char> milk and fatness, my soul is satisfied, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:5">and with lips of joyful shouts, my mouth will praise You, <verse eid="PSA 63:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 63:6"/>when I remember You on my bed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:6">through the watches of the night I meditate on You. <verse eid="PSA 63:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 63:7"/>For You have been a help to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:7">and in the shadow of Your wings I will shout for joy. <verse eid="PSA 63:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 63:8"/>My soul clings to You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:8">Your right hand has taken hold of me. <verse eid="PSA 63:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 63:9"/>And those <char style="add">who</char> seek my soul for desolation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:9">they will go into the depths of the earth. <verse eid="PSA 63:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 63:10"/>They will fall by the hand of the sword; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:10">they will become a portion for foxes. <verse eid="PSA 63:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 63:11"/>And the king will rejoice in God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:11">everyone swearing by Him will exult, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 63:11">but the mouth of those speaking lies will be stopped up. <verse eid="PSA 63:11"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 63"/>

<chapter number="64" style="c" sid="PSA 64"/>

<para style="s">The Hurtful Tongue</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 64:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">James 3:1–12</char></note> Hear, O God, my voice in my complaint; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:1">from the dread of the enemy, may You preserve my life. <verse eid="PSA 64:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 64:2"/>Hide me from the counsel of the wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:2">from the mob of workers of iniquity, <verse eid="PSA 64:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 64:3"/>who sharpen their tongue like a sword, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:3">and aim a bitter word <char style="add">as</char> their arrow, <verse eid="PSA 64:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 64:4"/>to shoot in secret <char style="add">at</char> the blameless; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:4">suddenly they shoot at him, and do not fear. <verse eid="PSA 64:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 64:5"/>They strengthen themselves <char style="add">in</char> a word of evil; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:5">they recount the hiding of snares—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:5">they say, “Who is looking at them?” <verse eid="PSA 64:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 64:6"/>They search out injustice: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:6">“We have perfected a searching plot.” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:6">And the inner man and the heart <char style="add">is</char> deep! <verse eid="PSA 64:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 64:7"/>And God will shoot at them an arrow—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:7">suddenly they will be wounded. <verse eid="PSA 64:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 64:8"/>They will be made to stumble, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:8">their own tongue <char style="add">being</char> against them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:8">all those looking on them will flee. <verse eid="PSA 64:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 64:9"/>And all mankind will fear, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:9">and they will declare the work of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:9">and His deed they will wisely consider. <verse eid="PSA 64:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 64:10"/>A righteous one will be glad in YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:10">and he will take refuge in Him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 64:10">and let all the upright in heart exult! <verse eid="PSA 64:10"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 64"/>

<chapter number="65" style="c" sid="PSA 65"/>

<para style="s">Praise Awaits God in Zion</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Psalm of David. A Song.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 65:1"/> To You praise <char style="add">is</char> waiting, O God, in Zion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:1">and to You the vow will be fulfilled. <verse eid="PSA 65:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 65:2"/>O Hearer of prayer, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:2">to You all flesh will come. <verse eid="PSA 65:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 65:3"/>Matters of iniquities prevail against me—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:3">our transgressions, You wipe them away! <verse eid="PSA 65:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 65:4"/>Blessed <char style="add">is the one</char> You choose </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:4">and bring near, <char style="add">that</char> he may dwell in Your courts; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 65:4">we will be satisfied with the goodness of Your house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:4">the holiness of Your temple. <verse eid="PSA 65:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 65:5"/><char style="add">With</char> fearsome <char style="add">things</char>, may You answer us in righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:5">O God of our salvation, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 65:5">the confidence <char style="add">for</char> all the farthest ends </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:5">of the earth and the sea, <verse eid="PSA 65:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 65:6"/>the One establishing the mountains by His strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:6">being girded with might, <verse eid="PSA 65:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 65:7"/>stilling the roaring of the seas, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:7">the roar of their waves, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:7">and the uproar of the peoples. <verse eid="PSA 65:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 65:8"/>And those dwelling <char style="add">at</char> the ends were afraid of Your signs; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:8">the goings forth of morning and evening You cause to sing.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">65.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">where morning dawns and evening fades You call forth songs of joy.</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 65:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 65:9"/>You attend to the earth and give it abundance;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">65.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and make it overflow</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:9">greatly You enrich it; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 65:9">the stream of God is full of water; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:9">You provide their grain when thus You prepare it<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">65.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">You prepare our grain by providing for it</char></note>— <verse eid="PSA 65:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 65:10"/>soaking its furrows, descending <char style="add">on</char> its ridges; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:10">with showers You soften it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:10">its springing up You bless. <verse eid="PSA 65:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 65:11"/>You crown the year <char style="add">with</char> Your goodness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:11">and Your tracks drip <char style="add">with</char> fatness. <verse eid="PSA 65:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 65:12"/>They drip <char style="add">on</char> the pastures of the wilderness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:12">and the hills are surrounded <char style="add">with</char> joy. <verse eid="PSA 65:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 65:13"/>The meadows are clothed <char style="add">with</char> the flock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:13">and the valleys are feeble with grain—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 65:13">they shout <char style="add">for joy</char> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 65:13"><char style="add">and</char> even sing. <verse eid="PSA 65:13"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 65"/>

<chapter number="66" style="c" sid="PSA 66"/>

<para style="s">Make a Joyful Noise</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Song. A Psalm.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 66:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 100:1–5</char></note> Shout to God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:1">all the earth! <verse eid="PSA 66:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 66:2"/>Sing forth the glory of His name; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:2">make glorious His praise! <verse eid="PSA 66:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 66:3"/>Say to God, “How awesome <char style="add">are</char> Your works! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:3">In the abundance of Your might, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:3">Your enemies feign obedience to You. <verse eid="PSA 66:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 66:4"/>All the earth will bow down to You </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:4">and will sing to You—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:4">they will sing praises <char style="add">to</char> Your name.” </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 66:4">Selah <verse eid="PSA 66:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 66:5"/>Come and see the works of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:5">being fearsome <char style="add">in</char> His dealing with the sons of man. <verse eid="PSA 66:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 66:6"/>He turned the sea to dry land; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:6">through the river they passed over on foot. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:6">There we rejoiced in Him, <verse eid="PSA 66:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 66:7"/>ruling in His might forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:7">His eyes keep watch on the nations; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:7">let those rebelling not lift themselves high. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 66:7">Selah <verse eid="PSA 66:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 66:8"/>bless our God, O peoples, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:8">and make heard the voice of His praise— <verse eid="PSA 66:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 66:9"/>the One putting our soul among the living </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:9">and not having given our feet to slip. <verse eid="PSA 66:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 66:10"/>For You have tested us, O God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:10">You have refined us like the refining of silver. <verse eid="PSA 66:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 66:11"/>You have brought us into a net; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:11">You have placed pressure on our backs. <verse eid="PSA 66:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 66:12"/>You have caused man to ride over our heads; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:12">we came into the fire and into the water, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:12">and You brought us forth to a watered place. <verse eid="PSA 66:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 66:13"/>I will come into your house with burnt offerings; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:13">I will fulfill to You my vows, <verse eid="PSA 66:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 66:14"/>for which my lips have opened, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:14">and my mouth has spoken in the distress for me. <verse eid="PSA 66:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 66:15"/>Burnt offerings of fatlings I will offer to You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:15">with the fragrant smoke of rams; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:15">I will offer of bulls with goats. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 66:15">Selah <verse eid="PSA 66:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 66:16"/>Come, listen, all who fear God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:16">and I will recount what He has done for my soul. <verse eid="PSA 66:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 66:17"/>With my mouth I called out to Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:17">and He was praised under my tongue.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">66.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and His praise was on my tongue</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 66:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 66:18"/>If I had seen iniquity in my heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:18">the Lord would not have listened. <verse eid="PSA 66:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 66:19"/>Surely God has heard; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:19">He has attended to the voice of my prayer. <verse eid="PSA 66:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 66:20"/>Blessed <char style="add">be</char> God, who has not turned aside my prayer, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 66:20">or His loving devotion from me. <verse eid="PSA 66:20"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 66"/>

<chapter number="67" style="c" sid="PSA 67"/>

<para style="s">May God Cause His Face to Shine upon Us</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. On stringed instruments. A Psalm. A Song.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 67:1"/> May God be gracious to us and bless us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 67:1"><char style="add">and</char> cause His face to shine upon us, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 67:1">Selah <verse eid="PSA 67:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 67:2"/>for the knowing of Your way on the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 67:2">Your salvation among all nations. <verse eid="PSA 67:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 67:3"/>May the peoples praise You, O God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 67:3">may the peoples praise You—all of them. <verse eid="PSA 67:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 67:4"/>May the nations be glad and sing for joy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 67:4">for you will judge the peoples with uprightness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 67:4">and You will guide the nations on the earth. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 67:4">Selah <verse eid="PSA 67:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 67:5"/>let the peoples praise You, O God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 67:5">let the peoples praise You—all of them. <verse eid="PSA 67:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 67:6"/>The earth has given her produce; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 67:6">God, our God, blesses us! <verse eid="PSA 67:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 67:7"/>God blesses us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 67:7">and all the ends of the earth shall fear Him. <verse eid="PSA 67:7"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 67"/>

<chapter number="68" style="c" sid="PSA 68"/>

<para style="s">God’s Enemies Are Scattered</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. Of David. A Psalm. A Song.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 68:1"/> Arises, His enemies are scattered, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:1">and those hating Him flee before His face. <verse eid="PSA 68:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 68:2"/>As smoke is driven away, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:2">you will drive <char style="add">them</char> away; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 68:2">like the melting of wax from the face of the fire, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:2">the wicked will perish before the face of God. <verse eid="PSA 68:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 68:3"/>And the righteous will be glad; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:3">they will exult before God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:3">and will rejoice exceedingly. <verse eid="PSA 68:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 68:4"/>Sing to God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:4">sing praises <char style="add">to</char> His name! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 68:4">Lift up to the One riding on the clouds—<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">68.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">rides through the deserts</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:4">YAH <char style="add">is</char> His name—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:4">and rejoice before His face! <verse eid="PSA 68:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 68:5"/>A father of the fatherless, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:5">and a defender of widows, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:5"><char style="add">is</char> God, in the habitation of His holiness. <verse eid="PSA 68:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 68:6"/>God causes the solitary to dwell in a home; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:6">He brings out the prisoners into prosperity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:6">but the rebellious ones have dwelt in a scorched land. <verse eid="PSA 68:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 68:7"/>O God, in Your going forth before the face of Your people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:7">in Your marching through the wilderness, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 68:7">Selah <verse eid="PSA 68:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 68:8"/>the earth shook; also the heavens poured down </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:8">before the face of God, the One of Sinai, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:8">before the face of God, the God of Israel. <verse eid="PSA 68:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 68:9"/>You showered rain of freewill offerings, O God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:9">when Your inheritance was weary, You restored it. <verse eid="PSA 68:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 68:10"/>Your community dwelt in it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:10">You provided for the poor from Your goodness, O God. <verse eid="PSA 68:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 68:11"/>The Lord gives speech, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:11"><char style="add">and</char> those bearing news were a great army: <verse eid="PSA 68:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 68:12"/>“The kings of the armies—they flee, they flee! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:12">And she who dwells <char style="add">in</char> the house divides the spoil! <verse eid="PSA 68:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 68:13"/>Though you⁺ lie down among the sheepfolds—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:13">the wings of the dove are covered with silver, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:13">and her pinions with yellow gold.” <verse eid="PSA 68:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 68:14"/>When Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">68.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char></note> scattered the kings in it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:14">it was as the snow on Zalmon. <verse eid="PSA 68:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 68:15"/>A mountain of God <char style="add">is</char> Mount Bashan; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:15">a mountain of peaks <char style="add">is</char> Mount Bashan! <verse eid="PSA 68:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 68:16"/>Why do you⁺ gaze in envy, O mountains of peaks? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:16">On the mountain <char style="add">where</char> God desires to dwell, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:16">YHWH indeed will dwell forever. <verse eid="PSA 68:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 68:17"/>The chariots of God <char style="add">are</char> myriads—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:17">thousands upon thousands! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 68:17">The Lord <char style="add">is</char> among them <char style="add">on</char> Sinai, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:17">in the sanctuary.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">68.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Lord has come from Sinai in His holiness</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 68:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 68:18"/>You have gone up to the height, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:18">You have led captive captivity; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 68:18">You have received gifts from man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:18">even <char style="add">from</char> the rebellious ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:18">that YAH God may dwell there. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">68.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Ephesians 4:8</char></note><verse eid="PSA 68:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 68:19"/>Blessed <char style="add">be</char> the Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:19"><char style="add">who</char> day <char style="add">by</char> day lifts us up—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:19">the God of our salvation! </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 68:19">Selah <verse eid="PSA 68:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 68:20"/>God <char style="add">is</char> unto us a God of salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:20">and from YHWH the Lord <char style="add">is</char> <char style="add">our</char> coming forth from death. <verse eid="PSA 68:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 68:21"/>Surely God will wound the head of His enemies, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:21">the hairy crown of the one walking in his guilt. <verse eid="PSA 68:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 68:22"/>The Lord said, “From Bashan I will bring <char style="add">them</char> back; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:22">I will bring <char style="add">them</char> back from the depths of the sea, <verse eid="PSA 68:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 68:23"/>so that <char style="add">you</char> may plunge your foot in the blood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:23"><char style="add">and</char> the tongue of your dogs have its portion from <char style="add">your</char> enemies!” <verse eid="PSA 68:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 68:24"/>They have seen Your going about, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:24">the going about of my God <char style="add">and</char> my King, in the sanctuary. <verse eid="PSA 68:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 68:25"/>Those singing go in front, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:25"><char style="add">and</char> behind <char style="add">are those</char> playing strings, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:25"><char style="add">and</char> in the midst <char style="add">are</char> virgins playing timbrels. <verse eid="PSA 68:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 68:26"/>In the assemblies bless God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:26">YHWH, from the fountain of Israel. <verse eid="PSA 68:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 68:27"/>There <char style="add">is</char> little Benjamin leading them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:27"><char style="add">with</char> the princes of Judah <char style="add">in</char> their company, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:27">the princes of Zebulun, the princes of Naphtali. <verse eid="PSA 68:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 68:28"/>Summon, O God, your strength!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">68.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX and Syriac; most Hebrew manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Your God has summoned your strength</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:28">Make strong, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:28">this which You have done for us. <verse eid="PSA 68:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 68:29"/>Your temple <char style="add">is</char> upon Jerusalem—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:29">the kings shall bring a gift to You. <verse eid="PSA 68:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 68:30"/>Rebuke the creature of the reed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:30">the herd of bulls with the calves of the nations—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 68:30">trample underfoot the desire for silver, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:30">scatter the nations delighting in war! <verse eid="PSA 68:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 68:31"/>Envoys will come from Egypt; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:31">Cush<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">68.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the upper Nile region</char></note> will make its hands run to God. <verse eid="PSA 68:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 68:32"/>O kingdoms of the earth, sing to God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:32">sing praises to the Lord—</para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 68:32">Selah <verse eid="PSA 68:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 68:33"/>to the one riding on the heavens, the heavens of old! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:33">Behold, He gives forth with His voice, a voice of power. <verse eid="PSA 68:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 68:34"/>Ascribe strength to God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:34"><char style="add">for</char> His majesty <char style="add">is</char> over Israel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:34">and His power in the clouds. <verse eid="PSA 68:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 68:35"/><char style="add">You are</char> fearsome, O God, in Your sanctuary; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:35">the God of Israel—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 68:35">He <char style="add">is</char> giving power and strength to the people. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 68:35">Blessed be God! <verse eid="PSA 68:35"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 68"/>

<chapter number="69" style="c" sid="PSA 69"/>

<para style="s">The Waters Are up to My Neck</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. According to “The Lilies.” Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 69:1"/> Save me, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:1">for the waters have come up to the soul. <verse eid="PSA 69:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 69:2"/>I sink in the mire of the deep, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:2">and there is no place to stand; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 69:2">I have come into the depths of the waters, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:2">and a flood washes over me. <verse eid="PSA 69:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 69:3"/>I have grown weary with my calling out; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:3">my throat is dry; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 69:3">my eyes fail, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:3">waiting for my God. <verse eid="PSA 69:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 69:4"/>Those hating me without cause </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:4">outnumber the hairs of my head; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 69:4">many are those seeking my destruction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:4">my enemies <char style="add">with</char> deception! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 69:4">That which I did not steal, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:4">I must then return. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">69.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See John 15:25</char></note><verse eid="PSA 69:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 69:5"/>O God, You know of my foolishness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:5">and my guilt <char style="add">is</char> not hidden from You. <verse eid="PSA 69:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 69:6"/>Do not let those waiting on You come to shame because of me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:6">O Lord YHWH of hosts; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 69:6">do not let those seeking You be disgraced because of me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:6">O God of Israel! <verse eid="PSA 69:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 69:7"/><char style="add">It is</char> for Your sake that I have carried scorn, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:7"><char style="add">and</char> shame has covered my face. <verse eid="PSA 69:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 69:8"/>I have become a stranger to my brothers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:8">and a foreigner to the sons of my mother. <verse eid="PSA 69:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 69:9"/>For zeal for Your house has consumed me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:9">and the insults of those insulting You have fallen on me.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">69.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in John 2:17</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">69.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 15:3</char></note><verse eid="PSA 69:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 69:10"/>I even wept in the fasting of my soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:10">and it was for a reproach to me. <verse eid="PSA 69:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 69:11"/>I made my clothing sackcloth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:11">and I became to them as a byword. <verse eid="PSA 69:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 69:12"/>Those sitting <char style="add">at</char> the gate meditate against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:12">and I am the song of those drinking wine. <verse eid="PSA 69:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 69:13"/>And I—my prayer <char style="add">is</char> to You, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:13"><char style="add">in</char> the time of favor, O God, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 69:13">in the abundance of Your loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:13">may You answer me in the truth of Your salvation! <verse eid="PSA 69:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 69:14"/>Deliver me from the mire, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:14">that I should not sink! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 69:14">May I be delivered from those hating me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:14">and out of the depths of the waters. <verse eid="PSA 69:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 69:15"/>Do not let the flood of waters engulf me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:15">and do not let the deep swallow me up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:15">and do not let the pit shut its mouth over me! <verse eid="PSA 69:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 69:16"/>Answer me, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:16">for good <char style="add">is</char> Your loving devotion; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:16">according to the abundance of Your tender mercies, turn to me. <verse eid="PSA 69:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 69:17"/>And do not hide Your face from Your servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:17">for distress <char style="add">is</char> unto me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:17">hurry to answer me! <verse eid="PSA 69:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 69:18"/>Draw near to my soul <char style="add">and</char> redeem it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:18">on account of my enemies, may You ransom me. <verse eid="PSA 69:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 69:19"/>You know my scorn, and my shame, and my disgrace; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:19">all my adversaries <char style="add">are</char> before You. <verse eid="PSA 69:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 69:20"/>Reproach has broken my heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:20">and I am sick. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 69:20">And I looked for a bemoaner, and there was none, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:20">and for comforters, and I found none. <verse eid="PSA 69:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 69:21"/>And they gave gall for my food, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:21">and for my thirst they made me drink vinegar. <verse eid="PSA 69:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 69:22"/>May their table before them become a snare, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:22">and for a recompense—for a trap! <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">69.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> A slight revocalization of the Hebrew (see also LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate); literally </char><char style="fq" closed="false">may their prosperity be a trap</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Romans 11:9</char></note><verse eid="PSA 69:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 69:23"/>May their eyes grow dark from seeing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:23">and their backs be bent forever!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">69.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and may their loins tremble continually</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Romans 11:10</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 69:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 69:24"/>Pour out upon them Your indignation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:24">and may the burning of Your anger overtake them! <verse eid="PSA 69:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 69:25"/>May their encampment become desolate; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:25">may there be no one dwelling in their tents. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">69.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Acts 1:20</char></note><verse eid="PSA 69:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 69:26"/>For You—the one whom You struck—they pursue, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:26">and the pain of those You pierced they recount. <verse eid="PSA 69:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 69:27"/>May You add iniquity to their iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:27">and do not let them come into Your righteousness! <verse eid="PSA 69:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 69:28"/>May they be blotted out from the book of the living, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:28">and do not let them be written with the righteous! <verse eid="PSA 69:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 69:29"/>And I <char style="add">am</char> afflicted and pained; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:29">may Your salvation, O God, set me on high. <verse eid="PSA 69:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 69:30"/>I will praise the name of God with a song, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:30">and will I magnify Him with thanksgiving. <verse eid="PSA 69:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 69:31"/>And it is better to YHWH than an ox, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:31">a bull horned <char style="add">and</char> hoofed. <verse eid="PSA 69:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 69:32"/>The humble have seen—they rejoice—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:32">you seeking God, your⁺ heart shall live! <verse eid="PSA 69:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 69:33"/>For YHWH listens to the needy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:33">and he has not despised His captives. <verse eid="PSA 69:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 69:34"/>Let the heavens and earth shout praise to Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:34">the seas, and every moving thing in them. <verse eid="PSA 69:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 69:35"/>For God will save Zion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:35">and He will rebuild the cities of Judah, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:35">that they may dwell there and possess it. <verse eid="PSA 69:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 69:36"/>And the seed of His servants will inherit it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 69:36">and those loving His name will settle in it. <verse eid="PSA 69:36"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 69"/>

<chapter number="70" style="c" sid="PSA 70"/>

<para style="s">Hurry, O LORD, to Help Me!</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. Of David. For remembrance.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 70:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 141:1–10</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 40:1–17</char></note> O God, deliver me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 70:1">O YHWH, may You hurry—to help me! <verse eid="PSA 70:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 70:2"/>Let them be ashamed and confounded, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 70:2">those seeking my soul; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 70:2">let them be turned back and be disgraced, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 70:2">those taking delight <char style="add">in</char> my harm! <verse eid="PSA 70:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 70:3"/>Let them be turned back over the heel of their shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 70:3">those saying, “Aha, aha!” <verse eid="PSA 70:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 70:4"/>Let all those seeking You rejoice </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 70:4">and be glad in You; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 70:4">those loving Your salvation, let them say continually </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 70:4">“May God be magnified!” <verse eid="PSA 70:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 70:5"/>And I <char style="add">am</char> lowly and needy; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 70:5">O God, hurry to me! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 70:5">You <char style="add">are</char> my help and my deliverer, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 70:5">O YHWH—do not delay! <verse eid="PSA 70:5"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 70"/>

<chapter number="71" style="c" sid="PSA 71"/>

<para style="s">Be My Rock of Refuge</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 71:1"/>In You, O YHWH, I take refuge; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:1">let me not be put to shame forever! <verse eid="PSA 71:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 71:2"/>In Your righteousness, deliver me and cause me to escape; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:2">incline to me Your ear, and save me! <verse eid="PSA 71:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 71:3"/>May You be to me as a rock, a habitation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:3">to go in continually; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 71:3">You have given a command to save me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:3">for You <char style="add">are</char> my rock and my fortress. <verse eid="PSA 71:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 71:4"/>O My God, rescue me from the hand of a wicked one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:4">from the palm of the one acting unjustly and pressing. <verse eid="PSA 71:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 71:5"/>For You <char style="add">are</char> my hope, O Lord YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:5">my trust from my youth. <verse eid="PSA 71:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 71:6"/>By You I have been supported from the womb; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:6">from the bowels of my mother You cut me out. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:6">My praise <char style="add">is</char> continually for You. <verse eid="PSA 71:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 71:7"/>I have been as a wonder to many, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:7">and You <char style="add">are</char> my strong refuge. <verse eid="PSA 71:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 71:8"/>My mouth is filled <char style="add">with</char> Your praise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:8"><char style="add">with</char> Your splendor all the day. <verse eid="PSA 71:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 71:9"/>Do not cast me off in the time of old age; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:9">according to the consumption of my strength do not forsake me. <verse eid="PSA 71:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 71:10"/>For my enemies speak against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:10">and those watching my soul take counsel together, <verse eid="PSA 71:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 71:11"/>saying, “God has forsaken him. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:11">Pursue him and seize him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:11">for <char style="add">there is</char> none to deliver <char style="add">him</char>!” <verse eid="PSA 71:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 71:12"/>O God, do not be far from me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:12">O my God, hurry to <char style="add">be</char> my help! <verse eid="PSA 71:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 71:13"/>Let them be put to shame <char style="add">and</char> consumed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:13">those opposing my soul; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 71:13">let them be covered <char style="add">with</char> scorn and disgrace, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:13">those seeking my harm! <verse eid="PSA 71:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 71:14"/>But I continually will hope, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:14">and I will add upon all Your praise. <verse eid="PSA 71:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 71:15"/>My mouth will recount Your righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:15">all the day Your salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:15">though I do not know the numbers. <verse eid="PSA 71:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 71:16"/>I will come in the might of the Lord YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:16">I will cause Your righteousness to be remembered—Yours alone. <verse eid="PSA 71:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 71:17"/>O God, You have taught me from my youth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:17">and until now I declare Your wonders. <verse eid="PSA 71:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 71:18"/>Indeed, when <char style="add">I am</char> old and grayheaded, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:18">O God, do not forsake me, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 71:18">until I declare Your arm to a generation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:18">Your strength to everyone to come. <verse eid="PSA 71:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 71:19"/>And Your righteousness, O God, <char style="add">is</char> to the height! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:19"><char style="add">You</char> who have done great things, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:19">O God—who <char style="add">is</char> like You? <verse eid="PSA 71:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 71:20"/>Though You have made me see many troubles and distresses, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:20">You will return <char style="add">and</char> revive us; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 71:20">even from the depths of the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:20">You will return <char style="add">and</char> bring me up. <verse eid="PSA 71:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 71:21"/>You will increase my honor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:21">and surrounding <char style="add">me</char>, You will comfort me. <verse eid="PSA 71:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 71:22"/>I will also praise You with the harp </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:22"><char style="add">for</char> Your faithfulness, O my God; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 71:22">I will make music to You with the lyre, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:22">O Holy One of Israel! <verse eid="PSA 71:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 71:23"/>My lips will shout for joy </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:23">when when I sing praises to You, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 71:23">even my soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:23">which You have redeemed. <verse eid="PSA 71:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 71:24"/>My tongue will also utter </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:24">Your righteousness all the day, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 71:24">for they have been put to shame, for </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 71:24">they are humiliated—those seeking my harm. <verse eid="PSA 71:24"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 71"/>

<chapter number="72" style="c" sid="PSA 72"/>

<para style="s">Endow the King with Your Justice</para>

<para style="s">Of Solomon.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 72:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 45:1–17</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Chronicles 1:1–13</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Kings 3:1–15</char></note> O God, give Your judgments to the king, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:1">and Your justice to the son of the king. <verse eid="PSA 72:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 72:2"/>May he judge Your people with righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:2">and Your lowly ones with judgment. <verse eid="PSA 72:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 72:3"/>The mountains will carry peace to the people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:3">and the hills justice. <verse eid="PSA 72:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 72:4"/>He will judge for the lowly ones of the people; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:4">he will save the sons of the needy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:4">and will crush the one oppressing. <verse eid="PSA 72:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 72:5"/>They will fear You<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">72.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He shall endure</char></note> with the sun, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:5">and before the face of the moon, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:5"><char style="add">from</char> generation <char style="add">to</char> generations. <verse eid="PSA 72:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 72:6"/>He will come down like rain upon freshly cut grass, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:6">like showers dropping <char style="add">on</char> the earth. <verse eid="PSA 72:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 72:7"/>In his days the righteous will sprout forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:7">and <char style="add">an</char> abundance of peace, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:7">until the moon <char style="add">is</char> no more. <verse eid="PSA 72:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 72:8"/>And he will rule from sea to sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:8">and from the River<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">72.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Euphrates</char></note> to the ends of the earth. <verse eid="PSA 72:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 72:9"/>Before him the desert dwellers will bow down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:9">and his enemies will lick the dust. <verse eid="PSA 72:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 72:10"/>The kings of Tarshish and the isles will return a gift; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:10">the kings of Sheba and Seba will bring near a gift. <verse eid="PSA 72:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 72:11"/>And all kings will bow low before him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:11">all nations will serve him! <verse eid="PSA 72:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 72:12"/>For he will deliver the needy one crying out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:12">and the poor one without a helper to him. <verse eid="PSA 72:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 72:13"/>He will have pity on the poor and needy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:13">and he will save the souls of the needy. <verse eid="PSA 72:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 72:14"/>From oppression and from violence he will redeem their soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:14">and their blood will be precious in his eyes. <verse eid="PSA 72:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 72:15"/>Long may he live, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:15">and it shall be given to him from the gold of Sheba; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 72:15">and prayer shall be made for him continually; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:15">all the day he shall be blessed. <verse eid="PSA 72:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 72:16"/>There shall be an abundance of grain in the land; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:16">on the top of the mountains it shall wave, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 72:16">its fruit like Lebanon; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:16">and the <char style="add">people</char> of the city shall flourish like the grass of the earth. <verse eid="PSA 72:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 72:17"/>His name shall be forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:17">unto the turning of the sun his name shall increase;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">72.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">continue</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 72:17">and all nations shall be blessed in him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:17">they shall call him blessed. <verse eid="PSA 72:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 72:18"/>Blessed <char style="add">be</char> YHWH God, the God of Israel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:18">the One doing marvelous deeds—Him alone! <verse eid="PSA 72:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 72:19"/>And blessed <char style="add">be</char> the name of His glory forever;. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 72:19">And let all the earth be filled <char style="add">with</char> His glory! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 72:19">Amen and Amen. <verse eid="PSA 72:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 72:20"/>The prayers of David son of Jesse have come to an end. <verse eid="PSA 72:20"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 72"/>

<chapter number="73" style="c" sid="PSA 73"/>

<para style="s">BOOK III</para>

<para style="s">Psalms 73–89</para>

<para style="s">Surely God Is Good to Israel</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of Asaph.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 73:1"/> Surely God <char style="add">is</char> good to Israel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:1">to those pure of heart. <verse eid="PSA 73:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 73:2"/>And <char style="add">as for</char> me, at a little stretching out of my feet, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:2">my steps had nearly poured out. <verse eid="PSA 73:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 73:3"/>For I was envious of those boasting </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:3"><char style="add">when</char> I saw the prosperity of the wicked. <verse eid="PSA 73:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 73:4"/>For there are no pangs until their death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:4">and their body <char style="add">is</char> fat. <verse eid="PSA 73:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 73:5"/>They <char style="add">are</char> not in the trouble of mankind, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:5">and with men they are not are they plagued. <verse eid="PSA 73:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 73:6"/>Therefore pride is their necklace; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:6">a garment of violence is a covering for them. <verse eid="PSA 73:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 73:7"/>Their eye has bulged out from fat,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">73.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">From their prosperity proceeds iniquity</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; Syriac </char><char style="fq" closed="false">From their callous heart proceeds iniquity</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:7">the imaginations of their heart overflow. <verse eid="PSA 73:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 73:8"/>They scoff and speak with malice; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:8">from a high place they speak oppression. <verse eid="PSA 73:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 73:9"/>They have set their mouth in the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:9">and their tongue walks through the earth. <verse eid="PSA 73:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 73:10"/>Therefore his people turn here, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:10">and waters of fullness are wrung out for them. <verse eid="PSA 73:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 73:11"/>And they say, “How can God know? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:11">And is there knowledge in the Most High?” <verse eid="PSA 73:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 73:12"/>Behold, these <char style="add">are</char> the wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:12">and at ease always, they have increased in wealth. <verse eid="PSA 73:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 73:13"/>Surely <char style="add">in</char> vain I have cleansed my heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:13">and I have washed my hands in innocence. <verse eid="PSA 73:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 73:14"/>For I have been stricken all the day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:14">and chastened in the morning. <verse eid="PSA 73:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 73:15"/>If I had said, “I will speak like this,” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:15">behold, I would have betrayed the generation of Your sons. <verse eid="PSA 73:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 73:16"/>And I thought to know this—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:16">it <char style="add">was</char> toil in my eyes— <verse eid="PSA 73:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 73:17"/>until I came to the sanctuary of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:17"><char style="add">and</char> discerned their end. <verse eid="PSA 73:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 73:18"/>Surely You set them on slick ground; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:18">You make them fall to destruction. <verse eid="PSA 73:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 73:19"/>How they have become a desolation in a moment! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:19">They are swept away completely by terrors. <verse eid="PSA 73:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 73:20"/>As a dream from awakening, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:20">O Lord, in rousing Yourself, You shall despise their image. <verse eid="PSA 73:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 73:21"/>For my heart had grown sour, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:21">and my kidneys pierce themselves. <verse eid="PSA 73:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 73:22"/>And I <char style="add">was</char> brutish and could not know; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:22">I was a beast before You. <verse eid="PSA 73:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 73:23"/>And I <char style="add">am</char> always with You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:23">You hold my right hand. <verse eid="PSA 73:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 73:24"/>May You lead me with Your counsel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:24">and afterward You will receive me <char style="add">in</char> glory! <verse eid="PSA 73:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 73:25"/>Who <char style="add">is</char> unto me in the heavens? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:25">And besides You I do not take delight on the earth. <verse eid="PSA 73:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 73:26"/>My flesh and my heart may be consumed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:26">the rock<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">73.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">strength</char></note> of my heart and my portion </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:26"><char style="add">is</char> God to the age. <verse eid="PSA 73:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 73:27"/>For behold, those far from You will perish. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:27">You destroy everyone prostituting himself from You! <verse eid="PSA 73:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 73:28"/>But I—the nearness of God <char style="add">is</char> good for me—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:28">I have placed my refuge in the Lord YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 73:28">to recount all Your works. <verse eid="PSA 73:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 73"/>

<chapter number="74" style="c" sid="PSA 74"/>

<para style="s">Why Have You Rejected Us Forever?</para>

<para style="s">A Maskil† of Asaph.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 74:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Jeremiah 52:1–11</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 79:1–13</char></note> Why, O God, have You rejected us forever? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:1">Your anger smolders </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:1">against the flock of Your pasture. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">74.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Maskil</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 74:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 74:2"/>Remember Your congregation </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:2">You acquired of old; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 74:2">You redeemed <char style="add">as</char> the staff of Your inheritance </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:2">this Mount Zion—in it You have dwelt! <verse eid="PSA 74:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 74:3"/>Lift up Your steps to the perpetual desolations—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:3">to everything done wickedly <char style="add">by</char> the enemy in the sanctuary! <verse eid="PSA 74:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 74:4"/>Your adversaries have roared within Your meeting place; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:4">they have set up their signs <char style="add">for</char> signs. <verse eid="PSA 74:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 74:5"/>He made himself known like one bringing on high axes against a thicket of tree; <verse eid="PSA 74:5"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 74:6"/>and now all its engravings they strike down with ax and hatchet. <verse eid="PSA 74:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 74:7"/>They have sent Your sanctuary into the fire, to the ground; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:7">they have desecrated the dwelling place of Your Name. <verse eid="PSA 74:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 74:8"/>They said in their hearts, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:8">“Let us oppress them altogether!” </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 74:8">They have burned all the meeting places </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:8">of God in the land. <verse eid="PSA 74:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 74:9"/>Signs for us we do not see; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:9">there is no longer a prophet, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:9">and there is no one among us knowing until when. <verse eid="PSA 74:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 74:10"/>Until when, O God, will the adversary reproach? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:10">Will the enemy revile Your name forever? <verse eid="PSA 74:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 74:11"/>Why do You turn back Your hand, and Your right hand? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:11">May You remove <char style="add">it</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">74.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">May You destroy them</char></note> from the midst of Your bosom! <verse eid="PSA 74:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 74:12"/>For God <char style="add">is</char> my King from of old, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:12">working salvation in the midst of the earth. <verse eid="PSA 74:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 74:13"/>You divided the sea by Your strength; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:13">You broke the heads of the dragons upon the waters. <verse eid="PSA 74:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 74:14"/>You crushed the heads of Leviathan; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:14">You gave him <char style="add">as</char> food to the people of the dry places. <verse eid="PSA 74:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 74:15"/>You burst open spring and stream; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:15">You dried up the enduring rivers. <verse eid="PSA 74:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 74:16"/>To You <char style="add">is</char> the day, also to You <char style="add">is</char> the night; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:16">You established the light<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">74.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the moon</char></note> and the sun. <verse eid="PSA 74:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 74:17"/>You set all the boundaries of the earth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:17">summer and winter, You have formed them. <verse eid="PSA 74:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 74:18"/>Remember this, an enemy has reproached YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:18">and a foolish people have spurned Your name! <verse eid="PSA 74:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 74:19"/>Do not give to the wild beast the soul of Your dove; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:19">do not forget the life of Your afflicted ones forever! <verse eid="PSA 74:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 74:20"/>Look to the covenant! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:20">For the dark places of the earth are filled <char style="add">as</char> habitations of violence. <verse eid="PSA 74:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 74:21"/>Do not let the oppressed turn back, having been disgraced; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:21">let the afflicted and needy ones praise Your name. <verse eid="PSA 74:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 74:22"/>Arise, O God, defend Your cause! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:22">Remember the scorning of You from a fool all the day. <verse eid="PSA 74:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 74:23"/>Do not forget the voice of Your enemies, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 74:23">the uproar of those rising against You, going up continually. <verse eid="PSA 74:23"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 74"/>

<chapter number="75" style="c" sid="PSA 75"/>

<para style="s">God’s Righteous Judgment</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing: To “Do not Destroy.” A Psalm of Asaph. A Song.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 75:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Romans 2:1–16</char></note> We give thanks to You, O God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 75:1">we give thanks—for Your name is near—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 75:1">recounting Your wonders. <verse eid="PSA 75:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 75:2"/>“When I take the appointed place, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 75:2">I will judge uprightly. <verse eid="PSA 75:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 75:3"/>At the dissolving of the earth and all its dwellers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 75:3">I measure out its pillars. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 75:3">Selah <verse eid="PSA 75:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 75:4"/>I said to those boasting, ‘You⁺ shall not boast,’ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 75:4">and to the wicked, ‘You⁺ shall not lift up the horn; <verse eid="PSA 75:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 75:5"/>you⁺ shall not lift up your⁺ horn to the height, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 75:5"><char style="add">or</char> speak with an insolent neck.’” <verse eid="PSA 75:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 75:6"/>For <char style="add">it is</char> not from the going forth or from the sinking, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 75:6">and not from the wilderness <char style="add">is</char> exaltation, <verse eid="PSA 75:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 75:7"/>But God is judging—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 75:7">this one He brings low, and this one He lifts up. <verse eid="PSA 75:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 75:8"/>For a cup <char style="add">is</char> in the hand of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 75:8">and the wine is foaming, full of mixture, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 75:8">and He shall pour out from this—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 75:8">how its dregs shall be wrung out—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 75:8"><char style="add">and</char> all the wicked of the earth shall drink. <verse eid="PSA 75:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 75:9"/>And I will declare <char style="add">it</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">75.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">declare Him</char></note> forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 75:9">I will make music to the God of Jacob. <verse eid="PSA 75:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 75:10"/>“And all the horns of the wicked I will cut off; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 75:10">the horns of the righteous will be exalted.” <verse eid="PSA 75:10"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 75"/>

<chapter number="76" style="c" sid="PSA 76"/>

<para style="s">God’s name Is Great in Israel</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. On stringed instruments. A Psalm of Asaph. A Song.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 76:1"/> In Judah God is known, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 76:1">in Israel His name <char style="add">is</char> great. <verse eid="PSA 76:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 76:2"/>And His tent is in Salem,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">76.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Jerusalem</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 76:2">and his dwelling place in Zion. <verse eid="PSA 76:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 76:3"/>There he has shattered the arrows of the bow—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 76:3">the shield and sword and weapon of war. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 76:3">Selah <verse eid="PSA 76:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 76:4"/>luminous are You </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 76:4">and majestic, from the mountains of prey. <verse eid="PSA 76:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 76:5"/>They became plunder, the mighty of heart; they have slept their sleep, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 76:5">and the men of might could not find any of their hands. <verse eid="PSA 76:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 76:6"/>At Your rebuke, O God of Jacob, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 76:6">both the rider and horse are lain asleep. <verse eid="PSA 76:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 76:7"/>You are to be feared—You! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 76:7">And who can stand before Your face at the time of Your anger? <verse eid="PSA 76:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 76:8"/>From the heavens You have sounded the judgment; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 76:8">the earth has feared and has been still, <verse eid="PSA 76:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 76:9"/>at the rising of God to the judgment, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 76:9">to bring salvation <char style="add">to</char> all the lowly ones of the earth. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 76:9">Selah <verse eid="PSA 76:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 76:10"/>for the wrath of man shall praise You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 76:10">with the remainder of wrath You gird Yourself.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">76.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Surely Your wrath against men brings You praise, and the survivors of Your wrath will be restrained.</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 76:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 76:11"/>Make vows to YHWH your⁺ God, and fulfill <char style="add">them</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 76:11">let all around Him bring tribute </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 76:11">to the Fearsome One. <verse eid="PSA 76:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 76:12"/>He takes away the spirit of princes; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 76:12">He is feared by the kings of the earth. <verse eid="PSA 76:12"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 76"/>

<chapter number="77" style="c" sid="PSA 77"/>

<para style="s">In the Day of Trouble I Sought the Lord</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. According to Jeduthun. Of Asaph. A Psalm.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 77:1"/> My voice <char style="add">is</char> to God—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:1">indeed I cry out <char style="add">with</char> my voice to God—and He has given ear to me. <verse eid="PSA 77:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 77:2"/>In the day of my distress I sought the Lord; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:2">my hand in the night has been stretched out, and it does not slacken; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:2">my soul refuses to be comforted. <verse eid="PSA 77:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 77:3"/>I remember God, and I groan; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:3">I meditate, and my spirit becomes faint. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 77:3">Selah <verse eid="PSA 77:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 77:4"/>You hold the lids of my eyes; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:4">I am troubled, and I cannot speak. <verse eid="PSA 77:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 77:5"/>I consider the days of old, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:5">the years of ages <char style="add">past</char>. <verse eid="PSA 77:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 77:6"/>I remember, my song in the night; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:6">with my heart I converse, and my spirit searches. <verse eid="PSA 77:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 77:7"/>“Will the Lord forever reject <char style="add">us</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:7">and not anymore will He add to show favor? <verse eid="PSA 77:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 77:8"/>Has His loving devotion ceased forever? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:8">Has <char style="add">His</char> speech come to an end to generation and generation? <verse eid="PSA 77:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 77:9"/>Or has God forgotten to show favor? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:9">Has He shut up in anger His compassion?” </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 77:9">Selah <verse eid="PSA 77:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 77:10"/>and I said, “I am grieved. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:10">Has it changed—the right hand of the Most High?”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">77.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“To this I will appeal: to the years of the right hand of the Most High.”</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 77:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 77:11"/>I will remember the deeds of YAH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:11">indeed, I will remember Your wonder of old. <verse eid="PSA 77:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 77:12"/>And I have meditated on all Your work, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:12">and I put forth Your deeds. <verse eid="PSA 77:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 77:13"/>O God, in holiness <char style="add">is</char> Your way; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:13">what god <char style="add">is</char> great like God? <verse eid="PSA 77:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 77:14"/>You <char style="add">are</char> the God doing wonders; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:14">You have made known among the peoples Your strength. <verse eid="PSA 77:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 77:15"/>You have redeemed with <char style="add">Your</char> arm a people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:15">the sons of Jacob and Joseph. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 77:15">Selah <verse eid="PSA 77:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 77:16"/>the waters saw You, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:16">the waters saw You and swirled; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:16">even the depths trembled. <verse eid="PSA 77:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 77:17"/>The clouds poured forth waters, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:17">the skies gave forth a voice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:17">and Your arrows flashed back and forth. <verse eid="PSA 77:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 77:18"/>The voice of Your thunder <char style="add">was</char> in the whirlwind; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:18">the lightnings lit up the world; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:18">the earth trembled and shook. <verse eid="PSA 77:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 77:19"/>Your way <char style="add">was</char> in the sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:19">and Your paths in the great waters, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:19">and Your footprints were not known.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">77.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">were not to be found</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 77:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 77:20"/>You led Your people like a flock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 77:20">by the hand of Moses and Aaron. <verse eid="PSA 77:20"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 77"/>

<chapter number="78" style="c" sid="PSA 78"/>

<para style="s">I Will Open My Mouth in Parables</para>

<para style="s">A Maskil† of Asaph.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 78:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 13:34–35</char></note> Give ear, O my people, <char style="add">to</char> my instruction; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:1">stretch out your⁺ ear to the words of my mouth. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">78.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Maskil</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 78:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 78:2"/>I will open my mouth in a parable; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:2">I will pour forth things hidden from of old,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">78.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">riddles</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">78.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from the beginning</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see also LXX; cited in Matthew 13:35</char></note><verse eid="PSA 78:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 78:3"/>which we have heard and known, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:3">and our fathers have recounted to us. <verse eid="PSA 78:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 78:4"/>We will not hide <char style="add">them</char> from their children, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:4">recounting to a following generation: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 78:4">The praises of YHWH, and His strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:4">and His wonders that He has done. <verse eid="PSA 78:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 78:5"/>For He established a testimony in Jacob, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:5">and a law He has appointed in Israel, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 78:5">which He commanded <char style="add">to</char> our fathers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:5">to make them known to their sons, <verse eid="PSA 78:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 78:6"/>so that a following generation would know them—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:6">the sons to be born—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:6">to arise and recount to their sons, <verse eid="PSA 78:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 78:7"/>that they should put their hope in God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:7">and not forget the works of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:7">and keep His commandments. <verse eid="PSA 78:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 78:8"/>And they should not be like their fathers—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:8">a generation being stubborn and rebellious, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 78:8">a generation <char style="add">that</char> did not set firm its heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:8">and <char style="add">whose</char> spirit was not faithful to God. <verse eid="PSA 78:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 78:9"/>The sons of Ephraim, handling <char style="add">and</char> shooting the bow, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:9">turned back on the day of battle. <verse eid="PSA 78:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 78:10"/>They did not keep the covenant of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:10">and in His law they refused to walk, <verse eid="PSA 78:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 78:11"/>and they forgot His deeds, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:11">and His wonders that He had shown them. <verse eid="PSA 78:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 78:12"/>In the eyes of their fathers He did a wonder, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:12">in the land of Egypt, <char style="add">in</char> the field of Zoan. <verse eid="PSA 78:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 78:13"/>He divided the sea and let them cross over, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:13">and the waters He made stand up like a heap. <verse eid="PSA 78:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 78:14"/>And He led them with the cloud by day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:14">and all the night with a light of fire. <verse eid="PSA 78:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 78:15"/>He split open the rocks in the wilderness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:15">and gave to drink, like the depths <char style="add">in</char> abundance. <verse eid="PSA 78:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 78:16"/>And He brought forth streams from the rock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:16">and made waters come down like the rivers. <verse eid="PSA 78:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 78:17"/>And they added still to sin against Him </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:17">by rebelling against the Most High in the desert. <verse eid="PSA 78:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 78:18"/>And they tested God in their heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:18">by requesting food of their soul. <verse eid="PSA 78:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 78:19"/>And they spoke against God, saying, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:19">“Is God able to arrange a table in the wilderness? <verse eid="PSA 78:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 78:20"/>Behold, He struck the rock, and the waters gushed out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:20">and torrents overflowed; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 78:20">and also is He able to give bread </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:20">or provide food for His people?” <verse eid="PSA 78:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 78:21"/>Therefore YHWH heard </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:21">and boiled over, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 78:21">and a fire was kindled against Jacob, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:21">and anger came up against Israel, <verse eid="PSA 78:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 78:22"/>because they did not have faith in God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:22">and they did not trust in His salvation. <verse eid="PSA 78:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 78:23"/>And He commanded the clouds above, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:23">and the doors of the heavens He opened. <verse eid="PSA 78:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 78:24"/>And He rained down on them manna to eat—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:24">and he gave to them the grain of the heavens. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">78.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in John 6:31</char></note><verse eid="PSA 78:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 78:25"/>The bread of the mighty ones a man ate; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:25">food He sent to them in abundance. <verse eid="PSA 78:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 78:26"/>An east wind He caused to blow in the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:26">and He guided by His power the south wind. <verse eid="PSA 78:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 78:27"/>And He rained upon them food like the dust, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:27">and winged bird like the sand of the seas, <verse eid="PSA 78:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 78:28"/>and He felled them in the midst of their camp, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:28">all around their dwellings. <verse eid="PSA 78:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 78:29"/>So they ate and were satisfied greatly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:29">and their desires He brought to them. <verse eid="PSA 78:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 78:30"/>They were not estranged from their desire, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:30">and still their food <char style="add">was</char> in their mouth. <verse eid="PSA 78:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 78:31"/>And the anger of God came upon them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:31">and He killed the fattest of them </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:31">and subdued the young men of Israel. <verse eid="PSA 78:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 78:32"/>In all this, still they sinned, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:32">and they did not have faith in His wonders. <verse eid="PSA 78:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 78:33"/>And He finished off their days in futility,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">78.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in vapor</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:33">and their years in terror. <verse eid="PSA 78:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 78:34"/>When He slew them, they would seek Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:34">and they turned back and sought after God. <verse eid="PSA 78:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 78:35"/>And they remembered that God <char style="add">was</char> their rock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:35">and El-Elyon<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">78.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">El-Elyon</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">God Most High</char></note> their Redeemer. <verse eid="PSA 78:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 78:36"/>And they deceived Him with their mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:36">and with their tongue they lied to Him. <verse eid="PSA 78:36"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 78:37"/>And their heart was not established with Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:37">and they were not faithful to His covenant. <verse eid="PSA 78:37"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 78:38"/>And He, the compassionate One, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:38">forgave the iniquity and did not destroy <char style="add">them</char>; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 78:38">and He often restrained His anger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:38">and He did not stir up all His wrath. <verse eid="PSA 78:38"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 78:39"/>And He remembered that they <char style="add">were</char> flesh, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:39">a breath going by that does not return. <verse eid="PSA 78:39"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 78:40"/>How often they rebelled against Him in the wilderness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:40"><char style="add">and</char> grieved Him in the desert! <verse eid="PSA 78:40"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 78:41"/>And they turned back and tested God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:41">and they pained the Holy One of Israel. <verse eid="PSA 78:41"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 78:42"/>They have not remembered His hand,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">78.42 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">His power</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:42">the day when He ransomed them from the adversary, <verse eid="PSA 78:42"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 78:43"/>when He worked His signs in Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:43">and His wonders in the field of Zoan. <verse eid="PSA 78:43"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 78:44"/>And He turned their rivers into blood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:44">and from their streams they could not drink. <verse eid="PSA 78:44"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 78:45"/>He sent among them the swarm, and it consumed them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:45">and the frog, and it destroyed them. <verse eid="PSA 78:45"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 78:46"/>And He gave to the ravager their produce, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:46">and their labor to the locust. <verse eid="PSA 78:46"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 78:47"/>He destroyed with hail their vines, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:47">and their sycamore trees with frost.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">78.47 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">sleet</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">driving rain</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 78:47"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 78:48"/>And He gave up to the hail their cattle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:48">and their flocks to the firebolts. <verse eid="PSA 78:48"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="PSA 78:49"/>He sent against them the burning of His anger—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:49">fury, and rage, and distress, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:49">a discharge of messengers of evils. <verse eid="PSA 78:49"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="PSA 78:50"/>He made level a path for His anger; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:50">He did not spare their soul from death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:50">and He gave over their life to the pestilence. <verse eid="PSA 78:50"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="PSA 78:51"/>He even struck all the firstborn in Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:51">the first of the vigour in the tents of Ham. <verse eid="PSA 78:51"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="PSA 78:52"/>And His people He made go forth like sheep, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:52">and He guided them like a flock in the wilderness. <verse eid="PSA 78:52"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="53" style="v" sid="PSA 78:53"/>And He led them to safety, and they did not dread, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:53">and the sea covered their enemies. <verse eid="PSA 78:53"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="54" style="v" sid="PSA 78:54"/>And He brought them to the border of His holiness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:54">this mountain His right hand had acquired. <verse eid="PSA 78:54"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="55" style="v" sid="PSA 78:55"/>And He drove out the nations before their face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:55">and caused them to fall in the line of inheritance, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:55">and the tribes of Israel He settled in their tents. <verse eid="PSA 78:55"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="56" style="v" sid="PSA 78:56"/>And they tested and provoked El-Elyon,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">78.56 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">El-Elyon</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">God Most High</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:56">and His testimonies they did not keep. <verse eid="PSA 78:56"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="57" style="v" sid="PSA 78:57"/>And they turned back and were treacherous like their fathers; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:57">they were turned like a bow of deceit. <verse eid="PSA 78:57"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="58" style="v" sid="PSA 78:58"/>And they provoked Him to anger with their high places, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:58">and with their carved images they made Him jealous. <verse eid="PSA 78:58"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="59" style="v" sid="PSA 78:59"/>God heard and boiled over, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:59">and exceedingly He rejected Israel; <verse eid="PSA 78:59"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="60" style="v" sid="PSA 78:60"/>and He left behind the dwelling place of Shiloh, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:60">the tent He had pitched among men, <verse eid="PSA 78:60"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="61" style="v" sid="PSA 78:61"/>and He delivered His strength to captivity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:61">and His splendor to the hand of the adversary. <verse eid="PSA 78:61"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="62" style="v" sid="PSA 78:62"/>And He delivered up His people to the sword, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:62">and on His inheritance He boiled over. <verse eid="PSA 78:62"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="63" style="v" sid="PSA 78:63"/>Fire consumed His young men, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:63">and His virgins have not been praised. <verse eid="PSA 78:63"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="64" style="v" sid="PSA 78:64"/>His priests fell by the sword, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:64">and the widows could not weep. <verse eid="PSA 78:64"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="65" style="v" sid="PSA 78:65"/>And the Lord awoke as a sleeper, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:65">as a mighty one overcome by wine. <verse eid="PSA 78:65"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="66" style="v" sid="PSA 78:66"/>And He beat his adversaries back; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:66">a reproach forever He gave to them. <verse eid="PSA 78:66"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="67" style="v" sid="PSA 78:67"/>And He rejected the tent of Joseph, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:67">and the tribe of Ephraim He would not choose. <verse eid="PSA 78:67"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="68" style="v" sid="PSA 78:68"/>And He chose the tribe of Judah, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:68">Mount Zion, which He loved. <verse eid="PSA 78:68"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="69" style="v" sid="PSA 78:69"/>And He built His sanctuary like the heights; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:69">like the earth He founded it forever. <verse eid="PSA 78:69"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="70" style="v" sid="PSA 78:70"/>And He chose David His servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:70">and He took him from the folds of <char style="add">his</char> flock; <verse eid="PSA 78:70"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="71" style="v" sid="PSA 78:71"/>He brought him from tending the ewes </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:71">to be shepherd of Jacob His people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:71">and of Israel His inheritance. <verse eid="PSA 78:71"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="72" style="v" sid="PSA 78:72"/>And he tended them with the integrity of his heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 78:72">and by the skillfulness of his hands he guided them. <verse eid="PSA 78:72"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 78"/>

<chapter number="79" style="c" sid="PSA 79"/>

<para style="s">A Prayer for Deliverance</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of Asaph.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 79:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Jeremiah 52:1–11</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 74:1–23</char></note> O God, the nations have come into Your inheritance; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:1">they have defiled Your holy temple; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:1">they have laid Jerusalem in ruins. <verse eid="PSA 79:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 79:2"/>They have given the corpses of Your servants </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:2"><char style="add">as</char> food for the birds of the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:2">the flesh of Your holy ones for the beasts of the earth. <verse eid="PSA 79:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 79:3"/>They have poured out their blood like the waters </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:3">around Jerusalem, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:3">and there is none to bury them. <verse eid="PSA 79:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 79:4"/>We have become a reproach for our neighbors, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:4">a mocking and derision for those around us. <verse eid="PSA 79:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 79:5"/>Until when, O YHWH? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:5">Will You be angry forever? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:5">Will Your jealousy burn like fire? <verse eid="PSA 79:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 79:6"/>Pour out Your wrath toward the nations </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:6">that have not known You, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 79:6">and upon the kingdoms </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:6">that have not called on Your name! <verse eid="PSA 79:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 79:7"/>For they have devoured Jacob, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:7">and his habitation they have made desolate. <verse eid="PSA 79:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 79:8"/>Do not remember the former iniquities against us; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:8">hurry to let Your compassion come, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:8">for we have been brought very low. <verse eid="PSA 79:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 79:9"/>Help us, O God of our salvation! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:9">And deliver us, because of the glory of of Your name, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 79:9">and cover over our sins </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:9">for the sake of Your name. <verse eid="PSA 79:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 79:10"/>Why should the nations say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:10">“Where <char style="add">is</char> their God?” </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 79:10">Let it be known among the nations before our eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:10">the avenging of the blood of Your servants that was shed! <verse eid="PSA 79:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 79:11"/>Let the groaning of the prisoner come before You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:11">by the greatness of Your power, preserve the sons of death. <verse eid="PSA 79:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 79:12"/>And may You return to our neighbors sevenfold into their bosom </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:12">their reproach with which they have reproached You, O Lord! <verse eid="PSA 79:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 79:13"/>Then we, Your people, and the sheep of Your pasture, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:13">will give thanks to You forever; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 79:13">for generation and generation </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 79:13">we will declare Your praise. <verse eid="PSA 79:13"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 79"/>

<chapter number="80" style="c" sid="PSA 80"/>

<para style="s">Hear Us, O Shepherd of Israel</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. According to “Lilies.” A Testimony. Of Asaph. A Psalm.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 80:1"/> O Shepherd of Israel, Give ear! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:1"><char style="add">The One</char> leading Joseph as a flock, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 80:1">dwelling <char style="add">above</char> the cherubim, shine forth <verse eid="PSA 80:1"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 80:2"/>before the face of Ephraim and Benjamin and Manasseh! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 80:2">Rouse Your strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:2">and come to bring salvation for us! <verse eid="PSA 80:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 80:3"/>O God, restore us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:3">and cause Your face to shine, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:3">and we shall be saved! <verse eid="PSA 80:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 80:4"/>O YHWH, God of Hosts, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:4">until when will You smolder </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:4">at the prayer of Your people? <verse eid="PSA 80:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 80:5"/>You have fed them the bread of tears, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:5">and caused them to drink with tears a third part. <verse eid="PSA 80:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 80:6"/>You have made us a strife to our neighbors, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:6">and our enemies mock at it. <verse eid="PSA 80:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 80:7"/>O God of Hosts, restore us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:7">and cause Your face to shine, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:7">and we shall be saved! <verse eid="PSA 80:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 80:8"/>A vine from Egypt You pulled out; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:8">You drove out the nations and planted her. <verse eid="PSA 80:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 80:9"/>You cleared before her face and let her root take root, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:9">and she filled the land. <verse eid="PSA 80:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 80:10"/>The hills were covered with her shade, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:10">and the mighty cedars with her branches. <verse eid="PSA 80:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 80:11"/>She sent out her branches to the Sea,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">80.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the Mediterranean Sea, also called the Great Sea</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:11">and her shoots to the River.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">80.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the Euphrates</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 80:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 80:12"/>Why have You broken down her walls, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:12">and all passing by the way pluck her fruit? <verse eid="PSA 80:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 80:13"/>The boar from the forest tears at her, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:13">and the wild beast of the field feeds on her. <verse eid="PSA 80:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 80:14"/>O God of Hosts, return, we pray! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:14">Look down from the heavens and see, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 80:14">and attend to this vine, <verse eid="PSA 80:14"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 80:15"/>and the root that Your right hand has planted, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:15">and the son You have made strong for Yourself, <verse eid="PSA 80:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 80:16"/>having been burned in the fire, having been cut down. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:16">May they perish at the rebuke of Your face! <verse eid="PSA 80:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 80:17"/>Let Your hand be upon the man of Your right hand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:17">upon the son of man You made strong for Yourself. <verse eid="PSA 80:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 80:18"/>Then we will not turn back from You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:18">revive us, and we will call on Your name. <verse eid="PSA 80:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 80:19"/>O YHWH, God of Hosts, restore us! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:19">Cause Your face to shine, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 80:19">and we shall be saved! <verse eid="PSA 80:19"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 80"/>

<chapter number="81" style="c" sid="PSA 81"/>

<para style="s">Sing for Joy to God Our Strength</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. According to Gittith.† Of Asaph.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 81:1"/> Ring out <char style="add">praise</char> to God our strength; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:1">shout <char style="add">for joy</char> to the God of Jacob! <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">81.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Gittith</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; here and in Psalms 8 and 84.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 81:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 81:2"/>Lift up a melody and strike the timbrel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:2">the sweet-sounding harp with the lute. <verse eid="PSA 81:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 81:3"/>Blow the shofar on the new moon, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:3">on the full moon at the day of our Feast. <verse eid="PSA 81:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 81:4"/>For it <char style="add">is</char> a statute, O Israel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:4">an ordinance of the God of Jacob. <verse eid="PSA 81:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 81:5"/><char style="add">As</char> a testimony He established it in Joseph,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">81.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for Joseph</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:5">in His going forth over the land of Egypt. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:5">I heard a language <char style="add">that</char> I did not know: <verse eid="PSA 81:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 81:6"/>“I turned aside his shoulder from the burden; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:6">his hands pass over from the basket. <verse eid="PSA 81:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 81:7"/>In the <char style="add">time of</char> distress you called, and I drew you out; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:7">I answered you in the secret place of thunder; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:7">I tested you at the waters of Meribah.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">81.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Meribah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">quarreling</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Exodus 17:7.</char></note> </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 81:7">Selah <verse eid="PSA 81:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 81:8"/>hear, O My people, and I will testify against you—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:8">O Israel, if you would listen to Me! <verse eid="PSA 81:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 81:9"/>There shall not be among you a strange god, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:9">and you shall not bow down to foreign god. <verse eid="PSA 81:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 81:10"/>I <char style="add">am</char> YHWH your God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:10">who brought you out from the land of Egypt; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 81:10">open wide your mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:10">and I will fill it. <verse eid="PSA 81:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 81:11"/>My people would not listen to My voice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:11">and Israel has not consented to Me. <verse eid="PSA 81:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 81:12"/>And I sent them away in the stubbornness of their hearts, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:12">to walk by their own counsels. <verse eid="PSA 81:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 81:13"/>If only My people would listen to Me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:13">Israel would walk in My ways! <verse eid="PSA 81:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 81:14"/>In a moment I would subdue their enemies, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:14">and over their adversaries I would turn back My hand. <verse eid="PSA 81:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 81:15"/>Those hating YHWH would feign obedience before Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:15">and their time would be forever. <verse eid="PSA 81:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 81:16"/>And He would feed him of the fat of wheat, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 81:16">and <char style="add">with</char> honey from the rock I would satisfy you.” <verse eid="PSA 81:16"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 81"/>

<chapter number="82" style="c" sid="PSA 82"/>

<para style="s">God Presides in the Divine Assembly</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of Asaph.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 82:1"/> God takes His stand in the congregation of the divine; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 82:1">among the gods he renders judgment: <verse eid="PSA 82:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 82:2"/>“Until when will you⁺ judge unjustly,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">82.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">How long will you defend the unjust</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 82:2">and lift <char style="add">up</char> the faces of the wicked? </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 82:2">Selah <verse eid="PSA 82:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 82:3"/>Judge for the weak and the fatherless; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 82:3"><char style="add">for</char> the oppressed and needy bring justice. <verse eid="PSA 82:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 82:4"/>Rescue the weak and needy; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 82:4">deliver them from the hand of the wicked. <verse eid="PSA 82:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 82:5"/>They do not know, ad they do not understand; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 82:5">in the darkness they walk about; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 82:5">all the foundations of the earth are shaken. <verse eid="PSA 82:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 82:6"/>I said, ‘You⁺ <char style="add">are</char> gods, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 82:6">and all of you⁺ sons of the Most High.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">82.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in John 10:34</char></note><verse eid="PSA 82:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 82:7"/>Surely like a man you⁺ will die, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 82:7">and like one of the princes you⁺ will fall.” <verse eid="PSA 82:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 82:8"/>Rise up, O God, <char style="add">and</char> judge the earth! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 82:8">For You have an inheritance among all the nations. <verse eid="PSA 82:8"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 82"/>

<chapter number="83" style="c" sid="PSA 83"/>

<para style="s">O God, Be Not Silent</para>

<para style="s">A song. A Psalm of Asaph.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 83:1"/> O God, <char style="add">keep</char> no silence to You; do not be silent,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">83.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">deaf</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:1">and do not be still, O God. <verse eid="PSA 83:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 83:2"/>For behold, Your enemies roar, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:2">and those hating You have lifted up the head. <verse eid="PSA 83:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 83:3"/>Against Your people, they act with cunning counsel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:3">and they take counsel together against Your treasured ones. <verse eid="PSA 83:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 83:4"/>They say, “Come, and we shall make them disappear as a nation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:4">and the name of Israel will not be remembered anymore.” <verse eid="PSA 83:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 83:5"/>For, they consulted together in heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:5">they cut an alliance against You— <verse eid="PSA 83:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 83:6"/>the tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:6">Moab and the Hagrites, <verse eid="PSA 83:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 83:7"/>Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:7">Philistia with those dwelling <char style="add">in</char> Tyre. <verse eid="PSA 83:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 83:8"/>Assyria also has joined with them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:8">they have become an arm for the sons of Lot. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 83:8">Selah <verse eid="PSA 83:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 83:9"/>may You do to them as <char style="add">to</char> Midian, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:9">as <char style="add">to</char> Sisera, as <char style="add">to</char> Jabin, at the River Kishon. <verse eid="PSA 83:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 83:10"/>They perished at Endor; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:10">they became dung for the earth! <verse eid="PSA 83:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 83:11"/>Make their nobles like Oreb and like Zeeb, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:11">and like Zebah, and like Zalmunna—all their princes— <verse eid="PSA 83:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 83:12"/>who said, “Let us possess for ourselves </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:12">the pastures of God.” <verse eid="PSA 83:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 83:13"/>O my God, set them like the whirling dust, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:13">like chaff before the face of the wind! <verse eid="PSA 83:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 83:14"/>As the fire burns a forest, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:14">and as the flame sets the mountains on fire, <verse eid="PSA 83:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 83:15"/>so may You pursue them with Your tempest </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:15">and terrify them with Your storm. <verse eid="PSA 83:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 83:16"/>Fill their faces <char style="add">with</char> shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:16">and they shall seek Your name, O YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 83:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 83:17"/>Let them be put to shame and dismayed until forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:17">and may they be ashamed and perish! <verse eid="PSA 83:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 83:18"/>And they shall know that You—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:18">Your name <char style="add">is</char> YHWH—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 83:18">You alone <char style="add">are</char> Most High over all the earth! <verse eid="PSA 83:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 83"/>

<chapter number="84" style="c" sid="PSA 84"/>

<para style="s">Better Is One Day in Your Courts</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. According to Gittith.† Of the sons of Korah. A Psalm.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 84:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 1:14–18</char></note> How lovely <char style="add">is</char> Your dwelling place, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:1">O YHWH of hosts! <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">84.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Gittith</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; here and in Psalms 8 and 81.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 84:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 84:2"/>My soul longs, even faints, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:2">for the courts of YHWH; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 84:2">my heart and my flesh cry out </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:2">to the living God. <verse eid="PSA 84:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 84:3"/>Even the sparrow finds a home, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:3">and the swallow a nest for herself, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 84:3">where she places her young—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:3">near Your altars, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:3">YHWH of hosts, my King and My God, <verse eid="PSA 84:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 84:4"/>blessed <char style="add">are</char> those dwelling in Your house! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:4">Ever they are praising You. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 84:4">Selah <verse eid="PSA 84:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 84:5"/>blessed <char style="add">is</char> the man, the strength of him <char style="add">is</char> in You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:5">highways <char style="add">are</char> in their heart. <verse eid="PSA 84:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 84:6"/>Passing through the Valley of Baca,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">84.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Valley of Poplars</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:6">they make it a spring; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:6">even with blessings<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">84.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with pools</char></note> the early rain<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">84.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the autumn rain</char></note> covers it. <verse eid="PSA 84:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 84:7"/>They go from strength to strength; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:7"><char style="add">each</char> appears before God in Zion. <verse eid="PSA 84:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 84:8"/>O YHWH, God of Hosts, hear my prayer; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:8">give ear, O God of Jacob! </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 84:8">Selah <verse eid="PSA 84:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 84:9"/>may You see our shield, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:9">and look upon the face of Your anointed. <verse eid="PSA 84:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 84:10"/>For better a day in Your courts </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:10">than a thousand; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 84:10">I would choose to stand at the entrance in the house of my God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:10">than to dwell in the tents of the wicked. <verse eid="PSA 84:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 84:11"/>For a sun and shield <char style="add">is</char> YHWH God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:11">favor and honor YHWH will give, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 84:11"><char style="add">and</char> He will not withhold good </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:11">for those walking with integrity. <verse eid="PSA 84:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 84:12"/>O YHWH of hosts, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 84:12">blessed <char style="add">is</char> the man trusting in You. <verse eid="PSA 84:12"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 84"/>

<chapter number="85" style="c" sid="PSA 85"/>

<para style="s">You Showed Favor to Your Land</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. Of the sons of Korah a Psalm.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 85:1"/> You have shown favor, O YHWH, <char style="add">to</char> Your land; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:1">You have turned back the captivity of Jacob.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">85.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">restored the fortunes of Jacob</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 85:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 85:2"/>You have borne away the iniquity of Your people; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:2">You have covered all their sin. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 85:2">Selah <verse eid="PSA 85:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 85:3"/>You have gathered up all Your fury; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:3">You have turned from the burning of Your anger. <verse eid="PSA 85:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 85:4"/>Restore us, O God of our salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:4">and Your anger toward us cause to cease! <verse eid="PSA 85:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 85:5"/>Will You be angry with us forever? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:5">Will You draw out Your anger to generation and generation? <verse eid="PSA 85:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 85:6"/>Will You not turn back <char style="add">and</char> revive us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:6">that Your people may rejoice in You? <verse eid="PSA 85:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 85:7"/>Show us, O YHWH, Your loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:7">and give to us Your salvation! <verse eid="PSA 85:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 85:8"/>Let me hear what <char style="add">my</char> God YHWH will speak, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:8">for He will speak peace to His people and to His holy ones; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:8">He will not let them return to folly. <verse eid="PSA 85:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 85:9"/>Surely His salvation <char style="add">is</char> near to those fearing Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:9">that glory may dwell in our land. <verse eid="PSA 85:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 85:10"/>Loving devotion and faithfulness have met together; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:10">righteousness and peace have kissed. <verse eid="PSA 85:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 85:11"/>Faithfulness springs forth from the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:11">and righteousness looks down from the heavens. <verse eid="PSA 85:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 85:12"/>Indeed YHWH will give that which is good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:12">and our land will give forth its produce. <verse eid="PSA 85:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 85:13"/>Righteousness will go before Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 85:13">to prepare the way of His steps. <verse eid="PSA 85:13"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 85"/>

<chapter number="86" style="c" sid="PSA 86"/>

<para style="s">Tried but Trusting</para>

<para style="s">A Prayer of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 86:1"/> Incline Your ear, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:1">answer me, for I <char style="add">am</char> afflicted and in need. <verse eid="PSA 86:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 86:2"/>May You guard my life, for <char style="add">am</char> I faithful; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:2">may You save Your servant—the one trusting in You—You my God. <verse eid="PSA 86:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 86:3"/>Show favor to me, O Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:3">for to You I call out all the day. <verse eid="PSA 86:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 86:4"/>Make glad the soul of Your servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:4">for to You, O Lord, I lift up my soul. <verse eid="PSA 86:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 86:5"/>For You, O Lord, <char style="add">are</char> good and forgiving, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:5">and abundant in in loving devotion to all those calling on You. <verse eid="PSA 86:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 86:6"/>Give ear, O YHWH, <char style="add">to</char> my prayer, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:6">and attend to the voice of my pleas. <verse eid="PSA 86:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 86:7"/>In the day of my distress I call on you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:7">for You will answer me! <verse eid="PSA 86:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 86:8"/>None like You <char style="add">is</char> among the gods, O Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:8">and not like Your works. <verse eid="PSA 86:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 86:9"/>All the nations whom You have made </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:9">shall come and bow down before Your face, O Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:9">and they will glorify Your name. <verse eid="PSA 86:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 86:10"/>For You <char style="add">are</char> great, and the One doing wonders; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:10">You <char style="add">are</char> God—You alone. <verse eid="PSA 86:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 86:11"/>Instruct me, O YHWH, <char style="add">in</char> Your way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:11"><char style="add">and</char> I will walk in Your truth; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 86:11">unite my heart </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:11">to fear Your name. <verse eid="PSA 86:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 86:12"/>I will confess You, O Lord my God, with all my heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:12">and I will glorify Your name forever. <verse eid="PSA 86:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 86:13"/>For Your loving devotion <char style="add">is</char> great toward me. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:13">And You have delivered my soul from the depths of Sheol. <verse eid="PSA 86:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 86:14"/>O God, arrogant ones have risen against me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:14">and a gathering of ruthless ones have sought my life; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:14">and they do not set You before them. <verse eid="PSA 86:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 86:15"/>But You, O Lord, <char style="add">are</char> a compassionate and gracious God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:15">slow to anger and abounding in in loving devotion and faithfulness. <verse eid="PSA 86:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 86:16"/>Turn to me and show favor to me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:16">give Your strength to Your servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:16">and give salvation to the son of Your maidservant. <verse eid="PSA 86:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 86:17"/>Make with me a sign for good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:17">and those hating me will see it and be put to shame! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 86:17">For You, YHWH, have helped me and comforted me! <verse eid="PSA 86:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 86"/>

<chapter number="87" style="c" sid="PSA 87"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Loves the Gates of Zion</para>

<para style="s">Of the sons of Korah. A Psalm. A song.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 87:1"/> His foundation </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 87:1"><char style="add">is</char> on the holy mountains.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">87.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He has founded His city on the holy mountains</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 87:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 87:2"/>YHWH loves the gates of Zion </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 87:2">above all the dwellings of Jacob. <verse eid="PSA 87:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 87:3"/>Glorious things are ascribed to you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 87:3">O city of God. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 87:3">Selah <verse eid="PSA 87:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 87:4"/>“I will mention Rahab<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">87.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Rahab</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is a poetic name for Egypt.</char></note> and Babylon </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 87:4">among those who know Me—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 87:4">behold Philistia and Tyre, with Cush:<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">87.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the upper Nile region</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 87:4">This one was born there. <verse eid="PSA 87:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 87:5"/>And of Zion it will be said: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 87:5">“<char style="add">This</char> man and <char style="add">that</char> man were born in her; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 87:5">and He, the Most High, will establish her.” <verse eid="PSA 87:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 87:6"/>YHWH will record in the register of the peoples: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 87:6">“This one was born there.” </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 87:6">Selah <verse eid="PSA 87:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 87:7"/>and those singing, also as players on instruments: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 87:7">“All my springs <char style="add">are</char> in you.” <verse eid="PSA 87:7"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 87"/>

<chapter number="88" style="c" sid="PSA 88"/>

<para style="s">I Cry Out before You</para>

<para style="s">A Song. A Psalm of the sons of Korah, for the one directing. According to Mahalath Leannoth.† A Maskil† of Heman the Ezrahite.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 88:1"/> O YHWH, God of my salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:1"><char style="add">by</char> day I have cried out, <char style="add">and</char> in the night before You. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">88.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Mahalath Leannoth</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; see also Psalm 53:1.</char></note><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">88.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Maskil</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 88:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 88:2"/>May my prayer come before Your face; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:2">incline Your ear to my cry! <verse eid="PSA 88:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 88:3"/>For my soul is filled with troubles, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:3">and my life has reached to Sheol. <verse eid="PSA 88:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 88:4"/>I am counted with those going down into the Pit; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:4">I am like a man with no strength, <verse eid="PSA 88:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 88:5"/>among the dead <char style="add">set</char> free, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:5">like the slain lying down in the grave, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 88:5">whom You do not remember anymore, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:5">even they <char style="add">who</char> are cut off from Your hand. <verse eid="PSA 88:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 88:6"/>You have set me in the lowest Pit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:6">in darkness in the depths. <verse eid="PSA 88:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 88:7"/>Upon me Your wrath has grabbed hold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:7">and <char style="add">with</char> all Your waves You have afflicted. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 88:7">Selah <verse eid="PSA 88:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 88:8"/>You have put my acquaintances far from me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:8">You have made me loathsome to them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:8"><char style="add">I am</char> shut in, and I cannot go forth. <verse eid="PSA 88:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 88:9"/>My eye languishes from <char style="add">this</char> affliction; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:9">I have called to You, O YHWH, all the day; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:9">I have stretched out to You my hands. <verse eid="PSA 88:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 88:10"/>Will You work wonders for the dead? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:10">And if departed spirits rise up, do they thank You? </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 88:10">Selah <verse eid="PSA 88:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 88:11"/>Can Your loving devotion be recounted in the Grave, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:11"><char style="add">or</char> Your faithfulness in Abaddon?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">88.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Abaddon</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Destruction</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 88:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 88:12"/>Will Your wonders be known in the darkness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:12">and Your righteousness in the land of forgetfulness? <verse eid="PSA 88:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 88:13"/>And I, O YHWH, cry for help to You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:13">and in the morning my prayer comes before You. <verse eid="PSA 88:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 88:14"/>Why, O YHWH, do You reject my soul? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:14">You hide Your face from me. <verse eid="PSA 88:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 88:15"/>I <char style="add">am</char> afflicted and dying from my youth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:15">I bear Your terrors; I am in despair. <verse eid="PSA 88:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 88:16"/>Your wrath has passed over me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:16">Your terrors have destroyed me. <verse eid="PSA 88:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 88:17"/>They came around me like the waters all the day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:17">they surrounded me altogether. <verse eid="PSA 88:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 88:18"/>You have put far my beloved and friend; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 88:18">my close acquaintance <char style="add">is</char> darkness. <verse eid="PSA 88:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 88"/>

<chapter number="89" style="c" sid="PSA 89"/>

<para style="s">I Will Sing of His Love Forever</para>

<para style="s">A Maskil† of Ethan the Ezrahite.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 89:1"/> I will sing of the loving devotion of YHWH forever. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:1">To generation and generation I will make known Your faithfulness with my mouth. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">89.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Maskil</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 89:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 89:2"/>For I have said, “Loving devotion is built up forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:2">the heavens—You establish Your faithfulness in them.” <verse eid="PSA 89:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 89:3"/>“I have cut a covenant with My chosen one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:3">I have sworn to David My servant: <verse eid="PSA 89:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 89:4"/>‘Even to forever I will establish Your seed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:4">and build up for generation and generation your throne.’” </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 89:4">Selah <verse eid="PSA 89:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 89:5"/>and the heavens will praise Your wonders, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:5"><char style="add">and</char> Your faithfulness also in the assembly of the holy ones. <verse eid="PSA 89:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 89:6"/>For who in the heavens can be compared to YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:6">likened to YHWH among the sons of the mighty?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">89.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the sons of God</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the heavenly beings</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 89:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 89:7"/>God is to be feared greatly in the council of the holy ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:7">and to be revered by all those surrounding Him. <verse eid="PSA 89:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 89:8"/>O YHWH, God of Hosts, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:8">who <char style="add">is</char> like You, O mighty YAH? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:8">And Your faithfulness surrounds You! <verse eid="PSA 89:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 89:9"/>You rule over the pride of the sea; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:9">its waves mount up, <char style="add">and</char> You still them. <verse eid="PSA 89:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 89:10"/>You crushed Rahab as one slain; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:10">with the arm of Your strength, You scattered Your enemies. <verse eid="PSA 89:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 89:11"/>Unto You <char style="add">are</char> the heavens; the earth also <char style="add">is</char> unto You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:11">the world and its fullness—You have founded them. <verse eid="PSA 89:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 89:12"/>The north and the south, You have created them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:12">Tabor and Hermon ring out praise in Your name. <verse eid="PSA 89:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 89:13"/>Unto You <char style="add">is</char> an arm with might; strong <char style="add">is</char> Your hand; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:13">high <char style="add">is</char> Your right hand. <verse eid="PSA 89:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 89:14"/>Righteousness and justice <char style="add">are</char> the foundation of Your throne; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:14">loving devotion and faithfulness go before Your face. <verse eid="PSA 89:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 89:15"/>Blessed <char style="add">are</char> the people knowing the joyful sound; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:15">O YHWH, in the light of Your face they walk. <verse eid="PSA 89:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 89:16"/>In Your name they rejoice all the day, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:16">and in Your righteousness they are lifted high. <verse eid="PSA 89:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 89:17"/>For You <char style="add">are</char> the splendor of their strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:17">and by Your favor our horn is raised high. <verse eid="PSA 89:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 89:18"/>Indeed, unto YHWH <char style="add">is</char> our shield, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:18">and our king unto the Holy One of Israel. <verse eid="PSA 89:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 89:19"/>Once You spoke in a vision </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:19">to Your holy ones, and said: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 89:19">“I have given help to a mighty one; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:19">I have exalted one chosen from the people. <verse eid="PSA 89:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 89:20"/>I have found David My servant; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:20">with the oil of My holiness I anointed him, <verse eid="PSA 89:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 89:21"/>with whom My hand is established—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:21">My arm also will strengthen him. <verse eid="PSA 89:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 89:22"/>The enemy will not exact tribute from him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:22">and a son of wickedness shall not afflict him. <verse eid="PSA 89:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 89:23"/>And I will crush his foes before his face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:23">and those hating him I will strike. <verse eid="PSA 89:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 89:24"/>And My faithfulness and My loving devotion <char style="add">are</char> with him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:24">and in My name his horn will be exalted. <verse eid="PSA 89:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 89:25"/>And I will set his hand over the sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:25">and his right hand over the rivers. <verse eid="PSA 89:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 89:26"/>He will call to Me, ‘You <char style="add">are</char> My Father, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:26">my God, and the Rock of my salvation.’ <verse eid="PSA 89:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 89:27"/>I also appoint him firstborn, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:27">the highest of the kings of the earth. <verse eid="PSA 89:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 89:28"/>Forever I will keep for him My loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:28">and My covenant will stand fast for him. <verse eid="PSA 89:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 89:29"/>And I will establish His seed forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:29">and his throne like the days of the heavens. <verse eid="PSA 89:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 89:30"/>If his sons should abandon My instruction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:30">and do not walk in My ordinances, <verse eid="PSA 89:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 89:31"/>if they violate My statutes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:31">and do not keep My commandments, <verse eid="PSA 89:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 89:32"/>then I will attend <char style="add">to</char> their transgression with the rod, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:32">and <char style="add">to</char> their iniquity with stripes. <verse eid="PSA 89:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 89:33"/>And I will not break off My loving devotion from him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:33">and I will not be false in My faithfulness. <verse eid="PSA 89:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 89:34"/>I will not violate My covenant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:34">and a declaration of My lips I will not change. <verse eid="PSA 89:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 89:35"/>Once I have sworn by My holiness—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:35">I will not lie to David— <verse eid="PSA 89:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 89:36"/>His seed shall be forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:36">and his throne like the sun before Me. <verse eid="PSA 89:36"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 89:37"/>Like the moon It will be established forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:37">even <char style="add">as</char> the faithful witness in the sky.” </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 89:37">Selah <verse eid="PSA 89:37"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 89:38"/>and You have cast away and rejected; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:38">You have been enraged with Your anointed. <verse eid="PSA 89:38"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 89:39"/>You have renounced the covenant of Your servant; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:39">You have defiled his diadem on the ground. <verse eid="PSA 89:39"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 89:40"/>You have broken down all his walls; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:40">You have set his strongholds <char style="add">to</char> ruin. <verse eid="PSA 89:40"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 89:41"/>All passing by the way plunder him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:41">he has become a reproach to his neighbors. <verse eid="PSA 89:41"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 89:42"/>You have raised high the right hand of his adversaries; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:42">all of his enemies You have made glad. <verse eid="PSA 89:42"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 89:43"/>Also You have turned back the sharpness of his sword, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:43">and You have not made it stand in the battle. <verse eid="PSA 89:43"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 89:44"/>You have made his brightness cease, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:44">and You have cast down his throne to the ground. <verse eid="PSA 89:44"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 89:45"/>You have shortened the days of his youth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:45">You have covered over him <char style="add">with</char> shame. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 89:45">Selah <verse eid="PSA 89:45"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 89:46"/>until when, O YHWH? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:46">Will You hide Yourself forever? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:46">Will Your rage keep burning like fire? <verse eid="PSA 89:46"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 89:47"/>Remember me—how <char style="add">short</char> a lifetime; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:47">for what emptiness You created all the sons of men! <verse eid="PSA 89:47"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 89:48"/>What man can live and not see death? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:48">Can he deliver his soul from the hand of Sheol? </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 89:48">Selah <verse eid="PSA 89:48"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="PSA 89:49"/>where <char style="add">is</char> Your loving devotion <char style="add">is</char> Your Of old, O Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:49">which You swore of David in Your faithfulness? <verse eid="PSA 89:49"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="PSA 89:50"/>Remember, O Lord, the reproach of Your servants—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:50">I bear in my bosom from all the many peoples, <verse eid="PSA 89:50"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="PSA 89:51"/>with which Your enemies have taunted, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 89:51">with which they have reproached the footsteps of Your anointed one. <verse eid="PSA 89:51"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="PSA 89:52"/>Blessed <char style="add">be</char> YHWH forever! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 89:52">Amen and Amen. <verse eid="PSA 89:52"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 89"/>

<chapter number="90" style="c" sid="PSA 90"/>

<para style="s">BOOK IV</para>

<para style="s">Psalms 90–106</para>

<para style="s">From Everlasting to Everlasting</para>

<para style="s">A Prayer of Moses, the man of God.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 90:1"/> Lord, You have been a dwelling place for us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:1">in generation and generation. <verse eid="PSA 90:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 90:2"/>In the <char style="add">time</char> before the mountains were brought forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:2">or You formed the earth and the world, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 90:2">and from forever even to forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:2">You <char style="add">are</char> God. <verse eid="PSA 90:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 90:3"/>You return man to dust </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:3">and say, “Return, O sons of men!” <verse eid="PSA 90:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 90:4"/>For a thousand years in your eyes </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:4"><char style="add">are</char> like a day past that passes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:4">or a watch in the night. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">90.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See 2 Peter 3:8.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 90:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 90:5"/>You sweep them away; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:5">they are in their sleep like the grass that sprouts up in the morning. <verse eid="PSA 90:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 90:6"/>In the morning it blossoms and flourishes; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:6">in the evening it is cut down and withers. <verse eid="PSA 90:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 90:7"/>For we are consumed by Your anger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:7">and by Your wrath we are terrified. <verse eid="PSA 90:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 90:8"/>You have set our iniquities before You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:8">our hidden <char style="add">things</char> in the light of Your face. <verse eid="PSA 90:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 90:9"/>For all our days decline in Your fury; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:9">we finish our years as a sigh. <verse eid="PSA 90:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 90:10"/>The days of our years, in them <char style="add">are</char> seventy years, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:10">or if by strength eighty years; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 90:10">yet their pride <char style="add">is</char> toil and trouble—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:10">for it is cut off soon, and we fly away. <verse eid="PSA 90:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 90:11"/>Who knows the power of Your anger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:11">for as the fear of You <char style="add">is</char> Your wrath? <verse eid="PSA 90:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 90:12"/>So teach <char style="add">us</char> to number our days, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:12">that we may bring in a heart of wisdom. <verse eid="PSA 90:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 90:13"/>Turn back, O YHWH—until when?—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:13">And have compassion on Your servants! <verse eid="PSA 90:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 90:14"/>Satisfy us in the morning with Your loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:14">that we may sing for joy and be glad in all our days. <verse eid="PSA 90:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 90:15"/>Let us be glad according to the days You have afflicted us—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:15">the years we have seen evil. <verse eid="PSA 90:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 90:16"/>Let Your work be shown to Your servants, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:16">and Your splendor upon their sons. <verse eid="PSA 90:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 90:17"/>And may the favor<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">90.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">beauty</char></note> of YHWH our God come to be upon us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:17">and may You support the work of our hands upon us—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 90:17">and the work of our hands establish! <verse eid="PSA 90:17"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 90"/>

<chapter number="91" style="c" sid="PSA 91"/>

<para style="s">You Are My Refuge and My Fortress</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 91:1"/>The one sitting in the secret place of the Most High, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:1">in the shade of Shaddai<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">91.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Shaddai</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Almighty</char></note> he will abide. <verse eid="PSA 91:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 91:2"/>I will say of YHWH: “My refuge and my stronghold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:2">My God, I trust in Him!” <verse eid="PSA 91:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 91:3"/>Surely He will snatch you </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:3">from the snare of the trapper, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:3">from the plague of calamity. <verse eid="PSA 91:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 91:4"/>With His pinions He will give cover for you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:4">and under His wings you will take refuge; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:4">a shield and buckler <char style="add">is</char> His faithfulness. <verse eid="PSA 91:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 91:5"/>You shall not be afraid of the terror of the night, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:5"><char style="add">or</char> of the arrow <char style="add">that</char> flies by day, <verse eid="PSA 91:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 91:6"/>from the plague that walks in the darkness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:6"><char style="add">or</char> from the pestilence that destroys at noon. <verse eid="PSA 91:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 91:7"/>A thousand may fall at your side, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:7">and a multitude at your right hand—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:7">it shall not draw near to you. <verse eid="PSA 91:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 91:8"/>But with your eyes you shall look, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:8">and you shall see the reward of the wicked. <verse eid="PSA 91:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 91:9"/>Because You, O YHWH <char style="add">are</char> my refuge; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:9">the Most High you have made your dwelling place. <verse eid="PSA 91:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 91:10"/>Evil shall not meet with you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:10">and plague shall not come near, by your tent. <verse eid="PSA 91:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 91:11"/>For He will command His angels concerning you </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:11">to guard you in all your ways. <verse eid="PSA 91:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 91:12"/>Upon the hands they shall lift you up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:12">lest you strike your foot against a stone. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">91.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Matthew 4:6 and Luke 4:10–11</char></note><verse eid="PSA 91:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 91:13"/>Upon the lion and cobra you will tread; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:13">you will trample the young lion and the serpent. <verse eid="PSA 91:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 91:14"/>“Because in Me he has delighted, so will I rescue him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:14">I will set him up high because he has known My Name. <verse eid="PSA 91:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 91:15"/>He will call on Me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:15">and I will answer him; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 91:15">I <char style="add">am</char> with him in distress; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:15">I will deliver him and honor him. <verse eid="PSA 91:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 91:16"/>With length of days I will satisfy him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 91:16">and cause him to look on My salvation.” <verse eid="PSA 91:16"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 91"/>

<chapter number="92" style="c" sid="PSA 92"/>

<para style="s">How Great Are Your Works!</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm. A Song for the Sabbath day.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 92:1"/> <char style="add">It is</char> good to give thanks to YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:1">and to sing praise to Your name, O Most High, <verse eid="PSA 92:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 92:2"/>to declare in the morning Your loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:2">and Your faithfulness in the nights, <verse eid="PSA 92:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 92:3"/>on ten strings and on the harp, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:3">with a melody of the lyre. <verse eid="PSA 92:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 92:4"/>For You have made me glad, O YHWH, by Your work; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:4">at the works of Your hands I shout <char style="add">for joy</char>. <verse eid="PSA 92:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 92:5"/>How great are Your works, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:5"><char style="add">how</char> very deep Your thoughts! <verse eid="PSA 92:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 92:6"/>A stupid man does not know, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:6">and a fool cannot understand this: <verse eid="PSA 92:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 92:7"/>The wicked sprout like grass, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:7">and all the workers of iniquity blossom, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:7">to be destroyed forever and ever! <verse eid="PSA 92:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 92:8"/>And You <char style="add">are</char> on high forever, O YHWH! <verse eid="PSA 92:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 92:9"/>For behold, Your enemies, O YHWH—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:9">for behold, Your enemies will perish; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:9">all the workers of iniquity will be scattered! <verse eid="PSA 92:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 92:10"/>But You have lifted high my horn like that of a wild ox; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:10">I have been anointed with fresh oil. <verse eid="PSA 92:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 92:11"/>And my eye has looked on my enemies; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:11">of those rising up against me, those doing evil,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">92.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the wailing of my wicked foes</char></note> my ears hear. <verse eid="PSA 92:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 92:12"/>The righteous one will sprout like a palm tree; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:12">like a cedar in Lebanon he will grow. <verse eid="PSA 92:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 92:13"/>Those planted in the house of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:13">in the courts of our God, they will sprout. <verse eid="PSA 92:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 92:14"/>Still bearing fruit in old age, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:14">they will remain fat and flourishing— <verse eid="PSA 92:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 92:15"/>to declare that YHWH my Rock <char style="add">is</char> upright, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 92:15">and <char style="add">there is</char> no injustice in Him. <verse eid="PSA 92:15"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 92"/>

<chapter number="93" style="c" sid="PSA 93"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Reigns!</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 93:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 99:1–9</char></note>YHWH reigns! In majesty He is robed. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 93:1">YHWH has girded Himself <char style="add">with</char> strength. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 93:1">Surely the world is established; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 93:1">no more can it be shaken. <verse eid="PSA 93:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 93:2"/>Your throne <char style="add">is</char> established from that time; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 93:2">You <char style="add">are King</char> from everlasting. <verse eid="PSA 93:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 93:3"/>The floodwaters have lifted up, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 93:3">the streams have lifted up their voice; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 93:3">the streams have lifted up their breakers. <verse eid="PSA 93:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 93:4"/>More than the voices of many waters, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 93:4"><char style="add">more</char> majestic <char style="add">than</char> the breakers of the sea, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 93:4">majestic on high <char style="add">is</char> YHWH! <verse eid="PSA 93:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 93:5"/>Your testimonies are fully confirmed; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 93:5">Your house is lovely <char style="add">in</char> holiness, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 93:5">for the length of days. <verse eid="PSA 93:5"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 93"/>

<chapter number="94" style="c" sid="PSA 94"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Will Not Forget His People</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 94:1"/>God of vengeance, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:1">O God of vengeance, shine forth! <verse eid="PSA 94:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 94:2"/>Rise up, O Judge of the earth! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:2">Return a recompense on the proud. <verse eid="PSA 94:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 94:3"/>Until when <char style="add">will</char> the wicked, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:3">until when <char style="add">will</char> the wicked exult? <verse eid="PSA 94:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 94:4"/>They pour out words of arrogance; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:4">all the workers of iniquity boast in themselves. <verse eid="PSA 94:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 94:5"/>Your people, O YHWH, they crush, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:5">and Your heritage they afflict. <verse eid="PSA 94:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 94:6"/>The widow and the foreigner they kill, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:6">and the fatherless they murder. <verse eid="PSA 94:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 94:7"/>And they say, “Yah does not see, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:7">and the God of Jacob does not discern.” <verse eid="PSA 94:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 94:8"/>Discern, O senseless among the people! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:8">O fools, when will you⁺ be wise? <verse eid="PSA 94:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 94:9"/>The One planting the ear, can He not hear? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:9">Or the One forming the eye, can He not see? <verse eid="PSA 94:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 94:10"/>The One disciplining the nations, does He not correct—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:10">the One teaching a man knowledge? <verse eid="PSA 94:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 94:11"/>YHWH knows the thoughts of man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:11">that they <char style="add">are</char> vapor. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">94.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">futile</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in 1 Corinthians 3:20</char></note><verse eid="PSA 94:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 94:12"/>Blessed <char style="add">is</char> the man whom You instruct, O YAH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:12">and teach him from Your law, <verse eid="PSA 94:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 94:13"/>that You may give rest to him from the days of evil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:13">until a pit is dug for the wicked. <verse eid="PSA 94:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 94:14"/>For YHWH will not forsake His people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:14">and he will not forsake His inheritance. <verse eid="PSA 94:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 94:15"/>But to righteousness the judgment will return, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:15">and all the upright of heart will follow it. <verse eid="PSA 94:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 94:16"/>Who will rise up for me against the evildoers? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:16">Who will stand up for me against the workers of iniquity? <verse eid="PSA 94:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 94:17"/>Unless YHWH <char style="add">had been</char> the help for me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:17">My soul would soon have dwelt in silence. <verse eid="PSA 94:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 94:18"/>When I said, “My foot is slipping,” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:18">Your loving devotion, O YHWH, supports me. <verse eid="PSA 94:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 94:19"/>In the abundance of my anxieties within me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:19">Your comforts delighted my soul. <verse eid="PSA 94:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 94:20"/>Can the throne of iniquity join with You—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:20">one shaping mischief by statute? <verse eid="PSA 94:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 94:21"/>They band together against the soul of the righteous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:21">and condemn innocent blood.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">94.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">condemn the innocent to death</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 94:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 94:22"/>And YHWH has become for me as a place up high, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:22">and my God as the rock of my refuge. <verse eid="PSA 94:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 94:23"/>And He has turned back upon them their own iniquity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:23">and in their wickedness He will finish them off—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 94:23">YHWH our God, will finish them off! <verse eid="PSA 94:23"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 94"/>

<chapter number="95" style="c" sid="PSA 95"/>

<para style="s">Do Not Harden Your Hearts</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 95:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Hebrews 3:7–11</char></note>O come, let us sing out to YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 95:1">let us shout to the Rock of our salvation! <verse eid="PSA 95:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 95:2"/>Let us come before His face with thanksgiving, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 95:2">let us shout joyfully with psalms to Him! <verse eid="PSA 95:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 95:3"/>For a great God <char style="add">is</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 95:3">and the great King above all gods— <verse eid="PSA 95:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 95:4"/>in whose hand <char style="add">are</char> the depths of the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 95:4">and the peaks of the mountains <char style="add">are</char> unto Him, <verse eid="PSA 95:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 95:5"/><char style="add">and</char> to whom <char style="add">is</char> the sea, for He made it, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 95:5">and His hands formed the dry land. <verse eid="PSA 95:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 95:6"/>O come, let us worship and bow down; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 95:6">let us kneel before the face of YHWH our Maker! <verse eid="PSA 95:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 95:7"/>For He <char style="add">is</char> our God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 95:7">and we <char style="add">are</char> the people of His pasture, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 95:7">and the sheep of His hand. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 95:7">Today, if you⁺ hear His voice: <verse eid="PSA 95:7"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 95:8"/>You⁺ shall not harden your⁺ hearts, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 95:8">as <char style="add">at</char> Meribah, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 95:8">as <char style="add">in</char> the day at Massah in the wilderness,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">95.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">as you did in the rebellion</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Meribah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">quarreling</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Exodus 17:7; cited in Hebrews 3:15 and Hebrews 4:7.</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">95.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the day of testing in the wilderness</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Massah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">testing</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Exodus 17:7.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 95:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 95:9"/>when your⁺ fathers tested Me—they tried Me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 95:9">even though they had seen My work. <verse eid="PSA 95:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 95:10"/>Forty years I was repulsed by <char style="add">that</char> generation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 95:10">and I said, “They <char style="add">are</char> a people going astray <char style="add">in</char> heart,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">95.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">They always go astray in the heart</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 95:10">and they have not known My ways.” <verse eid="PSA 95:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 95:11"/>So I swore in My anger, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 95:11">“They shall not come into My rest!” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">95.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Hebrews 3:7–11, Hebrews 4:3, and Hebrews 4:5</char></note><verse eid="PSA 95:11"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 95"/>

<chapter number="96" style="c" sid="PSA 96"/>

<para style="s">Sing to Yahweh, All the Earth</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 96:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Chronicles 16:23–36</char></note>Sing to YHWH a new song; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:1">sing to YHWH, all the earth! <verse eid="PSA 96:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 96:2"/>Sing to YHWH, bless His name; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:2">give the news from day to day of His salvation! <verse eid="PSA 96:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 96:3"/>Recount among the nations His glory, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:3">among all the peoples His wonders. <verse eid="PSA 96:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 96:4"/>For great <char style="add">is</char> YHWH, and to be praised greatly; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:4">He <char style="add">is</char> to be feared above all gods. <verse eid="PSA 96:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 96:5"/>For all the gods of the peoples <char style="add">are</char> idols, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:5">and YHWH made the heavens. <verse eid="PSA 96:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 96:6"/>Splendor and majesty <char style="add">are</char> before His face; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:6">strength and beauty <char style="add">are</char> in His sanctuary. <verse eid="PSA 96:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 96:7"/>Give to YHWH, O families of the peoples, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:7">give to YHWH honor and strength! <verse eid="PSA 96:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 96:8"/>Give to YHWH the glory <char style="add">due</char> His name; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:8">lift up an offering and come into His courts! <verse eid="PSA 96:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 96:9"/>Bow down before YHWH in the splendor of <char style="add">His</char> holiness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:9">tremble before Him, all the earth! <verse eid="PSA 96:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 96:10"/>Say among the nations, “YHWH reigns!” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:10">Surely the world is firmly set—it cannot be shaken; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:10">He will judge the peoples with uprightness. <verse eid="PSA 96:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 96:11"/>Let the heavens rejoice </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:11">and let the earth be glad; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:11">let the sea and its fullness roar! <verse eid="PSA 96:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 96:12"/>Let the field be joyful, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:12">and all that <char style="add">is</char> in it! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 96:12">Then all the trees of the forest will shout for joy, <verse eid="PSA 96:12"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 96:13"/>before YHWH, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 96:13">for He is coming—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:13">for He is coming to judge the earth! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 96:13">He will judge the world in righteousness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 96:13">and the peoples in His faithfulness. <verse eid="PSA 96:13"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 96"/>

<chapter number="97" style="c" sid="PSA 97"/>

<para style="s">Let the Earth Rejoice</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 97:1"/>YHWH reigns, let the earth rejoice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:1">let the many shores be glad! <verse eid="PSA 97:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 97:2"/>Cloud and darkness surround Him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:2">righteousness and justice <char style="add">are</char> the foundation of His throne. <verse eid="PSA 97:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 97:3"/>A fire goes out before His face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:3">and burns up His adversaries round about. <verse eid="PSA 97:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 97:4"/>His lightnings give light <char style="add">to</char> the world; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:4">the earth sees, and trembles. <verse eid="PSA 97:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 97:5"/>The mountains are melted like wax </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:5">from before the face of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:5">from before the face of the Lord of all the earth. <verse eid="PSA 97:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 97:6"/>The heavens declare His righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:6">and all the peoples see His glory. <verse eid="PSA 97:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 97:7"/>Let all those serving a carved image be put to shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:7">those boasting in idols! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:7">Bow down to Him, all gods! <verse eid="PSA 97:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 97:8"/>Zion hears and is glad; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:8">the daughters of Judah rejoice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:8">because of Your judgments, O YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 97:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 97:9"/>For You, O YHWH-Elyon,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">97.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">YHWH-Elyon</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">LORD Most High</char></note> <char style="add">are</char> over all the earth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:9">greatly are You exalted over all gods. <verse eid="PSA 97:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 97:10"/>O lovers of YHWH, hate evil; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:10">He preserves the souls of His holy ones; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:10">from the hand of the wicked He delivers them. <verse eid="PSA 97:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 97:11"/>Light shines on the righteous,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">97.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> One Hebrew manuscript, LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; most Hebrew manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Light is sown for the righteous</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:11">and gladness for the upright of heart. <verse eid="PSA 97:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 97:12"/>Be glad, O righteous ones, in YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 97:12">and give thanks at the remembrance of His holiness! <verse eid="PSA 97:12"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 97"/>

<chapter number="98" style="c" sid="PSA 98"/>

<para style="s">Sing to Yahweh a New Song</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 98:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Isaiah 42:10–17</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 149:1–9</char></note> Sing to YHWH a new song, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 98:1">for He has done wonders! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 98:1">His right hand has gained victory for Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 98:1">even the arm of His holiness. <verse eid="PSA 98:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 98:2"/>YHWH has made known His victory; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 98:2">before the eyes of the nations, He has revealed His righteousness. <verse eid="PSA 98:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 98:3"/>He has remembered His kindness and His faithfulness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 98:3">to the house of Israel; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 98:3">all the ends of the earth have seen </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 98:3">the victory of our God. <verse eid="PSA 98:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 98:4"/>Shout joyfully to YHWH, all the earth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 98:4">break forth and cry aloud and sing praises! <verse eid="PSA 98:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 98:5"/>Sing praises to YHWH with the harp, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 98:5">with the harp and the voice of melody! <verse eid="PSA 98:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 98:6"/>With the trumpets and the voice of the shofar, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 98:6">shout joyfully before the face of YHWH the King! <verse eid="PSA 98:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 98:7"/>Let the sea roar, and its fullness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 98:7">the world, and those dwelling in it! <verse eid="PSA 98:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 98:8"/>Let the rivers clap the hands; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 98:8">let the hills cry aloud together, <verse eid="PSA 98:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 98:9"/>before the face of YHWH—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 98:9">for He is coming to judge the earth! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 98:9">He will judge the world with righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 98:9">and the peoples with uprightness! <verse eid="PSA 98:9"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 98"/>

<chapter number="99" style="c" sid="PSA 99"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Reigns!</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 99:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 93:1–5</char></note>YHWH reigns, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:1">let the peoples tremble! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 99:1">He dwells <char style="add">above</char> the cherubim, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:1">let the earth be shaken! <verse eid="PSA 99:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 99:2"/>YHWH <char style="add">is</char> great in Zion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:2">and high <char style="add">is</char> He over all the peoples. <verse eid="PSA 99:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 99:3"/>Let them praise Your great and awesome name! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:3">Holy <char style="add">is</char> He!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">99.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">it is holy!</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 99:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 99:4"/>The mighty King loves justice,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">99.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">The might of the King loves justice.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:4">You have established uprightness; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 99:4">justice and righteousness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:4">You have done in Jacob. <verse eid="PSA 99:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 99:5"/>Exalt YHWH, our God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:5">and bow down at His footstool! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:5">Holy <char style="add">is</char> He! <verse eid="PSA 99:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 99:6"/>Moses and Aaron <char style="add">were</char> among His priests, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:6">and Samuel among those calling on His name—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:6">they called to YHWH, and He answered them. <verse eid="PSA 99:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 99:7"/>Within the pillar of cloud He spoke to them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:7">they kept His testimonies, and the statute He gave to them. <verse eid="PSA 99:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 99:8"/>O YHWH our God, You answered them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:8">a forgiving God You became for them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:8">and one taking vengeance over their misdeeds. <verse eid="PSA 99:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 99:9"/>Exalt YHWH, our God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:9">and bow down at the mountain of His holiness—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 99:9">for holy <char style="add">is</char> YHWH our God! <verse eid="PSA 99:9"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 99"/>

<chapter number="100" style="c" sid="PSA 100"/>

<para style="s">Make a Joyful Noise</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of thanksgiving.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 100:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 66:1–20</char></note> Shout to YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 100:1">all the earth. <verse eid="PSA 100:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 100:2"/>Serve YHWH with gladness! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 100:2">Come before His face with a shout of joy! <verse eid="PSA 100:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 100:3"/>Know that YHWH, He <char style="add">is</char> God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 100:3">He has made us and not we ourselves;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">100.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and we are His</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 100:3"><char style="add">we are</char> His people and the sheep of His pasture. <verse eid="PSA 100:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 100:4"/>Enter His gates with thanksgiving, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 100:4">His courts with praise; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 100:4">give thanks to Him; bless His name! <verse eid="PSA 100:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 100:5"/>For YHWH <char style="add">is</char> good; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 100:5">forever <char style="add">is</char> His loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 100:5">and unto generation and generation His faithfulness. <verse eid="PSA 100:5"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 100"/>

<chapter number="101" style="c" sid="PSA 101"/>

<para style="s">I Will Set No Worthless Thing before My Eyes</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm. Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 101:1"/> I will sing of loving devotion and justice; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 101:1">to You, O YHWH, I will sing praises. <verse eid="PSA 101:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 101:2"/>I will act wisely in the way of integrity. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 101:2">When will You come to me? </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 101:2">I walk about in the integrity of my heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 101:2">in the midst of my house. <verse eid="PSA 101:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 101:3"/>I do not set before my eyes </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 101:3">an object of worthlessness; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 101:3">I have hated the work of those turning aside—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 101:3">it shall not cling to me! <verse eid="PSA 101:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 101:4"/>A perverse heart shall depart from me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 101:4">evil I will not know. <verse eid="PSA 101:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 101:5"/>The one slandering his neighbor in secret, I will put an end </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 101:5"><char style="add">to</char> him; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 101:5">the high of eyes and proud of heart—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 101:5">him I will not endure. <verse eid="PSA 101:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 101:6"/>My eyes <char style="add">are</char> on the faithful ones of the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 101:6">to dwell with me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 101:6">the one walking in the way of integrity, he </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 101:6">shall minister to me. <verse eid="PSA 101:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 101:7"/>There shall not dwell within my house </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 101:7">one working deceit; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 101:7">the one speaking lies </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 101:7">shall not be fixed before my eyes. <verse eid="PSA 101:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 101:8"/>At morning I cut off all the wicked of the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 101:8">to cut off from the city of YHWH all workers of iniquity! <verse eid="PSA 101:8"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 101"/>

<chapter number="102" style="c" sid="PSA 102"/>

<para style="s">The Prayer of the Afflicted</para>

<para style="s">A Prayer of one afflicted, when he grows weak and pours out his complaint before YHWH.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 102:1"/> O YHWH, may You hear my prayer </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:1">and may my cry come to You! <verse eid="PSA 102:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 102:2"/>Do not hide Your face from me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:2">in the day of distress for me! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 102:2">Incline to me Your ear; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:2">on the day <char style="add">that</char> I call may You hurry and answer me! <verse eid="PSA 102:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 102:3"/>For my days come to an end like smoke, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:3">and my bones like a burning <char style="add">wick</char> have been charred. <verse eid="PSA 102:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 102:4"/>My heart has been struck like the grass and has withered, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:4"><char style="add">so</char> that I forget to eat my bread. <verse eid="PSA 102:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 102:5"/>From the voice of my groaning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:5">my bone has clung to my flesh. <verse eid="PSA 102:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 102:6"/>I am like a vulture of the desert; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:6">I have become like an owl of the wasteland. <verse eid="PSA 102:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 102:7"/>I stay awake, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:7">and I am like a bird alone on the housetop. <verse eid="PSA 102:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 102:8"/>All the day my enemies the taunt me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:8">those shouting boastfully swear against me. <verse eid="PSA 102:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 102:9"/>For I have eaten ashes like bread, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:9">and my drink I have mingled with weeping, <verse eid="PSA 102:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 102:10"/>from the face of Your anger and Your wrath, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:10">for You have lifted me up and cast me away. <verse eid="PSA 102:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 102:11"/>My days <char style="add">are</char> like a shadow stretching out; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:11">and I, like the grass, wither away. <verse eid="PSA 102:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 102:12"/>But You, O YHWH, dwell forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:12">and Your memorial to generation and generation. <verse eid="PSA 102:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 102:13"/>You will rise up <char style="add">and</char> have compassion <char style="add">on</char> Zion—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:13">for the time to show her favor, indeed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:13">the appointed time, has come. <verse eid="PSA 102:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 102:14"/>How Your servants take delight <char style="add">in</char> her stones—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:14">even her dust they favor! <verse eid="PSA 102:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 102:15"/>And the nations will fear the name of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:15">and all the kings of the earth Your glory. <verse eid="PSA 102:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 102:16"/>For YHWH has built up Zion; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:16">He has appeared in His glory. <verse eid="PSA 102:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 102:17"/>He has turned toward the prayer of the destitute, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:17">and He will not despise their prayer. <verse eid="PSA 102:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 102:18"/>This will be written for the generation to come, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:18">and a people yet to be created will praise YAH. <verse eid="PSA 102:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 102:19"/>For He looked down from the height of His sanctuary, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:19">YHWH looked out from the heavens to the earth, <verse eid="PSA 102:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 102:20"/>to hear the groaning of the prisoner, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:20">to release the sons of death; <verse eid="PSA 102:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 102:21"/>to declare in Zion the name of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:21">and His praise in Jerusalem, <verse eid="PSA 102:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 102:22"/>in the gathering of the peoples together—and the kingdoms—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:22">to serve YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 102:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 102:23"/>He has broken my strength on the way; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:23">He has shortened my days. <verse eid="PSA 102:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 102:24"/>I said, “O my God, do not take me up in the midst of my days; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:24">Your years <char style="add">are</char> generation <char style="add">to</char> generations. <verse eid="PSA 102:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 102:25"/>Before time You founded the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:25">and the heavens <char style="add">are</char> the work of Your hands. <verse eid="PSA 102:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 102:26"/>They will perish, but You will stand; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:26">and all of them will wear out like a garment—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 102:26">like clothing, You will pass them on, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:26">and they will pass away. <verse eid="PSA 102:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 102:27"/>And You are the same, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:27">and Your years will not end. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">102.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Hebrews 1:10–12</char></note><verse eid="PSA 102:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 102:28"/>The sons of Your servants will settle down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 102:28">and their seed will be established before Your face.” <verse eid="PSA 102:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 102"/>

<chapter number="103" style="c" sid="PSA 103"/>

<para style="s">Bless Yahweh, O My Soul</para>

<para style="s">Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 103:1"/> Bless, O my soul, YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:1">and all within me—His holy name! <verse eid="PSA 103:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 103:2"/>O my soul, bless YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:2">and do not forget all His benefits— <verse eid="PSA 103:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 103:3"/>the One forgiving all your iniquities, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:3">the One healing all your diseases, <verse eid="PSA 103:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 103:4"/>the One redeeming your life from destruction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:4">the One crowning you with loving devotion and compassion, <verse eid="PSA 103:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 103:5"/>the One filling your beauty with the good; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:5">your youth is renewed like the eagle. <verse eid="PSA 103:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 103:6"/>YHWH is doing righteousness </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:6">and justice for all being oppressed. <verse eid="PSA 103:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 103:7"/>He made known His ways to Moses, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:7">His deeds to the sons of Israel. <verse eid="PSA 103:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 103:8"/>Compassionate and gracious <char style="add">is</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:8">slow <char style="add">to</char> anger and abounding <char style="add">in</char> loving devotion. <verse eid="PSA 103:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 103:9"/>He will not contend forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:9">and He will not keep <char style="add">it</char> forever. <verse eid="PSA 103:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 103:10"/>He has not done to us according to our sins, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:10">and He has not dealt with us according to our iniquities. <verse eid="PSA 103:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 103:11"/>For as the heavens are high above the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:11"><char style="add">so</char> His loving devotion is mighty for those fearing Him. <verse eid="PSA 103:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 103:12"/>As far as the east <char style="add">is</char> from the west, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:12"><char style="add">so</char> has He put our transgressions far from us. <verse eid="PSA 103:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 103:13"/>As a father has compassion for <char style="add">his</char> children, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:13"><char style="add">so</char> YHWH has compassion for those fearing Him. <verse eid="PSA 103:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 103:14"/>For He knows our form; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:14">He remembers that we <char style="add">are</char> dust. <verse eid="PSA 103:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 103:15"/>A man—his days <char style="add">are</char> like grass; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:15">like the flower of the field, so he blossoms; <verse eid="PSA 103:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 103:16"/>For the wind passes over it, and it is no more; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:16">and its place does not recognize it anymore. <verse eid="PSA 103:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 103:17"/>But the loving devotion of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> from forever and even to forever </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:17">upon those fearing Him, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 103:17">and His righteousness to the sons of the sons— <verse eid="PSA 103:17"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 103:18"/>to those keeping His covenant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:18">and to those remembering His precepts, to do them. <verse eid="PSA 103:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 103:19"/>YHWH has established His throne in the heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:19">and His kingdom rules over all. <verse eid="PSA 103:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 103:20"/>Bless YHWH, His angels, mighty of strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:20">doing His word, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:20">to listen to the voice of His word. <verse eid="PSA 103:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 103:21"/>Bless YHWH, all His hosts, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:21">His ministering ones doing His pleasure. <verse eid="PSA 103:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 103:22"/>Bless YHWH, all His works, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 103:22">in all places of His dominion. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 103:22">O my soul, bless YHWH! <verse eid="PSA 103:22"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 103"/>

<chapter number="104" style="c" sid="PSA 104"/>

<para style="s">How Many Are Your Works, O LORD!</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 104:1"/>O my soul, bless YHWH! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 104:1">O YHWH my God, You are very great; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:1">with honor and majesty You are clothed. <verse eid="PSA 104:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 104:2"/>Covering Himself <char style="add">with</char> light as a garment, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:2">stretching out the heavens like a curtain, <verse eid="PSA 104:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 104:3"/>the One laying the beams in the waters </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:3">of His upper chambers, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 104:3">the One making the clouds His chariot, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:3">the One walking on the wings of the wind, <verse eid="PSA 104:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 104:4"/>making the winds His messengers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:4">His servants flaming fire. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">104.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He makes His angels winds, His servants flames of fire.</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Hebrews 1:7</char></note><verse eid="PSA 104:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 104:5"/>He set the earth upon <char style="add">its</char> foundations; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:5">it should not be shaken forever and ever. <verse eid="PSA 104:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 104:6"/>The deep, as <char style="add">with</char> a garment You covered it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:6">upon the mountains the waters were standing. <verse eid="PSA 104:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 104:7"/>From Your rebuke they fled; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:7">from the voice of Your thunder they hurried away. <verse eid="PSA 104:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 104:8"/>Upon the mountains, the valleys sank down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:8">to the place that You established for them. <verse eid="PSA 104:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 104:9"/>You have set a boundary <char style="add">that</char> they may not cross over; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:9">they may never return to cover the earth. <verse eid="PSA 104:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 104:10"/>He sends the springs into the valleys; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:10">they flow between the hills. <verse eid="PSA 104:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 104:11"/>They give drink to every beast of the field; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:11">the wild donkeys break their thirst. <verse eid="PSA 104:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 104:12"/>Nearby them the birds of the heavens are dwelling; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:12">from between the branches they give forth a voice. <verse eid="PSA 104:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 104:13"/>Watering the hills from His upper chambers; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:13">with the fruit of Your works the earth is satisfied— <verse eid="PSA 104:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 104:14"/>causing the grass to sprout for the cattle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:14">and vegetation for the service of man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:14">to bring forth food from the earth, <verse eid="PSA 104:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 104:15"/>and wine makes glad the heart of man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:15">to make <char style="add">his</char> face shine from oil, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:15">and bread supports the heart of man. <verse eid="PSA 104:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 104:16"/>The trees of YHWH are satisfied, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:16">the cedars of Lebanon that He planted, <verse eid="PSA 104:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 104:17"/>where in the birds make their nests; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:17">the stork—the cypresses<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">104.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">pines</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">junipers</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">firs</char></note> <char style="add">are</char> her house. <verse eid="PSA 104:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 104:18"/>The high mountains <char style="add">are</char> for the wild goats; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:18">the crags a refuge for the rock badgers.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">104.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the coneys</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the hyraxes</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 104:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 104:19"/>He made the moon for appointed times; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:19">the sun knows its entrance. <verse eid="PSA 104:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 104:20"/>You make darkness, and it becomes night; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:20">in it all the living <char style="add">things</char> of the forest creep about. <verse eid="PSA 104:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 104:21"/>The young lions roar for the prey </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:21">and seek their food from God. <verse eid="PSA 104:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 104:22"/>The sun rises, they are gathered; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:22">and in their dens they stretch out. <verse eid="PSA 104:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 104:23"/>Man goes out to his work, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:23">and to his labor until the evening. <verse eid="PSA 104:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 104:24"/>How many are Your works, O YHWH! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:24">All of them You have made in wisdom; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:24">the earth is full of Your creatures. <verse eid="PSA 104:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 104:25"/>This <char style="add">is</char> the sea, great and wide—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:25">in it <char style="add">are</char> teeming things, and without number, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:25">living things small with the great. <verse eid="PSA 104:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 104:26"/>There the ships go about, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:26"><char style="add">and</char> Leviathan, which You formed to play in it. <verse eid="PSA 104:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 104:27"/>All of them look to You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:27">to give their food, in its season. <verse eid="PSA 104:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 104:28"/>You give to them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:28"><char style="add">and</char> they gather in; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 104:28">You open Your hand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:28"><char style="add">and</char> they are satisfied <char style="add">with</char> good. <verse eid="PSA 104:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 104:29"/>You hide Your face—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:29">they are troubled; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 104:29">You gather their spirit—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:29">they die, and to their dust they return. <verse eid="PSA 104:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 104:30"/>You send forth Your Spirit<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">104.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">breath</char></note>—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:30">they are created, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 104:30">and You renew </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:30">the face of the earth. <verse eid="PSA 104:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 104:31"/>May the glory of YHWH be forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:31">may YHWH rejoice in His works— <verse eid="PSA 104:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 104:32"/>the One looking on the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:32">and it trembles; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 104:32">He touches the mountains, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:32">and they smoke. <verse eid="PSA 104:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 104:33"/>I will sing to YHWH during my life; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:33">I will sing praise to my God while I <char style="add">live</char>! <verse eid="PSA 104:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 104:34"/>May my melody be pleasing to Him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:34">I rejoice in YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 104:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 104:35"/>May the sinful ones be consumed from the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 104:35">and the wicked shall not be anymore! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 104:35">O my soul, bless YHWH! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 104:35">Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">104.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 104:35"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 104"/>

<chapter number="105" style="c" sid="PSA 105"/>

<para style="s">Tell of His Wonders</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 105:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Chronicles 16:7–22</char></note>Give thanks to YHWH; call on His name; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:1">make known among the nations His deeds! <verse eid="PSA 105:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 105:2"/>Sing to Him, make music to Him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:2">meditate on all His wonders! <verse eid="PSA 105:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 105:3"/>Glory in the name of His holiness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:3">let the heart of those seeking YHWH rejoice! <verse eid="PSA 105:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 105:4"/>Search after YHWH and His strength; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:4">seek His face continually. <verse eid="PSA 105:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 105:5"/>Remember His wonders that He has done—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:5">His wonders and the judgments of His mouth— <verse eid="PSA 105:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 105:6"/>O seed of Abraham His servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:6">O sons of Jacob, His chosen ones! <verse eid="PSA 105:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 105:7"/>He <char style="add">is</char> YHWH our God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:7">His judgments <char style="add">are</char> over all the earth. <verse eid="PSA 105:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 105:8"/>He remembers His covenant forever—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:8">the word He commanded for a thousand generations— <verse eid="PSA 105:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 105:9"/>that which He cut with Abraham, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:9">and His oath to Isaac. <verse eid="PSA 105:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 105:10"/>And He established it to Jacob as a decree, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:10">to Israel <char style="add">as</char> a covenant forever, <verse eid="PSA 105:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 105:11"/>saying, “To you I will give the land of Canaan, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:11">the portion of your⁺ inheritance.” <verse eid="PSA 105:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 105:12"/>In their being few in number, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:12">few indeed, and strangers in it, <verse eid="PSA 105:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 105:13"/>and they went about from nation to nation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:13">from a kingdom to another people. <verse eid="PSA 105:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 105:14"/>He has permitted no man to oppress them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:14">and He rebuked kings for them: <verse eid="PSA 105:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 105:15"/>“You⁺ shall not touch My anointed ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:15">and to My prophets You⁺ shall not do evil.” <verse eid="PSA 105:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 105:16"/>And He called down famine on the land; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:16">the whole staff of bread He has broken. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">105.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">supply</char></note><verse eid="PSA 105:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 105:17"/>He sent before them a man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:17"><char style="add">to</char> be sold as a slave—Joseph. <verse eid="PSA 105:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 105:18"/>They afflicted his feet with the fetters; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:18"><char style="add">into</char> iron came his neck, <verse eid="PSA 105:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 105:19"/>until the time of the coming of His word—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:19">the word of YHWH tried him. <verse eid="PSA 105:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 105:20"/>The king sent and released him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:20">and the ruler of the peoples drew him out. <verse eid="PSA 105:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 105:21"/>He made him lord of his house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:21">and ruler of all his substance, <verse eid="PSA 105:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 105:22"/>to instruct<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">105.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX and Syriac; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to bind</char></note> his princes by his soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:22">and his elders to make wise. <verse eid="PSA 105:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 105:23"/>And Israel came to Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:23">and Jacob resided in the land of Ham. <verse eid="PSA 105:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 105:24"/>And His people He made exceedingly fruitful, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:24">and made them mightier than their enemies. <verse eid="PSA 105:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 105:25"/>He turned their heart to hate His people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:25">to act deceitfully with His servants. <verse eid="PSA 105:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 105:26"/>He sent Moses His servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:26">Aaron whom He had chosen. <verse eid="PSA 105:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 105:27"/>They set among them the words of His signs, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:27">and wonders in the land of Ham. <verse eid="PSA 105:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 105:28"/>He sent darkness and it became dark, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:28">and they defied His words.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">105.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX and Syriac; Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for had they not defied His words?</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 105:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 105:29"/>He turned their waters to blood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:29">and He put to death their fish. <verse eid="PSA 105:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 105:30"/>Their land swarmed with frogs, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:30">in the inner chambers of their kings. <verse eid="PSA 105:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 105:31"/>He spoke, and the swarm came, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:31">gnats in all their country. <verse eid="PSA 105:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 105:32"/>He gave hail for rain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:32">flames of fire in their land. <verse eid="PSA 105:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 105:33"/>And He struck their vines and their fig trees, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:33">and He shattered the trees of their country. <verse eid="PSA 105:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 105:34"/>He spoke, and the locust came, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:34">and the young locust without number, <verse eid="PSA 105:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 105:35"/>and it ate up every herb in their land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:35">and it devoured the fruit of their ground. <verse eid="PSA 105:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 105:36"/>And He struck all the firstborn in their land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:36">the firstfruits of all their vigor. <verse eid="PSA 105:36"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 105:37"/>And He brought them out with silver and gold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:37">and there were none among His tribes stumbling. <verse eid="PSA 105:37"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 105:38"/>Egypt was glad at their going out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:38">for the dread of them had fallen upon them. <verse eid="PSA 105:38"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 105:39"/>He spread a cloud for a screen, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:39">and fire to light up the night. <verse eid="PSA 105:39"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 105:40"/>They asked, and He brought quail, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:40">and with the bread of the heavens He satisfied them. <verse eid="PSA 105:40"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 105:41"/>He opened the rock, and waters gushed from it; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:41">they went forth in the desert like a river. <verse eid="PSA 105:41"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 105:42"/>For He remembered the word of His holiness to Abraham </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:42">His servant. <verse eid="PSA 105:42"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 105:43"/>And He brought out His people with rejoicing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:43"><char style="add">and</char> His chosen with a shout of joy. <verse eid="PSA 105:43"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 105:44"/>And He gave to them the lands of the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:44">and they possessed the labor of the peoples, <verse eid="PSA 105:44"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 105:45"/>that they may keep His statutes </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 105:45">and obey His laws. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 105:45">Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">105.45 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 105:45"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 105"/>

<chapter number="106" style="c" sid="PSA 106"/>

<para style="s">Give Thanks to Yahweh, for He Is Good</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 106:1"/>Hallelujah!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">106.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelujah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 48</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 106:1">Give thanks to YHWH for <char style="add">He is</char> good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:1">for His loving devotion <char style="add">is</char> forever! <verse eid="PSA 106:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 106:2"/>Who can describe the mighty acts of YHWH? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:2">Who can sound all His praise? <verse eid="PSA 106:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 106:3"/>Blessed <char style="add">are</char> those guarding justice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:3">doing righteousness at every time. <verse eid="PSA 106:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 106:4"/>Remember me, O YHWH, in favor <char style="add">to</char> Your people; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:4">attend to me with Your salvation, <verse eid="PSA 106:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 106:5"/>to look on the prosperity of Your chosen ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:5"><char style="add">and</char> to be glad in the gladness of Your nation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:5"><char style="add">and</char> to glory with Your inheritance. <verse eid="PSA 106:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 106:6"/>We have sinned, with our fathers; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:6">we have been perverse; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:6">we have acted wickedly. <verse eid="PSA 106:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 106:7"/>Our fathers in Egypt did not consider Your wonders; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:7">they did not remember the abundance of Your kindness; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 106:7">and they rebelled by the sea—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:7">at the Sea of Reeds.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">106.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Sea of Reeds</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 9 and 22</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 106:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 106:8"/>And He saved them for the sake of His name, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:8">to make known His might. <verse eid="PSA 106:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 106:9"/>And He rebuked the Sea of Reeds, and it dried up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:9">and He made them walk through the depths as through a desert. <verse eid="PSA 106:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 106:10"/>And He saved them from the hand of the one hating, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:10">and He redeemed them from the hand of the enemy. <verse eid="PSA 106:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 106:11"/>For the waters covered their enemies; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:11">not one of them remained. <verse eid="PSA 106:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 106:12"/>And they had faith in His words; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:12">they sang His praise. <verse eid="PSA 106:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 106:13"/>They were quick to forget His works; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:13">they have not wait for His counsel; <verse eid="PSA 106:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 106:14"/>and they craved with desire in the wilderness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:14">and they tested God in the desert. <verse eid="PSA 106:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 106:15"/>And He gave to them their request, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:15">and He sent leanness upon their soul. <verse eid="PSA 106:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 106:16"/>And they were jealous of Moses in the camp, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:16">of Aaron, the holy one of YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 106:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 106:17"/>The earth opened up and swallowed Dathan, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:17">and it covered over the company of Abiram. <verse eid="PSA 106:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 106:18"/>And a fire was kindled in their company; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:18">the flame consumed the wicked. <verse eid="PSA 106:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 106:19"/>They made a calf in Horeb,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">106.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Mount Sinai, or possibly a mountain in the range containing Mount Sinai</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:19">and they bowed down to a molten image. <verse eid="PSA 106:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 106:20"/>And they exchanged their Glory<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">106.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">their glorious God</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:20">for the image of an ox eating grass. <verse eid="PSA 106:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 106:21"/>They forgot God their Savior, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:21">the One having done great <char style="add">things</char> in Egypt, <verse eid="PSA 106:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 106:22"/>wonders in the land of Ham, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:22">fearful <char style="add">things</char> by the Sea of Reeds. <verse eid="PSA 106:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 106:23"/>And he said he would destroy them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:23">had not Moses his chosen one </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 106:23">stood in the breach before His face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:23">to turn away His fury from destroying them. <verse eid="PSA 106:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 106:24"/>Then they despised the land of the desire; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:24">they were not faithful to His word, <verse eid="PSA 106:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 106:25"/>and they grumbled in their tents; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:25">they did not listen to the voice of YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 106:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 106:26"/>And He lifted up His hand against them </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:26">to make them fall in the desert, <verse eid="PSA 106:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 106:27"/>and to make their seed fall<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">106.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to disperse their seed</char></note> among the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:27">and to scatter them in the lands. <verse eid="PSA 106:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 106:28"/>They even joined themselves <char style="add">to</char> Baal-Peor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:28">and they ate sacrifices to the dead. <verse eid="PSA 106:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 106:29"/>And they provoked <char style="add">Him</char> to anger with their deeds, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:29">and a plague broke out among them. <verse eid="PSA 106:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 106:30"/>And Phinehas stood up and intervened, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:30">and the plague was restrained. <verse eid="PSA 106:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 106:31"/>And it was reckoned to him as righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:31">to generation and generation, even to forever. <verse eid="PSA 106:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 106:32"/>And they caused wrath at the waters of Meribah,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">106.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Meribah</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">quarreling</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Exodus 17:7.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:32">and it was evil to Moses on account of them. <verse eid="PSA 106:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 106:33"/>For they rebelled against his spirit,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">106.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they provoked His Spirit</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:33">and he spoke rashly with his lips. <verse eid="PSA 106:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 106:34"/>They did not destroy the peoples </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:34">whom YHWH had given to them the order. <verse eid="PSA 106:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 106:35"/>And they mingled with the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:35">and they learned their works. <verse eid="PSA 106:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 106:36"/>And they served their idols, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:36">and they were to them as a snare. <verse eid="PSA 106:36"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 106:37"/>And they sacrificed their sons </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:37">and their daughters to the demons; <verse eid="PSA 106:37"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 106:38"/>and they shed innocent blood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:38">the blood of their sons and their daughters, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 106:38">whom they sacrificed to the idols of Canaan, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:38">and the land was polluted with the blood. <verse eid="PSA 106:38"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 106:39"/>And they were defiled by their deeds </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:39">and prostituted themselves by their practices. <verse eid="PSA 106:39"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 106:40"/>And the anger of YHWH was kindled against His people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:40">and He came to abhor His inheritance. <verse eid="PSA 106:40"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 106:41"/>And He gave them into the hand of the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:41">and those hating them ruled over them. <verse eid="PSA 106:41"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 106:42"/>And their enemies oppressed them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:42">and they were humbled under their hand. <verse eid="PSA 106:42"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 106:43"/>Many times He delivered them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:43">and they were rebellious in their counsel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:43">and were brought low in their iniquity. <verse eid="PSA 106:43"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 106:44"/>And He looked on the distress to them </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:44">in His hearing their cry. <verse eid="PSA 106:44"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 106:45"/>And He remembered unto them His covenant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:45">and He relented by the abundance of His loving devotion. <verse eid="PSA 106:45"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 106:46"/>And He appointed them for mercies </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:46">before the face of all their captors. <verse eid="PSA 106:46"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 106:47"/>Save us, O YHWH our God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:47">and gather us from the nations, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 106:47">to give thanks to the name of Your holiness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:47">to glory in Your praise! <verse eid="PSA 106:47"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 106:48"/>Blessed <char style="add">be</char> YHWH the God of Israel </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 106:48">from forever and even to forever. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 106:48">And let all the people say, “Amen!” </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 106:48">Praise YAH! <verse eid="PSA 106:48"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 106"/>

<chapter number="107" style="c" sid="PSA 107"/>

<para style="s">BOOK V</para>

<para style="s">Psalms 107–150</para>

<para style="s">Thanksgiving for Deliverance</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 107:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 8:22–25</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Mark 4:35–41</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 8:23–27</char></note>Give thanks to YHWH, for <char style="add">He is</char> good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:1">for His loving devotion <char style="add">is</char> forever! <verse eid="PSA 107:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 107:2"/>Let the redeemed of YHWH say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:2">whom He has redeemed from the hand of the enemy, <verse eid="PSA 107:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 107:3"/>and from the lands He has gathered them—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:3">from the east and from the west, from the north and from the sea.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">107.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from the north and from the south</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 107:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 107:4"/>They wandered in the wilderness, by the way in a desert; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:4">a city for of dwelling they did not find. <verse eid="PSA 107:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 107:5"/>Hungry and thirsty, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:5">their soul in them grew faint. <verse eid="PSA 107:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 107:6"/>And they cried out to YHWH in the distress for them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:6">from their straits He delivered them. <verse eid="PSA 107:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 107:7"/>And He made them tread on a straight path, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:7">to walk toward a city of dwelling. <verse eid="PSA 107:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 107:8"/>Let them give thanks to YHWH for His loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:8">and His wonders to the sons of man! <verse eid="PSA 107:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 107:9"/>For He satisfies the rushing soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:9">and the hungry soul He fills with goodness. <verse eid="PSA 107:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 107:10"/>They are sitting in darkness and in the shadow of death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:10">prisoners in affliction and irons, <verse eid="PSA 107:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 107:11"/>because they rebelled against the words of God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:11">and they despised the counsel of the Most High, <verse eid="PSA 107:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 107:12"/>and He humbled with labor their heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:12">they fell down, and no one was helping. <verse eid="PSA 107:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 107:13"/>And they cried out to YHWH in the distress for them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:13"><char style="add">and</char> from their straits He saved them. <verse eid="PSA 107:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 107:14"/>He brought them forth from darkness and the shadow of death, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:14">and their bonds He broke away. <verse eid="PSA 107:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 107:15"/>Let them give thanks to the LORD for His loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:15">and His wonders to the sons of man! <verse eid="PSA 107:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 107:16"/>For He has broken down doors of bronze, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:16">and He has cut through bars of iron! <verse eid="PSA 107:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 107:17"/>Fools from the path of their transgression, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:17">and by their iniquities they were afflicted. <verse eid="PSA 107:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 107:18"/>All food their soul abhorred, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:18">and they drew near to the gates of death. <verse eid="PSA 107:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 107:19"/>And they cried out to YHWH in the distress for them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:19"><char style="add">and</char> from their straits He saved them. <verse eid="PSA 107:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 107:20"/>He sent His word and healed them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:20">and He rescued them from the Pit. <verse eid="PSA 107:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 107:21"/>Let them give thanks to the LORD for His loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:21">and His wonders to the sons of man! <verse eid="PSA 107:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 107:22"/>And let them sacrifice sacrifices of thanksgiving, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:22">and recount His works with rejoicing! <verse eid="PSA 107:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 107:23"/>Those going down to the sea in ships, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:23">doing business on the great waters, <verse eid="PSA 107:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 107:24"/>they have seen the works of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:24">and His wonders in the deep. <verse eid="PSA 107:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 107:25"/>And He spoke and stationed the wind, a tempest, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:25">and it lifted high the waves; <verse eid="PSA 107:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 107:26"/>they went up <char style="add">to</char> the heavens, they went down <char style="add">to</char> the depths; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:26">their soul melted in evil. <verse eid="PSA 107:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 107:27"/>They reel and stagger like the drunkard, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:27">and all their wisdom is swallowed up.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">107.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and all their skill was useless</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and they were at their wits’ end</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 107:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 107:28"/>And they cried out to YHWH in the distress for them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:28">and from their straits He brought them out. <verse eid="PSA 107:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 107:29"/>He stilled the tempest to a whisper, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:29">and the waves of the sea<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">107.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> DSS; MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">their waves</char></note> were hushed. <verse eid="PSA 107:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 107:30"/>And they rejoiced because they grew quiet, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:30">and He guided them to the haven of their desire. <verse eid="PSA 107:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 107:31"/>Let them give thanks to the LORD for His loving devotion </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:31">and His wonders to the sons of man! <verse eid="PSA 107:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 107:32"/>And let them exalt Him in the assembly of the people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:32">and in the seat of the elders praise Him! <verse eid="PSA 107:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 107:33"/>He turns rivers into a wilderness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:33">and outpourings of waters into thirsty ground, <verse eid="PSA 107:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 107:34"/>a land of fruit into salty ground, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:34">from the wickedness of those dwelling in it. <verse eid="PSA 107:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 107:35"/>He turns the desert into pools of water, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:35">and a land of dryness into springs of waters. <verse eid="PSA 107:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 107:36"/>And the hungry He makes to dwell there, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:36">that they may establish a city for a dwelling place. <verse eid="PSA 107:36"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 107:37"/>And there they sow fields and plant vineyards, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:37">that they may yield the fruit of produce. <verse eid="PSA 107:37"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 107:38"/>And He blesses them and they multiply exceedingly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:38">and their cattle He does not let diminish. <verse eid="PSA 107:38"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 107:39"/>When they are diminished and brought low </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:39">from oppression, evil, and sorrow, <verse eid="PSA 107:39"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 107:40"/>He pours out contempt on nobles, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:40">and causes them to wander in a wasteland without a path. <verse eid="PSA 107:40"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 107:41"/>And He sets on high <char style="add">for</char> the needy from affliction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:41">and He places families as a flock. <verse eid="PSA 107:41"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 107:42"/>Let the upright see and rejoice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:42">and may all iniquity shut its mouth. <verse eid="PSA 107:42"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 107:43"/>And <char style="add">him</char> who <char style="add">is</char> wise, let him attend to these things, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 107:43">and they will consider the loving devotion of YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 107:43"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 107"/>

<chapter number="108" style="c" sid="PSA 108"/>

<para style="s">Israel’s Kingdom Blessing</para>

<para style="s">A Song. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 108:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 60:1–12</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 57:1–11</char></note> My heart being firm, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:1">I will sing and make music, even with my glory!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">108.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with all my being</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 108:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 108:2"/>Awake, O harp and lyre! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:2">I will awaken the dawn! <verse eid="PSA 108:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 108:3"/>I will praise You among the peoples, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:3">and I will sing praises to You among the nations. <verse eid="PSA 108:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 108:4"/>For great over the heavens <char style="add">is</char> Your loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:4">and up to the clouds <char style="add">is</char> Your faithfulness. <verse eid="PSA 108:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 108:5"/>Be exalted above the heavens, O God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:5">and over all the earth Your glory! <verse eid="PSA 108:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 108:6"/>That Your beloved may be delivered, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:6">save <char style="add">with</char> Your right hand, and answer me! <verse eid="PSA 108:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 108:7"/>God has spoken from His holy place:<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">108.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in His holiness</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from His sanctuary</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:7">“I will exult; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 108:7">I will divide Shechem, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:7">and measure out the Valley of Succoth. <verse eid="PSA 108:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 108:8"/>Unto Me <char style="add">is</char> Gilead, unto Me <char style="add">is</char> Manasseh; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:8">and Ephraim <char style="add">is</char> the strength of My head, Judah <char style="add">is</char> My scepter. <verse eid="PSA 108:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 108:9"/>Moab <char style="add">is</char> the basin of My washing; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:9">upon Edom I will cast My sandal; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:9">over Philistia I will shout in triumph.” <verse eid="PSA 108:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 108:10"/>Who will bring me to the fortified city? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:10">Who will lead me as far as Edom? <verse eid="PSA 108:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 108:11"/>Have You not, O God, cast us off? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:11">And will You no longer go forth, O God, with our armies? <verse eid="PSA 108:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 108:12"/>May You give to us help from adversity, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:12">and the salvation of man <char style="add">is</char> emptiness. <verse eid="PSA 108:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 108:13"/>With God we will act <char style="add">in</char> strength, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 108:13">and He will trample our adversaries. <verse eid="PSA 108:13"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 108"/>

<chapter number="109" style="c" sid="PSA 109"/>

<para style="s">The Song of the Slandered</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 109:1"/> O God of my praise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:1">do not be silent! <verse eid="PSA 109:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 109:2"/>For the mouth of the wicked and the mouth of the deceitful, they have opened against me—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:2">they speak against me with a tongue of lies; <verse eid="PSA 109:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 109:3"/>and with words of hatred they surround me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:3">and they fight me without cause. <verse eid="PSA 109:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 109:4"/>In exchange for my love they accuse me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:4">and I <char style="add">am</char> of prayer; <verse eid="PSA 109:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 109:5"/>and they set against me evil for good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:5">and hatred for my love. <verse eid="PSA 109:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 109:6"/>Appoint a wicked man over him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:6">and let an adversary stand at his right hand. <verse eid="PSA 109:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 109:7"/>In his being judged, may he go forth <char style="add">as</char> wicked, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:7">and let his prayer come to be as sin. <verse eid="PSA 109:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 109:8"/>May his days be few; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:8">may another take his position! <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">109.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Acts 1:20</char></note><verse eid="PSA 109:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 109:9"/>May his sons be fatherless, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:9">and his wife a widow. <verse eid="PSA 109:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 109:10"/>And let his sons wander continually and beg, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:10">and let them seek sustenance<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">109.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew; LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">let them be driven</char></note> from their desolate places! <verse eid="PSA 109:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 109:11"/>Let the creditor lay a snare for all that <char style="add">is</char> unto him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:11">and let strangers plunder his labour. <verse eid="PSA 109:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 109:12"/>None shall there be for him extending kindness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:12">and none shall there be showing favor to his fatherless. <verse eid="PSA 109:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 109:13"/>Let his posterity be for cutting off; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:13">in the next generation let their name be blotted out! <verse eid="PSA 109:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 109:14"/>May the iniquity of his fathers be remembered to YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:14">and the sin of his mother not be blotted out. <verse eid="PSA 109:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 109:15"/>Let them be before YHWH continually, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:15">that He may cut off from the earth their memory! <verse eid="PSA 109:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 109:16"/>Because that he has not remembered to do kindness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:16">and he pursued the poor and needy man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:16">and the broken of heart to kill <char style="add">him</char>. <verse eid="PSA 109:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 109:17"/>And he loved cursing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:17">and let it come to him; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 109:17">and he did not delight in blessing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:17">and let it be far from him! <verse eid="PSA 109:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 109:18"/>And he clothed himself with cursing as his garment, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:18">and it came in like the water within him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:18">and like the oil into his bones! <verse eid="PSA 109:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 109:19"/>May it be for him like the garment wrapped about him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:19">and continually as a belt he girds on. <verse eid="PSA 109:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 109:20"/>May this be the reward of my accusers from YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:20">and of those speaking evil against my soul! <verse eid="PSA 109:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 109:21"/>But You, O YHWH my Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:21">may you act with me for the sake of Your name; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:21">because of the goodness of Your loving devotion, deliver me! <verse eid="PSA 109:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 109:22"/>For I <char style="add">am</char> poor and needy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:22">and my heart is pierced within me. <verse eid="PSA 109:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 109:23"/>Like a shadow in its lengthening, I am gone; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:23">I am shaken off like the locust. <verse eid="PSA 109:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 109:24"/>My knees wobble from fasting, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:24">and my flesh has failed of fatness. <verse eid="PSA 109:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 109:25"/>And I have become an object of scorn for them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:25">they see me; they shake their head. <verse eid="PSA 109:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 109:26"/>Help me, O YHWH my God; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:26">save me according to Your loving devotion, <verse eid="PSA 109:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 109:27"/>that they may know that this <char style="add">is</char> Your hand; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:27">You, O YHWH, have done it! <verse eid="PSA 109:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 109:28"/>They may curse, but You will bless; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:28">may they rise up, and be put to shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:28">and may Your servant rejoice! <verse eid="PSA 109:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 109:29"/>May my accusers be clothed with disgrace, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:29">and may they be covered with their shame as the robe. <verse eid="PSA 109:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 109:30"/>I will confess YHWH greatly with my mouth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:30">and in the midst of the multitudes I will praise Him. <verse eid="PSA 109:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 109:31"/>For He shall stand at the right hand of the poor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 109:31">to save <char style="add">him</char> from those judging his soul. <verse eid="PSA 109:31"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 109"/>

<chapter number="110" style="c" sid="PSA 110"/>

<para style="s">God’s Faithful Messiah</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 110:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Hebrews 5:1–10</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Genesis 14:17–24</char></note> An utterance of YHWH to my Lord: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 110:1">“Sit at My right hand, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 110:1">until I make your enemies </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 110:1">a footstool for Your feet.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">110.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Matthew 22:44, Mark 12:36, Luke 20:42–43, Acts 2:34–35, and Hebrews 1:13</char></note>” <verse eid="PSA 110:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 110:2"/>YHWH sends forth the rod of your strength from Zion: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 110:2">“Rule in the midst of Your enemies!” <verse eid="PSA 110:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 110:3"/>Your people <char style="add">are</char> freewill offerings </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 110:3">in the day of your might, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 110:3">in the splendors of holiness; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 110:3">from the womb of the morning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 110:3">the dew of your youth <char style="add">is</char> unto you. <verse eid="PSA 110:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 110:4"/>YHWH has sworn, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 110:4">and He will not change His mind: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 110:4">“You <char style="add">are</char> a priest forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 110:4">according to the order of Melchizedek.” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">110.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Hebrews 5:6, Hebrews 7:17, and Hebrews 7:21</char></note><verse eid="PSA 110:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 110:5"/>My Lord <char style="add">is</char> at Your right hand; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 110:5">he will shatter kings in the day of his anger; <verse eid="PSA 110:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 110:6"/>He will judge among the nations, he will fill it with corpses; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 110:6">he will wound the head of many lands; <verse eid="PSA 110:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 110:7"/>from the brook by the way He will drink. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 110:7">By this He will lift up the head. <verse eid="PSA 110:7"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 110"/>

<chapter number="111" style="c" sid="PSA 111"/>

<para style="s">Majestic Is His Work</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 111:1"/>Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">111.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char><char style="ft" closed="false">. This psalm is an acrostic poem, each line beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 111:1">I will give thanks to YHWH with all of <char style="add">my</char> heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 111:1">in the council of the upright and in the assembly. <verse eid="PSA 111:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 111:2"/>Great <char style="add">are</char> the works of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 111:2">being searched out by all <char style="add">who</char> delight in them. <verse eid="PSA 111:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 111:3"/>Splendor and majesty <char style="add">are</char> His work, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 111:3">and His righteousness stands forever. <verse eid="PSA 111:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 111:4"/>A memorial He has made by His wonders; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 111:4">gracious and compassionate <char style="add">is</char> YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 111:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 111:5"/>Food He has given to those fearing Him; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 111:5">He remembers His covenant forever. <verse eid="PSA 111:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 111:6"/>The power of His works He has declared to His people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 111:6">by giving to them the inheritance of the nations. <verse eid="PSA 111:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 111:7"/>The works of His hands <char style="add">are</char> truth and justice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 111:7"><char style="add">and</char> all His precepts are trustworthy. <verse eid="PSA 111:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 111:8"/>They are upheld for ever everlasting; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 111:8">they are made in truth and uprightness. <verse eid="PSA 111:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 111:9"/>Redemption He has sent to His people; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 111:9">He has appointed His covenant forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 111:9">Holy and awesome <char style="add">is</char> His name! <verse eid="PSA 111:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 111:10"/>The beginning of wisdom <char style="add">is</char> the fear of YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 111:10">good understanding <char style="add">is</char> unto all those doing it. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 111:10">May His praise be enduring forever! <verse eid="PSA 111:10"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 111"/>

<chapter number="112" style="c" sid="PSA 112"/>

<para style="s">The Blessed Fear of Yahweh</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 112:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 128:1–6</char></note>Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">112.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char><char style="ft" closed="false">. This psalm is an acrostic poem, each line beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 112:1">Blessed <char style="add">is</char> the man fearing YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 112:1">in His commandments he has delighted greatly. <verse eid="PSA 112:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 112:2"/>His seed is mighty in the land; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 112:2">the generation of the upright will be blessed. <verse eid="PSA 112:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 112:3"/>Wealth and riches <char style="add">are</char> in his house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 112:3">and his righteousness stands forever. <verse eid="PSA 112:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 112:4"/>Light has risen in the darkness for the upright—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 112:4"><char style="add">for</char> the gracious, and compassionate, and righteous. <verse eid="PSA 112:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 112:5"/>The good man is gracious and lends freely; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 112:5">he contains his affairs with justice. <verse eid="PSA 112:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 112:6"/>Surely he will not be shaken forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 112:6">the righteous will be as a memorial forever. <verse eid="PSA 112:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 112:7"/>Of an evil report he is not afraid; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 112:7">his heart is firm, trusting in YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 112:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 112:8"/>His heart is upheld; he will not be afraid, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 112:8">until that he looks on his enemies. <verse eid="PSA 112:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 112:9"/>He has scattered—he has given to the needy; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 112:9">his righteousness stands forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 112:9">his horn is raised high in honor. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">112.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in 2 Corinthians 9:9</char></note><verse eid="PSA 112:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 112:10"/>A wicked one will see and be angry; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 112:10">he will gnash his teeth and melt away; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 112:10">the desire of the wicked ones will perish. <verse eid="PSA 112:10"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 112"/>

<chapter number="113" style="c" sid="PSA 113"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Exalts the Humble</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 113:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Samuel 1:1–8</char></note>Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">113.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 9</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 113:1">Praise, O servants of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 113:1">praise the name of YHWH! <verse eid="PSA 113:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 113:2"/>The name of YHWH be blessed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 113:2">from now and even to forever! <verse eid="PSA 113:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 113:3"/>From the rising of the sun to its coming in, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 113:3">praised <char style="add">is</char> the name of YHWH! <verse eid="PSA 113:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 113:4"/>High over all nations <char style="add">is</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 113:4"><char style="add">and</char> over the heavens His glory, <verse eid="PSA 113:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 113:5"/>who <char style="add">is</char> like YHWH our God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 113:5">being on high to dwell, <verse eid="PSA 113:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 113:6"/>stooping down to look on the heavens </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 113:6">and on the earth, <verse eid="PSA 113:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 113:7"/>raising up the poor from the dust. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 113:7">He lifts high the needy one from the ash heap, <verse eid="PSA 113:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 113:8"/>to make <char style="add">him</char> sit with princes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 113:8">with the princes of His people, <verse eid="PSA 113:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 113:9"/>settling in a home the barren woman, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 113:9">joyful like a mother of sons. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 113:9">Praise YAH! <verse eid="PSA 113:9"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 113"/>

<chapter number="114" style="c" sid="PSA 114"/>

<para style="s">A Psalm of Exodus</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 114:1"/>In the going forth of Israel from Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 114:1">the house of Jacob from a people speaking strangely, <verse eid="PSA 114:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 114:2"/>Judah became His sanctuary, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 114:2">Israel His dominion. <verse eid="PSA 114:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 114:3"/>The sea saw <char style="add">Him</char> and fled; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 114:3">the Jordan turned to the back. <verse eid="PSA 114:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 114:4"/>The mountains skipped like rams, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 114:4">the hills like sons of the flock. <verse eid="PSA 114:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 114:5"/>What <char style="add">was it</char> to you, O sea, that you fled, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 114:5">O Jordan, <char style="add">that</char> you turned back, <verse eid="PSA 114:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 114:6"/>O mountains, <char style="add">that</char> you⁺ skipped like rams, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 114:6">O hills, like sons of the flock? <verse eid="PSA 114:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 114:7"/>Tremble before the face of the Lord, O earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 114:7">before the face of the God of Jacob— <verse eid="PSA 114:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 114:8"/>turning the rock <char style="add">into</char> a pool of waters, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 114:8">the flint into a spring of waters! <verse eid="PSA 114:8"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 114"/>

<chapter number="115" style="c" sid="PSA 115"/>

<para style="s">To Your name Be the Glory</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 115:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 135:1–21</char></note>Not to us, O YHWH, not to us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:1">but to Your name, give glory, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 115:1">because of Your loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:1">because of Your faithfulness! <verse eid="PSA 115:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 115:2"/>Why should the nations say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:2">“Where now <char style="add">is</char> their God?” <verse eid="PSA 115:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 115:3"/>And our God <char style="add">is</char> in the heavens; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:3">all that he has pleased, He has done. <verse eid="PSA 115:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 115:4"/>Their idols <char style="add">are</char> silver and gold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:4">the work of the hands of man. <verse eid="PSA 115:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 115:5"/>A mouth <char style="add">is</char> unto them, and they do not speak; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:5">eyes <char style="add">are</char> unto them, and they do not see; <verse eid="PSA 115:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 115:6"/>ears <char style="add">are</char> unto them, and they do not hear; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:6">noses <char style="add">are</char> unto them, and they do not smell; <verse eid="PSA 115:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 115:7"/>they have hands and they do not feel; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:7">they have feet and they do not walk; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:7">and they do not utter by their throat.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">115.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they cannot even clear their throats</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 115:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 115:8"/>Those making them shall be like them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:8">everyone who is trusting in them. <verse eid="PSA 115:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 115:9"/>O Israel,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">115.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> MT; many Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, and Syriac </char><char style="fq" closed="false">O house of Israel</char></note> trust in YHWH! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:9">And He <char style="add">is</char> their help and their shield. <verse eid="PSA 115:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 115:10"/>O House of Aaron, trust in YHWH! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:10">And He <char style="add">is</char> their help and their shield. <verse eid="PSA 115:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 115:11"/>O fearers of YHWH, trust in YHWH! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:11">He <char style="add">is</char> their help and their shield. <verse eid="PSA 115:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 115:12"/>YHWH has remembered us; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:12">He will bless; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 115:12">He will bless the house of Israel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:12">He will bless the house of Aaron. <verse eid="PSA 115:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 115:13"/>He will bless those fearing YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:13">the small with the great. <verse eid="PSA 115:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 115:14"/>YHWH adds to you⁺—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:14">to you⁺ and to your⁺ sons! <verse eid="PSA 115:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 115:15"/>May you⁺ <char style="add">be</char> blessed by YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:15">maker of the heavens and the earth! <verse eid="PSA 115:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 115:16"/>The heavens of the heavens <char style="add">are</char> unto YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:16">and the earth He has given to the sons of man. <verse eid="PSA 115:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 115:17"/>The dead do not praise YAH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:17">and not any of those going down into silence. <verse eid="PSA 115:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 115:18"/>And we will bless YAH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 115:18">from now and even to forever. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 115:18">Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">115.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 115:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 115"/>

<chapter number="116" style="c" sid="PSA 116"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Has Heard My Voice</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 116:1"/>I have loved because YHWH has heard </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:1">the voice of my supplications, <verse eid="PSA 116:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 116:2"/>Because He has inclined His ear to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:2">even in the day I called. <verse eid="PSA 116:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 116:3"/>The cords of death surrounded me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:3">and the straits of Sheol found me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:3">distress and sorrow did I find. <verse eid="PSA 116:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 116:4"/>And in the name of YHWH I called out: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:4">“I pray, O YHWH, deliver my soul!” <verse eid="PSA 116:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 116:5"/>Gracious <char style="add">is</char> YHWH, and righteous; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:5">and our God is compassionate. <verse eid="PSA 116:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 116:6"/>YHWH preserves the simple ones; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:6">I was brought low, and to me He gave salvation. <verse eid="PSA 116:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 116:7"/>Return my soul, to your rest, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:7">for YHWH has dealt kindly with you. <verse eid="PSA 116:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 116:8"/>For you were rescued from death, O my soul, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:8">my eye from tears, my feet from stumbling. <verse eid="PSA 116:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 116:9"/>I will walk before the face of YHWH </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:9">in the land of the living. <verse eid="PSA 116:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 116:10"/>I believed, therefore I said, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:10">“I afflicted am greatly.” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">116.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">therefore I have spoken</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in 2 Corinthians 4:13</char></note><verse eid="PSA 116:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 116:11"/>I said in my hastening, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:11">“Every man is a liar.” <verse eid="PSA 116:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 116:12"/>What shall I return to YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:12">all His benefits <char style="add">are</char> upon me? <verse eid="PSA 116:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 116:13"/>I will take up the cup of salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:13">and upon the name of YHWH I will call. <verse eid="PSA 116:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 116:14"/>I will fulfill My vows to YHWH </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:14">now in front of all His people. <verse eid="PSA 116:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 116:15"/>Precious in the eyes of YHWH </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:15"><char style="add">is</char> the death of His holy ones. <verse eid="PSA 116:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 116:16"/>I ask, O YHWH—surely I <char style="add">am</char> Your servant; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:16">I <char style="add">am</char> Your servant, son of Your maidservant—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:16">You have loosed my bonds! <verse eid="PSA 116:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 116:17"/>To You I will sacrifice a sacrifice of thanksgiving, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:17">and in <char style="add">your</char> name, O YHWH, I will call. <verse eid="PSA 116:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 116:18"/>I will fulfill My vows to YHWH </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:18">now in front of all His people, <verse eid="PSA 116:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 116:19"/>in the courts of the house of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 116:19">in your midst, O Jerusalem. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 116:19">Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">116.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 116:19"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 116"/>

<chapter number="117" style="c" sid="PSA 117"/>

<para style="s">Extol Him, All You Peoples</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 117:1"/>Praise YHWH, all you nations; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 117:1">adore Him, all <char style="add">you</char> peoples!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">117.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 15:11</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 117:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 117:2"/>For mighty <char style="add">is</char> His loving devotion toward us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 117:2">and the faithfulness of YHWH <char style="add">is</char> forever. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 117:2">Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">117.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 117:2"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 117"/>

<chapter number="118" style="c" sid="PSA 118"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Is on My Side</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 118:1"/>Give thanks to YHWH, for <char style="add">He is</char> good, for </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:1">His loving devotion <char style="add">is</char> forever! <verse eid="PSA 118:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 118:2"/>Now let Israel<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">118.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the house of Israel</char></note> say that </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:2">His loving devotion <char style="add">is</char> forever! <verse eid="PSA 118:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 118:3"/>Now let the house of Aaron say </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:3">that His loving devotion <char style="add">is</char> forever! <verse eid="PSA 118:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 118:4"/>Now let those fearing YHWH say </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:4">that His loving devotion <char style="add">is</char> forever! <verse eid="PSA 118:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 118:5"/>In distress I called on YAH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:5">YAH answered me in a broad place. <verse eid="PSA 118:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 118:6"/>YHWH <char style="add">is</char> with me; I will not fear—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:6">what can man do to me?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">118.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">YHWH is on my side</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 7; LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">The Lord is my helper</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">118.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Hebrews 13:6</char></note><verse eid="PSA 118:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 118:7"/>YHWH <char style="add">is</char> with me as the One helping me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:7">and I shall look on those hating me. <verse eid="PSA 118:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 118:8"/><char style="add">It is</char> better to take refuge in YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:8">than to trust in man. <verse eid="PSA 118:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 118:9"/><char style="add">It is</char> better to take refuge in YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:9">than to trust in princes. <verse eid="PSA 118:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 118:10"/>All nations surrounded me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:10">in the name of YHWH I surely cut them off. <verse eid="PSA 118:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 118:11"/>They surrounded me, yes, they surrounded me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:11">and in the name of YHWH I surely cut them off! <verse eid="PSA 118:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 118:12"/>They have surrounded me like bees, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:12">they have been extinguished as fire among thorns; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:12">and in the name of YHWH I surely cut them off! <verse eid="PSA 118:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 118:13"/>You have severely thrust me that I might fall, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:13">and YHWH helped me. <verse eid="PSA 118:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 118:14"/>My strength and song <char style="add">is</char> YAH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:14">and He has become to me salvation. <verse eid="PSA 118:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 118:15"/>The voice of rejoicing and salvation <char style="add">is</char> in the tents of the righteous: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:15">“The right hand of YHWH acts with strength. <verse eid="PSA 118:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 118:16"/>The right hand of YHWH is exalted; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:16">the right hand of YHWH acts with strength.” <verse eid="PSA 118:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 118:17"/>I will not die, but I will live, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:17">that I might recount the works of YAH. <verse eid="PSA 118:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 118:18"/>Yah, chastened me severely, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:18">and to death He has not given me up. <verse eid="PSA 118:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 118:19"/>Open to me the gates of righteousness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:19">I will enter into them; I will give thanks to YAH. <verse eid="PSA 118:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 118:20"/>This <char style="add">is</char> the gate of YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:20">the righteous shall enter into it. <verse eid="PSA 118:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 118:21"/>I thank You, for You have answered me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:21">and You have become to me for salvation. <verse eid="PSA 118:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 118:22"/>The stone the builders rejected </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:22">has become as the head of the corner. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">118.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">has become the cornerstone</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Matthew 21:42, Mark 12:10, Luke 20:17, Acts 4:11, and 1 Peter 2:7</char></note><verse eid="PSA 118:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 118:23"/>From YHWH this is; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:23">it is marvelous in our eyes.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">118.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Matthew 21:42 and Mark 12:11</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 118:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 118:24"/>This <char style="add">is</char> the day YHWH has made; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:24">we will rejoice and be glad in it. <verse eid="PSA 118:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 118:25"/>I ask, O YHWH, save <char style="add">us</char> now. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:25">I ask, O YHWH, send prosperity now! <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">118.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">hosia-na</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, meaning </char><char style="fq" closed="false">save, we pray</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">save now</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Matthew 21:9, Matthew 21:15, Mark 11:9, and John 12:13.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 118:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 118:26"/>Blessed <char style="add">is</char> the one coming in the name of YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:26">we bless you⁺ from the house of YHWH. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">118.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Matthew 21:9, Matthew 23:39, Mark 11:9, Luke 13:35, Luke 19:38, and John 12:13</char></note><verse eid="PSA 118:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 118:27"/>YHWH <char style="add">is</char> God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:27">and He has given light to us! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 118:27">Bind the festal sacrifice with cords </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:27">to the horns of the altar!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">118.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Join in the festal procession with boughs in hand, up to the horns of the altar.</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 118:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 118:28"/>You <char style="add">are</char> my God, and I will give You thanks; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:28">my God, I will exalt You! <verse eid="PSA 118:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 118:29"/>Give thanks to YHWH, for <char style="add">He is</char> good; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 118:29">for His loving devotion <char style="add">is</char> forever! <verse eid="PSA 118:29"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 118"/>

<chapter number="119" style="c" sid="PSA 119"/>

<para style="s">Your Word Is a Lamp to My Feet</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 119:1"/>Blessed <char style="add">are</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">119.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> This psalm is an acrostic poem of twenty-two stanzas, following the letters of the Hebrew alphabet; within a stanza, each verse begins with the same Hebrew letter.</char></note> those complete in the way, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:1">those walking in the law of YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 119:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 119:2"/>Blessed <char style="add">are</char> those keeping His testimonies; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:2">with all the heart they seek Him. <verse eid="PSA 119:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 119:3"/>Also they do not do injustice; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:3">in His ways they walk. <verse eid="PSA 119:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 119:4"/>You have commanded Your precepts, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:4">to be kept diligently. <verse eid="PSA 119:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 119:5"/>Oh, that my ways were set firm </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:5">to keep Your statutes! <verse eid="PSA 119:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 119:6"/>Then I would not be ashamed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:6">in my looking to all Your commandments. <verse eid="PSA 119:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 119:7"/>I will praise You with uprightness of heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:7">in my learning the judgments of Your righteousness. <verse eid="PSA 119:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 119:8"/>Your statutes I will keep; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:8">may You not even to exceedingly forsake me! </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:8">בBETH<verse eid="PSA 119:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 119:9"/>How can a young man keep pure his way? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:9">By guarding <char style="add">it</char> according to Your word. <verse eid="PSA 119:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 119:10"/>With all my heart I have sought You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:10">do not let me stray from Your commandments. <verse eid="PSA 119:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 119:11"/>In my heart I have hidden Your word, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:11">that I should not sin against You. <verse eid="PSA 119:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 119:12"/>Blessed <char style="add">are</char> You, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:12">teach me Your statutes. <verse eid="PSA 119:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 119:13"/>With my lips I have recounted </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:13">all the judgments of Your mouth. <verse eid="PSA 119:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 119:14"/>In the way of Your testimonies I rejoice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:14">more than in all wealth. <verse eid="PSA 119:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 119:15"/>May I meditate on Your precepts </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:15">and look upon Your paths. <verse eid="PSA 119:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 119:16"/>In Your statutes I will delight myself; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:16">I will not forget Your word. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:16">גGIMEL<verse eid="PSA 119:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 119:17"/>Deal bountifully with Your servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:17"><char style="add">that</char> I may live and keep Your word. <verse eid="PSA 119:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 119:18"/>Open my eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:18">that I may see the wonders from Your law. <verse eid="PSA 119:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 119:19"/>I <char style="add">am</char> a sojourner on the earth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:19">do not hide from me Your commandments! <verse eid="PSA 119:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 119:20"/>My soul is crushed with longing </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:20">for Your judgments at all times. <verse eid="PSA 119:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 119:21"/>You rebuke the arrogant ones, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:21">the accursed ones, those going astray from Your commandments. <verse eid="PSA 119:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 119:22"/>Remove from me scorn and contempt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:22">for I have kept Your testimonies. <verse eid="PSA 119:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 119:23"/>Though princes sit against me and slander, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:23">Your servant meditates on Your statutes. <verse eid="PSA 119:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 119:24"/>Your testimonies also <char style="add">are</char> my delight—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:24">the men of my counsel. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:24">דDALETH<verse eid="PSA 119:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 119:25"/>My soul clings to the dust; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:25">revive me according to Your word! <verse eid="PSA 119:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 119:26"/>My ways I recounted, and You answered me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:26">teach me Your statutes. <verse eid="PSA 119:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 119:27"/>Make me understand the way of Your precepts, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:27">that I may meditate on Your wonders. <verse eid="PSA 119:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 119:28"/>My soul drips from sorrow; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:28">establish me according to Your word! <verse eid="PSA 119:28"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 119:29"/>Turn away from me the path of deceit, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:29">and <char style="add">with</char> Your law show favor to me. <verse eid="PSA 119:29"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 119:30"/>The way of truth I have chosen; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:30">Your ordinances I have set. <verse eid="PSA 119:30"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 119:31"/>I cling to Your testimonies, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:31">let me not be put to shame! <verse eid="PSA 119:31"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 119:32"/>The way of Your commandments I will run, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:32">for You will enlarge my heart. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:32">הHE<verse eid="PSA 119:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 119:33"/>Teach me, O YHWH, the way of Your statutes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:33">and I will keep it <char style="add">to</char> the end.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">119.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">keep it as my reward</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 119:33"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 119:34"/>Give me understanding, and I will guard Your law, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:34">and I will keep it with all <char style="add">my</char> heart. <verse eid="PSA 119:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 119:35"/>Cause me to tread in the path of Your commandments, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:35">for in it I delight. <verse eid="PSA 119:35"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 119:36"/>Incline my heart toward Your testimonies, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:36">and not toward dishonest gain. <verse eid="PSA 119:36"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 119:37"/>Make my eyes pass from seeing the vain <char style="add">thing</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:37">with Your word<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">119.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Two MT manuscripts and DSS; most MT manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in Your way</char></note> revive me. <verse eid="PSA 119:37"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 119:38"/>Make Your word stand for Your servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:38">which <char style="add">is</char> for the fearing of You. <verse eid="PSA 119:38"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 119:39"/>Remove the reproach that I dread, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:39">for Your judgments <char style="add">are</char> good. <verse eid="PSA 119:39"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 119:40"/>Behold, I long for Your precepts; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:40">Revive me in Your righteousness! </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:40">וWAW<verse eid="PSA 119:40"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 119:41"/>And may Your loving devotion come to me, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:41">Your salvation according to Your word. <verse eid="PSA 119:41"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 119:42"/>Then I will answer with a word for the one reproaching me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:42">for I trust in Your word. <verse eid="PSA 119:42"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 119:43"/>And do not take away from my mouth the word of truth even to exceedingly! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:43">For in Your judgments I have hoped. <verse eid="PSA 119:43"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 119:44"/>And I will keep Your law continually, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:44">forever and ever, <verse eid="PSA 119:44"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 119:45"/>and I will walk in a broad place, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:45">for Your precepts I have sought. <verse eid="PSA 119:45"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 119:46"/>And I will speak of Your testimonies before kings, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:46">and I will not be ashamed. <verse eid="PSA 119:46"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 119:47"/>And I will delight myself in Your commandments, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:47">which I have loved. <verse eid="PSA 119:47"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 119:48"/>And I will lift up my hands to Your commandments, which I have loved, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:48">and I will meditate on Your statutes. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:48">זZAYIN<verse eid="PSA 119:48"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="PSA 119:49"/>Remember the word to Your servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:49">upon that You have caused me to hope. <verse eid="PSA 119:49"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="PSA 119:50"/>This <char style="add">is</char> my comfort in my affliction, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:50">for Your word has given me life. <verse eid="PSA 119:50"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="PSA 119:51"/>The arrogant ones mock me even to exceedingly; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:51">from Your law I do not stretch away. <verse eid="PSA 119:51"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="PSA 119:52"/>I remember Your judgments from old, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:52">and I am comforted. <verse eid="PSA 119:52"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="53" style="v" sid="PSA 119:53"/>Indignation has seized me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:53">from the wicked forsaking Your law. <verse eid="PSA 119:53"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="54" style="v" sid="PSA 119:54"/>Your statutes have been songs to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:54">in the house of my sojourning. <verse eid="PSA 119:54"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="55" style="v" sid="PSA 119:55"/>I remember Your name in the night, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:55">and I keep Your law. <verse eid="PSA 119:55"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="56" style="v" sid="PSA 119:56"/>This has come to be for me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:56">for I have kept Your precepts. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:56">חHETH<verse eid="PSA 119:56"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="57" style="v" sid="PSA 119:57"/>YHWH <char style="add">is</char> my portion; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:57">I have said I would keep Your words. <verse eid="PSA 119:57"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="58" style="v" sid="PSA 119:58"/>I appeased Your face with all <char style="add">my</char> heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:58">be gracious to me according to Your word. <verse eid="PSA 119:58"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="59" style="v" sid="PSA 119:59"/>I have considered my paths, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:59">and turned back my feet to Your testimonies. <verse eid="PSA 119:59"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="60" style="v" sid="PSA 119:60"/>I hurried and did not delay </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:60">to keep Your commandments. <verse eid="PSA 119:60"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="61" style="v" sid="PSA 119:61"/>The cords of the wicked have surrounded me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:61">Your law I have not forgotten. <verse eid="PSA 119:61"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="62" style="v" sid="PSA 119:62"/><char style="add">In</char> the middle of the night, I rise to give thanks to You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:62">upon the judgments of Your righteousness. <verse eid="PSA 119:62"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="63" style="v" sid="PSA 119:63"/>I <char style="add">am</char> a companion to all who fear You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:63">and to those keeping Your precepts. <verse eid="PSA 119:63"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="64" style="v" sid="PSA 119:64"/>O YHWH, with Your loving devotion the earth is full; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:64">teach me Your statutes. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:64">טTETH<verse eid="PSA 119:64"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="65" style="v" sid="PSA 119:65"/>You have done well with Your servant, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:65">according to Your word. <verse eid="PSA 119:65"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="66" style="v" sid="PSA 119:66"/>So may You teach me good judgment and knowledge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:66">for in Your commandments I have believed. <verse eid="PSA 119:66"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="67" style="v" sid="PSA 119:67"/>Before I was afflicted, I was going astray; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:67">and now I have kept Your word. <verse eid="PSA 119:67"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="68" style="v" sid="PSA 119:68"/>You <char style="add">are</char> good, and the One doing good; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:68">may You teach me Your statutes. <verse eid="PSA 119:68"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="69" style="v" sid="PSA 119:69"/>The arrogant ones have smeared a lie over me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:69">I, with all <char style="add">my</char> heart, will guard Your precepts. <verse eid="PSA 119:69"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="70" style="v" sid="PSA 119:70"/>Their heart is unfeeling like fat;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">119.70 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">fat</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:70">I have delighted in Your law. <verse eid="PSA 119:70"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="71" style="v" sid="PSA 119:71"/><char style="add">It is</char> good for me that I was afflicted, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:71">so that I might learn Your statutes. <verse eid="PSA 119:71"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="72" style="v" sid="PSA 119:72"/>The law from Your mouth <char style="add">is</char> better to me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:72">than thousands of gold and silver. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:72">יYODH<verse eid="PSA 119:72"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="73" style="v" sid="PSA 119:73"/>Your hands have made me and established me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:73">give me understanding to learn Your commandments. <verse eid="PSA 119:73"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="74" style="v" sid="PSA 119:74"/>Those fearing You see me and rejoice, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:74">because in Your word I have hoped. <verse eid="PSA 119:74"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="75" style="v" sid="PSA 119:75"/>I know, O YHWH, that Your judgments <char style="add">are</char> righteous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:75">and in faithfulness You have afflicted me. <verse eid="PSA 119:75"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="76" style="v" sid="PSA 119:76"/>Your loving devotion, may it be, please, to comfort me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:76">according to Your word to Your servant. <verse eid="PSA 119:76"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="77" style="v" sid="PSA 119:77"/>May Your compassions come to me, that I may live, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:77">for Your law <char style="add">is</char> my delight. <verse eid="PSA 119:77"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="78" style="v" sid="PSA 119:78"/>May the arrogant ones be put to shame, for with a lie they dealt perversely with me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:78">I will meditate on Your precepts. <verse eid="PSA 119:78"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="79" style="v" sid="PSA 119:79"/>Let those who fear You turn to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:79">and those who know Your testimonies. <verse eid="PSA 119:79"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="80" style="v" sid="PSA 119:80"/>May my heart be perfect in Your statutes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:80">so that I may not be ashamed. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:80">כKAPH<verse eid="PSA 119:80"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="81" style="v" sid="PSA 119:81"/>My soul faints for Your salvation; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:81">for Your word I wait. <verse eid="PSA 119:81"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="82" style="v" sid="PSA 119:82"/>My eyes fail for your word, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:82">saying, “When will You comfort me?” <verse eid="PSA 119:82"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="83" style="v" sid="PSA 119:83"/>For, I have become like a wineskin in smoke; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:83">Your statutes I have not forgotten. <verse eid="PSA 119:83"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="84" style="v" sid="PSA 119:84"/>How many <char style="add">are</char> the days of Your servant?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">119.84 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">How many days must Your servant wait?</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:84">When will You execute judgment on my pursuers? <verse eid="PSA 119:84"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="85" style="v" sid="PSA 119:85"/>The arrogant ones have dug pits for me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:85">that <char style="add">are</char> not according to Your law. <verse eid="PSA 119:85"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="86" style="v" sid="PSA 119:86"/>All Your commandments <char style="add">are</char> firm, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:86">falsely they pursue me—Help me! <verse eid="PSA 119:86"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="87" style="v" sid="PSA 119:87"/>Almost they consumed me on the earth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:87">and I have not forsaken Your precepts. <verse eid="PSA 119:87"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="88" style="v" sid="PSA 119:88"/>According to Your loving devotion, revive me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:88">that I may keep the testimony of Your mouth. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:88">לLAMEDH<verse eid="PSA 119:88"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="89" style="v" sid="PSA 119:89"/>Forever, O YHWH, <char style="add">is</char> Your word, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:89">standing fixed in the heavens. <verse eid="PSA 119:89"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="90" style="v" sid="PSA 119:90"/>For generation and generation <char style="add">is</char> Your faithfulness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:90">You established the earth, and it stands. <verse eid="PSA 119:90"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="91" style="v" sid="PSA 119:91"/>According to Your ordinances, they stand this day,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">119.91 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">They stand to this day</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:91">for all things <char style="add">are</char> Your servants. <verse eid="PSA 119:91"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="92" style="v" sid="PSA 119:92"/>Had Your law not been my delight, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:92">then I would have perished in my affliction. <verse eid="PSA 119:92"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="93" style="v" sid="PSA 119:93"/>Forever, I will not forget Your precepts, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:93">for by them You have revived me. <verse eid="PSA 119:93"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="94" style="v" sid="PSA 119:94"/>Unto You I am—save me! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:94">For I have sought Your precepts. <verse eid="PSA 119:94"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="95" style="v" sid="PSA 119:95"/>The wicked wait for me to destroy me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:95">Your testimonies I will consider. <verse eid="PSA 119:95"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="96" style="v" sid="PSA 119:96"/>To all perfection I have seen an end; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:96">broad <char style="add">is</char> Your commandment exceedingly. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:96">מMEM<verse eid="PSA 119:96"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="97" style="v" sid="PSA 119:97"/>Oh, how I love Your law! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:97">All the day, it <char style="add">is</char> my meditation. <verse eid="PSA 119:97"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="98" style="v" sid="PSA 119:98"/><char style="add">By</char> Your commandment You make me wiser than my enemies; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:98">for, it <char style="add">is</char> with me forever. <verse eid="PSA 119:98"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="99" style="v" sid="PSA 119:99"/>I have insight above all my teachers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:99">for Your testimonies <char style="add">are</char> a meditation to me. <verse eid="PSA 119:99"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="100" style="v" sid="PSA 119:100"/>I understand above elders, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:100">for Your precepts I have kept. <verse eid="PSA 119:100"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="101" style="v" sid="PSA 119:101"/>From every path of evil I have restrained my feet, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:101">that I may keep Your word. <verse eid="PSA 119:101"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="102" style="v" sid="PSA 119:102"/>From Your ordinances I have not turned aside, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:102">for You have instructed me. <verse eid="PSA 119:102"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="103" style="v" sid="PSA 119:103"/>How smooth are Your words to my palate, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:103">more than honey to my mouth! <verse eid="PSA 119:103"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="104" style="v" sid="PSA 119:104"/>From Your precepts I gain understanding; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:104">upon thus, I hate every path of deception! </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:104">נNUN<verse eid="PSA 119:104"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="105" style="v" sid="PSA 119:105"/>Your word <char style="add">is</char> a lamp to my feet, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:105">and a light to my path. <verse eid="PSA 119:105"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="106" style="v" sid="PSA 119:106"/>I have sworn and confirmed: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:106">I will keep the judgments of Your righteousness. <verse eid="PSA 119:106"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="107" style="v" sid="PSA 119:107"/>I am afflicted even exceedingly, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:107">revive me according to Your word! <verse eid="PSA 119:107"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="108" style="v" sid="PSA 119:108"/>May You accept the freewill offerings of my mouth, please, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:108">and may You teach me Your judgments. <verse eid="PSA 119:108"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="109" style="v" sid="PSA 119:109"/>My soul <char style="add">is</char> in my hand continually, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:109">and I do not forget Your law. <verse eid="PSA 119:109"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="110" style="v" sid="PSA 119:110"/>The wicked have set a snare for me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:110">and from Your precepts I do not go astray. <verse eid="PSA 119:110"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="111" style="v" sid="PSA 119:111"/>I have inherited Your testimonies forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:111">for they <char style="add">are</char> the joy of my heart. <verse eid="PSA 119:111"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="112" style="v" sid="PSA 119:112"/>I have inclined my heart to perform Your statutes </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:112">forever, <char style="add">to</char> the end! </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:112">סSAMEKH<verse eid="PSA 119:112"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="113" style="v" sid="PSA 119:113"/>The double-minded I hate, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:113">and Your law I love. <verse eid="PSA 119:113"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="114" style="v" sid="PSA 119:114"/>You <char style="add">are</char> my hiding place and my shield; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:114">in Your word I hope. <verse eid="PSA 119:114"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="115" style="v" sid="PSA 119:115"/>Turn away from me, O evildoers! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:115">And I will keep the commandments of my God. <verse eid="PSA 119:115"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="116" style="v" sid="PSA 119:116"/>Uphold me according to Your word, and l will live; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:116">and do not make me ashamed of my hope! <verse eid="PSA 119:116"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="117" style="v" sid="PSA 119:117"/>Support me, and I will be saved; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:117">and I will gaze on Your statutes continually. <verse eid="PSA 119:117"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="118" style="v" sid="PSA 119:118"/>You have trodden down all those going astray from Your statutes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:118">for their treachery <char style="add">is</char> falsehood. <verse eid="PSA 119:118"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="119" style="v" sid="PSA 119:119"/>Like dross You put an end to all the wicked of the earth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:119">therefore I love Your testimonies. <verse eid="PSA 119:119"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="120" style="v" sid="PSA 119:120"/>My flesh bristles from dread of You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:120">and of your judgments I have been afraid. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:120">עAYIN<verse eid="PSA 119:120"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="121" style="v" sid="PSA 119:121"/>I have done justice and righteousness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:121">do not leave me to my oppressors! <verse eid="PSA 119:121"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="122" style="v" sid="PSA 119:122"/>Ensure Your servant for good; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:122">do not let the arrogant ones oppress me. <verse eid="PSA 119:122"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="123" style="v" sid="PSA 119:123"/>My eyes fail for Your salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:123">and for the word of Your righteousness. <verse eid="PSA 119:123"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="124" style="v" sid="PSA 119:124"/>Deal with Your servant according to Your loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:124">and teach me Your statutes. <verse eid="PSA 119:124"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="125" style="v" sid="PSA 119:125"/>I <char style="add">am</char> Your servant—give me understanding, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:125">that I may know Your testimonies. <verse eid="PSA 119:125"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="126" style="v" sid="PSA 119:126"/><char style="add">It is</char> time, O YHWH, to act; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:126">they have broken Your law! <verse eid="PSA 119:126"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="127" style="v" sid="PSA 119:127"/>Upon thus, I love Your commandments more than gold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:127">and more than fine gold. <verse eid="PSA 119:127"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="128" style="v" sid="PSA 119:128"/>Upon thus, all the precepts I have declared wholly right; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:128">every path of deception I hate. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:128">פPE<verse eid="PSA 119:128"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="129" style="v" sid="PSA 119:129"/>Wonderful <char style="add">are</char> Your testimonies; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:129">upon thus, my soul has kept watch <char style="add">over</char> them. <verse eid="PSA 119:129"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="130" style="v" sid="PSA 119:130"/>The opening of Your words gives light, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:130">giving understanding to the simple ones. <verse eid="PSA 119:130"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="131" style="v" sid="PSA 119:131"/>I have opened my mouth and I pant—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:131">for I have longed for Your commandments! <verse eid="PSA 119:131"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="132" style="v" sid="PSA 119:132"/>Turn to me and be gracious to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:132">according to justice to those loving Your name. <verse eid="PSA 119:132"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="133" style="v" sid="PSA 119:133"/>Establish my steps by Your word, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:133">and do not let any iniquity rule over me. <verse eid="PSA 119:133"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="134" style="v" sid="PSA 119:134"/>Redeem me from the oppression of man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:134">that I may keep Your precepts. <verse eid="PSA 119:134"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="135" style="v" sid="PSA 119:135"/>Make Your face shine on Your servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:135">and teach me Your statutes. <verse eid="PSA 119:135"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="136" style="v" sid="PSA 119:136"/>Streams of waters run down from my eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:136">because they have not kept Your law. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:136">צTZADE<verse eid="PSA 119:136"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="137" style="v" sid="PSA 119:137"/>You <char style="add">are</char> righteous, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:137">and Your judgments <char style="add">are</char> upright. <verse eid="PSA 119:137"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="138" style="v" sid="PSA 119:138"/>You have appointed your righteous testimonies, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:138">and exceedingly faithful. <verse eid="PSA 119:138"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="139" style="v" sid="PSA 119:139"/>My zeal has cut me off, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:139">because my adversaries have forgotten Your words. <verse eid="PSA 119:139"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="140" style="v" sid="PSA 119:140"/>Your word <char style="add">is</char> exceedingly pure, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:140">and Your servant has loved it. <verse eid="PSA 119:140"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="141" style="v" sid="PSA 119:141"/>I <char style="add">am</char> little and despised; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:141">I do not forget Your precepts. <verse eid="PSA 119:141"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="142" style="v" sid="PSA 119:142"/>Your righteousness <char style="add">is</char> righteous forever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:142">and Your law <char style="add">is</char> truth. <verse eid="PSA 119:142"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="143" style="v" sid="PSA 119:143"/>Trouble and distress have found me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:143">Your commandments <char style="add">are</char> my delight. <verse eid="PSA 119:143"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="144" style="v" sid="PSA 119:144"/>The righteousness of Your testimonies <char style="add">is</char> forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:144">give me understanding, that I may live! </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:144">קKOPH<verse eid="PSA 119:144"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="145" style="v" sid="PSA 119:145"/>I cry out with all <char style="add">my</char> heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:145">answer me, O YHWH! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:145">Your statutes I will guard. <verse eid="PSA 119:145"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="146" style="v" sid="PSA 119:146"/>I call out to You, save me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:146">that I may keep Your testimonies! <verse eid="PSA 119:146"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="147" style="v" sid="PSA 119:147"/>I went ahead at the dawn, and I cried out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:147"><char style="add">and</char> for Your word I have hoped. <verse eid="PSA 119:147"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="148" style="v" sid="PSA 119:148"/>My eyes have gone before the watches </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:148">to meditate on Your word. <verse eid="PSA 119:148"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="149" style="v" sid="PSA 119:149"/>Hear my voice, O YHWH, according to Your loving devotion; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:149">according to Your justice, preserve my life! <verse eid="PSA 119:149"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="150" style="v" sid="PSA 119:150"/>They draw near, those pursuing wickedness! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:150">From Your law they are far. <verse eid="PSA 119:150"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="151" style="v" sid="PSA 119:151"/>You <char style="add">are</char> near, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:151">and all Your commandments <char style="add">are</char> truth. <verse eid="PSA 119:151"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="152" style="v" sid="PSA 119:152"/>I have known of Your testimonies of old, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:152">that forever You have founded them. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:152">רRESH<verse eid="PSA 119:152"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="153" style="v" sid="PSA 119:153"/>See my affliction and rescue me! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:153">For I have not forgotten Your law. <verse eid="PSA 119:153"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="154" style="v" sid="PSA 119:154"/>Plead my plea and redeem me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:154">according to Your word, revive me! <verse eid="PSA 119:154"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="155" style="v" sid="PSA 119:155"/>Far from the wicked <char style="add">is</char> salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:155">because they have not not sought Your statutes. <verse eid="PSA 119:155"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="156" style="v" sid="PSA 119:156"/>Your mercies <char style="add">are</char> great, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:156">according to Your ordinances, revive me! <verse eid="PSA 119:156"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="157" style="v" sid="PSA 119:157"/>Many <char style="add">are</char> my pursuers and my adversaries; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:157">from Your testimonies I have not turned aside. <verse eid="PSA 119:157"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="158" style="v" sid="PSA 119:158"/>I have seen those acting treacherously, and I felt loathing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:158">because they have not kept Your word. <verse eid="PSA 119:158"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="159" style="v" sid="PSA 119:159"/>See, how I love Your precepts, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:159">according to Your loving devotion, revive me! <verse eid="PSA 119:159"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="160" style="v" sid="PSA 119:160"/>The head of Your word <char style="add">is</char> truth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:160">and every judgment of Your righteousness <char style="add">is</char> forever. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:160">שSIN and SHIN<verse eid="PSA 119:160"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="161" style="v" sid="PSA 119:161"/>Princes may pursue me without cause, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:161">and of Your word my heart was afraid. <verse eid="PSA 119:161"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="162" style="v" sid="PSA 119:162"/>I <char style="add">am</char> rejoicing over Your word </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:162">like one finding great plunder. <verse eid="PSA 119:162"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="163" style="v" sid="PSA 119:163"/>Deception I hate and abhor; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:163">Your law I do love. <verse eid="PSA 119:163"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="164" style="v" sid="PSA 119:164"/>Seven times in the day I praise You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:164">because of the judgments of Your righteousness. <verse eid="PSA 119:164"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="165" style="v" sid="PSA 119:165"/>Great prosperity <char style="add">is</char> unto those loving Your law, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:165">and nothing to them <char style="add">is</char> a stumbling block. <verse eid="PSA 119:165"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="166" style="v" sid="PSA 119:166"/>I wait for Your salvation, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:166">and Your commandments I have done. <verse eid="PSA 119:166"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="167" style="v" sid="PSA 119:167"/>My soul has kept Your testimonies, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:167">and I love them exceedingly. <verse eid="PSA 119:167"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="168" style="v" sid="PSA 119:168"/>I have kept Your precepts and Your testimonies, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:168">because all my ways <char style="add">are</char> before You. </para>

<para style="qa" vid="PSA 119:168">תTAW<verse eid="PSA 119:168"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="169" style="v" sid="PSA 119:169"/>Let my cry come before You, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:169">according to Your word, give me understanding. <verse eid="PSA 119:169"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="170" style="v" sid="PSA 119:170"/>Let my supplication come before You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:170">according to Your word, deliver me. <verse eid="PSA 119:170"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="171" style="v" sid="PSA 119:171"/>Let my lips pour forth praise, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:171">for You teach me Your statutes. <verse eid="PSA 119:171"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="172" style="v" sid="PSA 119:172"/>Let my tongue sing out Your word, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:172">for all Your commandments <char style="add">are</char> righteous. <verse eid="PSA 119:172"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="173" style="v" sid="PSA 119:173"/>Let Your hand be to help me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:173">for Your precepts I have chosen. <verse eid="PSA 119:173"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="174" style="v" sid="PSA 119:174"/>I long for Your salvation, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:174">and Your law <char style="add">is</char> my delight. <verse eid="PSA 119:174"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="175" style="v" sid="PSA 119:175"/>Let my soul live, and it shall praise You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:175">and may Your judgments help me. <verse eid="PSA 119:175"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="176" style="v" sid="PSA 119:176"/>I have gone astray, getting lost like a sheep; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:176">may You seek Your servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 119:176">for Your commandments I have not forgotten. <verse eid="PSA 119:176"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 119"/>

<chapter number="120" style="c" sid="PSA 120"/>

<para style="s">In My Distress I Cried to Yahweh</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 120:1"/> To YHWH, in the distress for me, I cried out, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 120:1">and He answered me. <verse eid="PSA 120:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 120:2"/>O YHWH, deliver my soul from a lip of falsehood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 120:2">from a tongue of deceit! <verse eid="PSA 120:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 120:3"/>What will He give to you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 120:3">or what will He add to you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 120:3">O tongue of deceit? <verse eid="PSA 120:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 120:4"/>The sharpened arrows of a mighty one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 120:4">with the burning coals of broom trees! <verse eid="PSA 120:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 120:5"/>Woe to me for I have sojourned <char style="add">in</char> Mesech; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 120:5">I have dwelt among the tents of Kedar! <verse eid="PSA 120:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 120:6"/>Too much has dwelt my soul </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 120:6">with the one hating peace! <verse eid="PSA 120:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 120:7"/>I <char style="add">am</char> peace, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 120:7">and when I speak, they <char style="add">are</char> for war. <verse eid="PSA 120:7"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 120"/>

<chapter number="121" style="c" sid="PSA 121"/>

<para style="s">I lift Up My Eyes to the Hills</para>

<para style="s">A Song for the Ascents.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 121:1"/> I lift up my eyes to the hills, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 121:1">from where my help does come. <verse eid="PSA 121:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 121:2"/>My help <char style="add">is</char> from YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 121:2">the Maker of the heavens and the earth. <verse eid="PSA 121:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 121:3"/>He will not give your foot to the slipping; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 121:3">the One guarding you will not slumber. <verse eid="PSA 121:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 121:4"/>Behold, He does not slumber, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 121:4">and He does not sleep—the One guarding Israel. <verse eid="PSA 121:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 121:5"/>YHWH <char style="add">is</char> the One guarding you; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 121:5">YHWH <char style="add">is</char> your shade on your right hand. <verse eid="PSA 121:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 121:6"/>By day the sun will not strike you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 121:6">nor the moon in the night. <verse eid="PSA 121:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 121:7"/>YHWH will guard you from all evil; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 121:7">He will guard your soul. <verse eid="PSA 121:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 121:8"/>YHWH will guard your going out and your coming in, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 121:8">from now even to forever. <verse eid="PSA 121:8"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 121"/>

<chapter number="122" style="c" sid="PSA 122"/>

<para style="s">Pray for the Peace of Jerusalem</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents. Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 122:1"/> I was glad at the saying to me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 122:1">“Let us go <char style="add">to</char> the house of YHWH.” <verse eid="PSA 122:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 122:2"/>Our feet have been standing within your gates, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 122:2">O Jerusalem! <verse eid="PSA 122:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 122:3"/>Jerusalem is built up </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 122:3">as a city joined to itself together; <verse eid="PSA 122:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 122:4"/>there the tribes go up, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 122:4">the tribes of YAH, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 122:4">as a testimony for Israel, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 122:4">to give thanks to the name of YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 122:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 122:5"/>For there sit the thrones of judgment, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 122:5">the thrones of the house of David. <verse eid="PSA 122:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 122:6"/>Ask for the peace of Jerusalem: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 122:6">“May they prosper,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">122.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">be secure</char></note> those loving you! <verse eid="PSA 122:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 122:7"/>May there be peace within your wall, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 122:7">prosperity<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">122.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">security</char></note> within your citadels!” <verse eid="PSA 122:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 122:8"/>For the sake of my brothers and my companions </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 122:8">let me now say: “Peace <char style="add">be</char> within you!” <verse eid="PSA 122:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 122:9"/>For the sake of the house of YHWH our God </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 122:9">I will seek good for you. <verse eid="PSA 122:9"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 122"/>

<chapter number="123" style="c" sid="PSA 123"/>

<para style="s">I lift Up My Eyes to You</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 123:1"/> Unto You I lift up my eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 123:1"><char style="add">to</char> the One sitting in the heavens. <verse eid="PSA 123:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 123:2"/>Behold, as the eyes of servants </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 123:2"><char style="add">are</char> to the hand of their masters, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 123:2">as the eyes of a maidservant </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 123:2"><char style="add">are</char> to the hand of her mistress, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 123:2">so <char style="add">are</char> our eyes to YHWH our God, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 123:2">until He shows us mercy. <verse eid="PSA 123:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 123:3"/>Have mercy on us, O YHWH, Have mercy on us! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 123:3">For we are filled exceedingly with contempt. <verse eid="PSA 123:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 123:4"/>Exceedingly our soul has been filled with the scorn of those at ease, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 123:4">with the contempt of the prideful ones. <verse eid="PSA 123:4"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 123"/>

<chapter number="124" style="c" sid="PSA 124"/>

<para style="s">Our Help Is in the name of Yahweh</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents. Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 124:1"/> If YHWH had not been for us—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 124:1">now let Israel say— <verse eid="PSA 124:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 124:2"/>if YHWH had not been for us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 124:2">in the rising up of men against us, <verse eid="PSA 124:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 124:3"/>then they would have swallowed us alive, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 124:3">in the burning of their anger against us; <verse eid="PSA 124:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 124:4"/>then the waters would have engulfed us, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 124:4">the stream would have passed over our soul; <verse eid="PSA 124:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 124:5"/>then would have passed over our soul </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 124:5">the raging waters. <verse eid="PSA 124:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 124:6"/>Blessed <char style="add">be</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 124:6">who has not given us as prey to their teeth! <verse eid="PSA 124:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 124:7"/>Our soul like a bird has escaped from the snare of the fowlers; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 124:7">the snare is broken, and we have slipped away. <verse eid="PSA 124:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 124:8"/>Our help <char style="add">is</char> in the name of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 124:8">the Maker of the heavens and the earth. <verse eid="PSA 124:8"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 124"/>

<chapter number="125" style="c" sid="PSA 125"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Surrounds His People</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 125:1"/> Those trusting in YHWH are like Mount Zion—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 125:1">it cannot be shaken; it abides forever. <verse eid="PSA 125:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 125:2"/>Jerusalem, the mountains surround her, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 125:2">and YHWH surrounds His people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 125:2">from now even to forever. <verse eid="PSA 125:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 125:3"/>For the rod of the wicked shall not rest </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 125:3">upon the lot of the righteous, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 125:3">so that the righteous do not stretch out their hands to injustice. <verse eid="PSA 125:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 125:4"/>Do good, O YHWH, to the good, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 125:4">and to the upright in their hearts! <verse eid="PSA 125:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 125:5"/>And those turning to their crooked ways, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 125:5">YHWH will lead them away with the workers of iniquity! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 125:5">Peace <char style="add">be</char> upon Israel! <verse eid="PSA 125:5"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 125"/>

<chapter number="126" style="c" sid="PSA 126"/>

<para style="s">Zion’s Captives Restored</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 126:1"/> In YHWH turning back the captivity of Zion,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">126.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">bringing back the captives to Zion</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">restoring the fortunes of Zion</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 126:1">we were like those dreaming.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">126.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">like those restored to health</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 126:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 126:2"/>Then our mouth was filled with laughter, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 126:2">and our tongue with a shout of joy. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 126:2">Then they said among the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 126:2">“YHWH, has done great things for these.” <verse eid="PSA 126:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 126:3"/>YHWH has done great things for us; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 126:3">and we came to be glad. <verse eid="PSA 126:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 126:4"/>Bring back, O YHWH, our captives,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">126.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Restore, O YHWH, our fortunes</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 126:4">like streams in the Negev! <verse eid="PSA 126:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 126:5"/>Those sowing in tears </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 126:5">will reap with a shout of joy. <verse eid="PSA 126:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 126:6"/>Going forth, he who goes and weeps, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 126:6">bearing the basket of seed, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 126:6">coming in, he comes with a shout, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 126:6">bearing his sheaves. <verse eid="PSA 126:6"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 126"/>

<chapter number="127" style="c" sid="PSA 127"/>

<para style="s">Children Are a Heritage from Yahweh</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents. Of Solomon.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 127:1"/> If YHWH does not build the house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 127:1">in vain do its builders labor on it; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 127:1">if YHWH does not guard the city, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 127:1">in vain the one guarding keeps watch. <verse eid="PSA 127:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 127:2"/><char style="add">It is</char> vain for you⁺, being early <char style="add">in</char> rising, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 127:2"><char style="add">and</char> delaying to sit, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 127:2">eating the bread of sorrows; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 127:2">for so He gives sleep to His beloved. <verse eid="PSA 127:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 127:3"/>Behold, an inheritance of YHWH <char style="add">are</char> sons, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 127:3">a reward <char style="add">is</char> the fruit of the womb. <verse eid="PSA 127:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 127:4"/>Like arrows in the hand of a mighty one, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 127:4">so <char style="add">are</char> the sons of one’s youth. <verse eid="PSA 127:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 127:5"/>Blessed <char style="add">is</char> the man </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 127:5">who has filled his quiver with them! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 127:5">He will not be put to shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 127:5">but he shall speak with the enemies at the gate. <verse eid="PSA 127:5"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 127"/>

<chapter number="128" style="c" sid="PSA 128"/>

<para style="s">The Blessed Fear of Yahweh</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 128:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 112:1–10</char></note> Blessed <char style="add">is</char> everyone who fears YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 128:1">those walking in His ways! <verse eid="PSA 128:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 128:2"/>The labor of your hands, surely you shall eat; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 128:2">blessings and good <char style="add">are</char> unto you. <verse eid="PSA 128:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 128:3"/>Your wife <char style="add">is</char> fruitful like a vine </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 128:3">in the sides of your house, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 128:3">your sons like shoots of olive trees </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 128:3">round about your table. <verse eid="PSA 128:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 128:4"/>Behold, how thus is blessed </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 128:4">the man fearing YHWH. <verse eid="PSA 128:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 128:5"/>May YHWH bless you from Zion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 128:5">that you may look on the good of Jerusalem </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 128:5">all the days of your life, <verse eid="PSA 128:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 128:6"/>and may you see </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 128:6">the sons of your sons! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 128:6">Peace <char style="add">be</char> upon Israel! <verse eid="PSA 128:6"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 128"/>

<chapter number="129" style="c" sid="PSA 129"/>

<para style="s">The Cords of the Wicked</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 129:1"/> Often they have distressed me from my youth—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 129:1">now let Israel say— <verse eid="PSA 129:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 129:2"/>Often they have distressed me from my youth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 129:2">yet they have not prevailed against me. <verse eid="PSA 129:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 129:3"/>Upon my back, the plowmen were plowing; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 129:3">they have made long their furrows. <verse eid="PSA 129:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 129:4"/>YHWH the Righteous One, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 129:4">may He cut off the cords of the wicked! <verse eid="PSA 129:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 129:5"/>May they be put to shame and turned back, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 129:5">all those hating Zion! <verse eid="PSA 129:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 129:6"/>May they be like grass on the rooftops </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 129:6">that has withered before it can grow, <verse eid="PSA 129:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 129:7"/>unable to fill the hand of one reaping, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 129:7">or the bosom of one binding sheaves. <verse eid="PSA 129:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 129:8"/>And neither let those passing by say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 129:8">“The blessing of YHWH <char style="add">be</char> upon you⁺; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 129:8">we bless you⁺ in the name of YHWH!” <verse eid="PSA 129:8"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 129"/>

<chapter number="130" style="c" sid="PSA 130"/>

<para style="s">Out of the Depths</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 130:1"/> Out of the depths </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 130:1">I have called out to You, O YHWH! <verse eid="PSA 130:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 130:2"/>O Lord, listen to my voice! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 130:2">Let Your ears be attentive to the voice of my supplications! <verse eid="PSA 130:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 130:3"/>If You were to mark iniquities, O YAH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 130:3">O Lord, who could stand? <verse eid="PSA 130:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 130:4"/>But with You <char style="add">is</char> forgiveness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 130:4">so that You may be feared. <verse eid="PSA 130:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 130:5"/>I wait for YHWH; my soul waits, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 130:5">and in His word I have hoped. <verse eid="PSA 130:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 130:6"/>My soul <char style="add">is</char> for the Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 130:6">more than those watching for the morning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 130:6">watching for the morning. <verse eid="PSA 130:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 130:7"/>Look with hope, O Israel, unto YHWH! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 130:7">For with YHWH is loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 130:7">and redemption <char style="add">is</char> abundant with Him. <verse eid="PSA 130:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 130:8"/>And He will redeem Israel </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 130:8">from all his iniquities. <verse eid="PSA 130:8"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 130"/>

<chapter number="131" style="c" sid="PSA 131"/>

<para style="s">I Have Stilled My Soul</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents. Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 131:1"/> O YHWH, my heart is not lifted high, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 131:1">and my eyes are not raised up, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 131:1">and neither have I gone about in great things, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 131:1">and in marvelous things beyond me. <verse eid="PSA 131:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 131:2"/>If not, I have stilled and quieted my soul </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 131:2">like a weaned child with his mother; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 131:2">my soul <char style="add">is</char> like a weaned child within me. <verse eid="PSA 131:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 131:3"/>Look with hope, O Israel, unto YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 131:3">from now even to forever! <verse eid="PSA 131:3"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 131"/>

<chapter number="132" style="c" sid="PSA 132"/>

<para style="s">Yahweh Has Chosen Zion</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 132:1"/> Remember for David, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:1">all his afflictions, <verse eid="PSA 132:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 132:2"/>how he swore to YHWH </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:2"><char style="add">and</char> vowed to the Mighty One of Jacob: <verse eid="PSA 132:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 132:3"/>“If I enter into the tent of my house, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:3">or if go up on the couch of my bed, <verse eid="PSA 132:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 132:4"/>I will not give sleep to my eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:4"><char style="add">and</char> slumber to my eyelids, <verse eid="PSA 132:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 132:5"/>until I find a place for YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:5"><char style="add">a</char> dwelling place for the Mighty One of Jacob.” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">132.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a dwelling place for the God of Jacob</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Acts 7:46.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 132:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 132:6"/>Behold, we have heard of it<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">132.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the ark</char></note> in Ephrathah, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:6">we have found it in the fields of Jaar. <verse eid="PSA 132:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 132:7"/>Let us go into His dwelling place; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:7">let us worship at the stool of His feet! <verse eid="PSA 132:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 132:8"/>Arise, O YHWH, to Your resting place—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:8">You and the ark of Your strength! <verse eid="PSA 132:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 132:9"/>May Your priests be clothed with righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:9">and Your holy ones shout for joy! <verse eid="PSA 132:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 132:10"/>For the sake of David Your servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:10">do not turn away the face of Your anointed one. <verse eid="PSA 132:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 132:11"/>YHWH has sworn <char style="add">in</char> truth of David; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:11">He will not turn back from it: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 132:11">“I will set one from the fruit of your belly </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:11">on the throne of yours. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">132.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Acts 2:30</char></note><verse eid="PSA 132:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 132:12"/>If your sons will keep My covenant </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:12">and My testimonies that I teach them, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 132:12">their sons also, forever <char style="add">and</char> ever, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:12">will sit on the throne of yours.” <verse eid="PSA 132:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 132:13"/>For YHWH has set His choice on Zion; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:13">He has desired <char style="add">it</char> as a seat for Himself: <verse eid="PSA 132:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 132:14"/>“This <char style="add">is</char> My resting place forever <char style="add">and</char> ever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:14">here I will sit, for I have desired it. <verse eid="PSA 132:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 132:15"/>I will abundantly bless her provision, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:15"><char style="add">and</char> her needy ones I will satisfy <char style="add">with</char> bread; <verse eid="PSA 132:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 132:16"/>and her priests I will clothe <char style="add">with</char> salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:16">and her godly ones will shout in joy. <verse eid="PSA 132:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 132:17"/>There I will make to sprout a horn for David; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:17">I will arrange a lamp for My anointed one. <verse eid="PSA 132:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 132:18"/>I will clothe his enemies with shame, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 132:18">and upon him his diadem will shine.” <verse eid="PSA 132:18"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 132"/>

<chapter number="133" style="c" sid="PSA 133"/>

<para style="s">How Pleasant to Live in Harmony!</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents. Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 133:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Ephesians 4:1–16</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Corinthians 1:10–17</char></note> Behold, how good and how pleasant </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 133:1"><char style="add">is</char> the dwelling of brothers even together! <verse eid="PSA 133:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 133:2"/><char style="add">It is</char> good like oil upon the head, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 133:2">running down upon the beard, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 133:2">the beard of Aaron, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 133:2">which is running down upon the mouth of his garments; <verse eid="PSA 133:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 133:3"/><char style="add">or</char> like the dew of Hermon, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 133:3">which is coming down upon the mountains of Zion. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 133:3">For there YHWH commanded the blessing—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 133:3">life even to forever! <verse eid="PSA 133:3"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 133"/>

<chapter number="134" style="c" sid="PSA 134"/>

<para style="s">Bless Yahweh, All You Servants</para>

<para style="s">A Song of the Ascents.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 134:1"/> Come, bless YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 134:1">all servants of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 134:1">those standing in the house </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 134:1">of YHWH by night! <verse eid="PSA 134:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 134:2"/>Lift up your⁺ hands to the holy place, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 134:2">and bless YHWH! <verse eid="PSA 134:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 134:3"/>May YHWH bless you from Zion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 134:3">Maker of heavens and earth! <verse eid="PSA 134:3"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 134"/>

<chapter number="135" style="c" sid="PSA 135"/>

<para style="s">Give Praise, O Servants of Yahweh</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 135:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 115:1–18</char></note>Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">135.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 3 and 21</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 135:1">Praise the name of YHWH! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:1">Give praise, O servants of YHWH <verse eid="PSA 135:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 135:2"/>who are standing in the house of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:2">in the courts of the house of our God! <verse eid="PSA 135:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 135:3"/>Praise YAH, for YHWH <char style="add">is</char> good; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:3">sing praises to His name, for <char style="add">it is</char> pleasant! <verse eid="PSA 135:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 135:4"/>For YAH has chosen Jacob for Himself, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:4">Israel for His possession. <verse eid="PSA 135:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 135:5"/>For I know that YHWH <char style="add">is</char> great, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:5">and our Lord is greater than all gods! <verse eid="PSA 135:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 135:6"/>All that YHWH delights in, He does, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:6">in the heavens and on the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:6">in the seas and all the depths, <verse eid="PSA 135:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 135:7"/>bringing up the clouds </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:7">from the ends of the earth. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 135:7">He has made lightning for the rain, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:7">bringing forth the wind from His storehouses— <verse eid="PSA 135:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 135:8"/>who struck the firstborn of Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:8">from man even to beast. <verse eid="PSA 135:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 135:9"/>He sent forth signs and wonders into your midst, O Egypt, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:9">unto Pharaoh and all of his servants— <verse eid="PSA 135:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 135:10"/>who struck many nations </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:10">and killed mighty kings, <verse eid="PSA 135:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 135:11"/>even Sihon king of the Amorite, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:11">and Og king of Bashan, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:11">and all the kingdoms of Canaan. <verse eid="PSA 135:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 135:12"/>And He gave their land <char style="add">as</char> an inheritance, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:12">an inheritance to Israel His people. <verse eid="PSA 135:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 135:13"/>O YHWH, Your name <char style="add">is</char> forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:13">YHWH, Your memorial <char style="add">is</char> to generation and generation! <verse eid="PSA 135:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 135:14"/>For YHWH will vindicate His people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:14">and He will have compassion on His servants. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">135.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">will judge His people</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see also LXX; cited in Hebrews 10:30.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 135:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 135:15"/>The idols of the nations <char style="add">are</char> silver and gold, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:15">the work of the hands of man. <verse eid="PSA 135:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 135:16"/>Mouths <char style="add">are</char> unto them, and they do not speak; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:16">eyes <char style="add">are</char> unto them, and they do not see. <verse eid="PSA 135:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 135:17"/>Ears <char style="add">are</char> unto them and they do not hear; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:17">indeed, there <char style="add">is</char> no breath in their mouths. <verse eid="PSA 135:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 135:18"/>Their makers shall come to be like them—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:18">everyone who is trusting in them! <verse eid="PSA 135:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 135:19"/>O House of Israel, bless YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:19">O house of Aaron, bless YHWH; <verse eid="PSA 135:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 135:20"/>O house of Levi, bless YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:20"><char style="add">all you</char> fearing YHWH, bless YHWH! <verse eid="PSA 135:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 135:21"/>Blessed be YHWH from Zion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 135:21">the One dwelling <char style="add">in</char> Jerusalem! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 135:21">Praise YAH! <verse eid="PSA 135:21"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 135"/>

<chapter number="136" style="c" sid="PSA 136"/>

<para style="s">His Loving Devotion Endures Forever</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 136:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Chronicles 7:1–3</char></note>Give thanks to YHWH, for <char style="add">He is</char> good, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:1">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 136:2"/>Give thanks to the God of gods, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:2">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 136:3"/>Give thanks to the Lord of lords, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:3">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 136:4"/>to the One doing great wonders by Himself alone, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:4">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 136:5"/>to the One making the heavens with understanding, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:5">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 136:6"/>to the One spreading out the earth upon the waters, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:6">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 136:7"/>to the One making great the lights—</para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:7">for His loving devotion is forever— <verse eid="PSA 136:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 136:8"/>the sun for ruling over the day, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:8">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 136:9"/>the moon and stars for ruling over the night, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:9">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 136:10"/>to the one striking Egypt, against their firstborn, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:10">for His loving devotion is forever. <verse eid="PSA 136:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 136:11"/>And He brought forth Israel from their midst, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:11">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 136:12"/>with a strong hand and an outstretched arm, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:12">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 136:13"/>to the One dividing the Red sea<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">136.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Sea of Reeds</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 15</char></note> into parts, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:13">for His loving devotion is forever. <verse eid="PSA 136:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 136:14"/>And He made Israel pass through the midst of it, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:14">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 136:15"/>and He shook off<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">136.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and He swept</char></note> Pharaoh and his army into the Red Sea, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:15">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 136:16"/>to the One leading His people through the wilderness, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:16">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 136:17"/>to the One striking great kings, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:17">for His loving devotion is forever. <verse eid="PSA 136:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 136:18"/>And He killed mighty kings, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:18">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 136:19"/>Sihon king of the Amorite, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:19">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 136:20"/>and Og king of Bashan, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:20">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 136:21"/>and He gave their land as an inheritance—</para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:21">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 136:22"/>an inheritance to Israel His servant, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:22">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 136:23"/>who in our lowliness remembered us, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:23">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 136:24"/>and rescued us from our enemies, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:24">for His loving devotion is forever; <verse eid="PSA 136:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 136:25"/>the One giving food to all flesh, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:25">for His loving devotion is forever. <verse eid="PSA 136:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 136:26"/>Give thanks to the God of the heavens, </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 136:26">for His loving devotion is forever! <verse eid="PSA 136:26"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 136"/>

<chapter number="137" style="c" sid="PSA 137"/>

<para style="s">By the Rivers of Babylon</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 137:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Ezekiel 1:1–3</char></note>By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 137:1">and we wept in our remembering Zion. <verse eid="PSA 137:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 137:2"/>Upon the willows<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">137.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">poplars</char></note> in her midst, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 137:2">we hung our harps. <verse eid="PSA 137:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 137:3"/>For there our captors required of us the words of a song, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 137:3">and our tormentors, joy: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 137:3">“Sing to us a song of Zion.” <verse eid="PSA 137:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 137:4"/>How can we sing a song of YHWH </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 137:4">in a foreign land? <verse eid="PSA 137:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 137:5"/>If I should forget you, O Jerusalem, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 137:5">may my right hand forget. <verse eid="PSA 137:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 137:6"/>May my tongue cling to my palate, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 137:6">if I do not remember you, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 137:6">if I do not exalt Jerusalem </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 137:6">above my chief joy! <verse eid="PSA 137:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 137:7"/>Remember, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 137:7">about the sons of Edom, on the day of Jerusalem—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 137:7">those saying, “Lay <char style="add">her</char> bare! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 137:7">Lay <char style="add">her</char> bare to her foundation!” <verse eid="PSA 137:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 137:8"/>O Daughter of Babylon, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 137:8">O destroyed one, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 137:8">blessed <char style="add">is</char> he who repays to you, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 137:8">dealing with you as you have dealt with us! <verse eid="PSA 137:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 137:9"/>Blessed <char style="add">is</char> he who seizes and dashes </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 137:9">your infants against the rock! <verse eid="PSA 137:9"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 137"/>

<chapter number="138" style="c" sid="PSA 138"/>

<para style="s">A Thankful Heart</para>

<para style="s">Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 138:1"/> I give You praise with all of my heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 138:1">before the gods I sing Your praises. <verse eid="PSA 138:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 138:2"/>I bow down toward the temple of Your holiness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 138:2">and I give thanks to Your name </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 138:2">for Your loving devotion, and for Your faithfulness; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 138:2">for You have magnified above all </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 138:2">Your name <char style="add">and</char> Your word. <verse eid="PSA 138:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 138:3"/>On the day I called out, then You answered me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 138:3">You embolden me in my soul <char style="add">with</char> strength.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">138.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">You emboldened and strengthened my soul</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 138:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 138:4"/>O YHWH, all the kings of the earth will give You thanks </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 138:4">when they hear the words of Your mouth. <verse eid="PSA 138:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 138:5"/>And they will sing of the ways of YHWH: </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 138:5">For great <char style="add">is</char> the glory of YHWH! <verse eid="PSA 138:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 138:6"/>For YHWH <char style="add">is</char> on high, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 138:6">and the lowly one He sees, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 138:6">and the haughty He knows from afar. <verse eid="PSA 138:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 138:7"/>When I walk in the midst of distress, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 138:7">You revive me against the anger of my enemies; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 138:7">You stretch out Your hand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 138:7">and Your right hand saves me. <verse eid="PSA 138:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 138:8"/>May YHWH complete <char style="add">this</char> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 138:8">on my behalf! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 138:8">O YHWH, Your loving devotion <char style="add">is</char> forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 138:8">do not forsake the works of Your hands! <verse eid="PSA 138:8"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 138"/>

<chapter number="139" style="c" sid="PSA 139"/>

<para style="s">You Have Searched Me and Known Me</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 139:1"/> O YHWH, You have searched me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:1">and know <char style="add">me</char>. <verse eid="PSA 139:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 139:2"/>You know my sitting down and my rising up; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:2">You discern my thought from afar. <verse eid="PSA 139:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 139:3"/>You have fanned My wandering and my lying down, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:3">and You are aware of all my ways. <verse eid="PSA 139:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 139:4"/>For <char style="add">there is</char> not a word on my tongue—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:4">behold, O YHWH, You have known it all. <verse eid="PSA 139:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 139:5"/>Behind and before, You hem me in, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:5">and You have laid Your hand upon me. <verse eid="PSA 139:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 139:6"/><char style="add">Such</char> knowledge <char style="add">is</char> wonderful for me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:6">it is high, I am not able to atttain it. <verse eid="PSA 139:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 139:7"/>Where can I go from Your Spirit? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:7">Or where can I flee from Your face? <verse eid="PSA 139:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 139:8"/>If I ascend <char style="add">to</char> the heavens, there You <char style="add">are</char>; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:8">and if I make my bed <char style="add">in</char> Sheol, behold, You! <verse eid="PSA 139:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 139:9"/><char style="add">If</char> I lift up the wings of the morning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:9">if I settle in the furthest part of the sea, <verse eid="PSA 139:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 139:10"/>even there Your hand will guide me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:10">and Your right hand will hold me fast. <verse eid="PSA 139:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 139:11"/>And I said, “Surely the darkness will cover me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:11">and the light <char style="add">become</char> night around me”— <verse eid="PSA 139:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 139:12"/>even the darkness is not dark to You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:12">and the night shines like the day—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:12">as the darkness, so <char style="add">is</char> the light. <verse eid="PSA 139:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 139:13"/>For You have possessed my kidneys; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:13">You covered me in the womb of my mother. <verse eid="PSA 139:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 139:14"/>I give You praise </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:14">upon that fearfully I have been distinguished; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 139:14">wonderful <char style="add">are</char> Your works, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:14">and my soul knows <char style="add">it</char> very well. <verse eid="PSA 139:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 139:15"/>My bone was not hidden from You </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:15">when I was made in secret, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 139:15">woven together </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:15">in the depths of earth. <verse eid="PSA 139:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 139:16"/>Your eyes saw my unformed body, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:16">and in Your book all of them were written—</para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 139:16">the days fashioned for me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:16">and not one <char style="add">was</char> yet among them! <verse eid="PSA 139:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 139:17"/>And how precious are Your thoughts to me,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">139.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">How amazing are Your thoughts concerning me</char></note> O God! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:17">How vast is their sum! <verse eid="PSA 139:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 139:18"/><char style="add">If</char> I could count them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:18">they would number more than the sand! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 139:18">I awaken, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:18">and I am still with You. <verse eid="PSA 139:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 139:19"/>If only You would slay, O God, the wicked; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:19">and the men of blood, may they turn aside from me— <verse eid="PSA 139:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 139:20"/>who speak against You for wickedness; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:20">Your enemies <char style="add">are</char> lifted up to vanity.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">139.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Your enemies take your name in vain</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Your enemies bear up in vain</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Your enemies take Your cities in vain</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 139:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 139:21"/>Do I not hate those hating you, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:21">and I loathe those standing against You? <verse eid="PSA 139:21"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 139:22"/>I have hated them with perfect hatred; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:22">they have become as enemies to me! <verse eid="PSA 139:22"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 139:23"/>Search me, O God, and know my heart; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:23">test me, and know my thoughts. <verse eid="PSA 139:23"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 139:24"/>And see if a way of wickedness <char style="add">is</char> in me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 139:24">and lead me in the way everlasting. <verse eid="PSA 139:24"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 139"/>

<chapter number="140" style="c" sid="PSA 140"/>

<para style="s">Rescue Me from Evil Men</para>

<para style="s">For the one directing. A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 140:1"/> Rescue me, O YHWH, from the evil man; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:1">from the man of violence guard me— <verse eid="PSA 140:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 140:2"/>those who devise evil in the heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:2"><char style="add">and</char> all the day they stir up wars. <verse eid="PSA 140:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 140:3"/>They sharpen their tongues like a snake; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:3">the venom of a viper <char style="add">is</char> under their lips. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 140:3">Selah <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">140.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Cited in Romans 3:13</char></note><verse eid="PSA 140:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 140:4"/>keep me, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:4">from the hands of the wicked, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 140:4">from the man of violence guard me—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:4">those who have devised to push down my steps. <verse eid="PSA 140:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 140:5"/>The prideful ones have hidden a snare for me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:5">and ropes they have spread <char style="add">as</char> a net by the side of the path; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:5">lures they have set for me. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 140:5">Selah <verse eid="PSA 140:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 140:6"/>I said, “O YHWH, You <char style="add">are</char> my God;” </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:6">give ear to, O YHWH, the voice of my supplications! <verse eid="PSA 140:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 140:7"/>YHWH <char style="add">my</char> Lord, the strength of my salvation, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:7">You have covered my head on the day of armor. <verse eid="PSA 140:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 140:8"/>Do not grant, O YHWH, the desires of the wicked; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:8">do not promote his wicked device; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:8"><char style="add">lest</char> they be exalted! </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 140:8">Selah <verse eid="PSA 140:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 140:9"/>the poison of those surrounding me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:9">the trouble of their lips, let it cover them! <verse eid="PSA 140:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 140:10"/>Let burning coals fall upon them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:10">let them be cast into the fire, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:10">into deep pits, never to rise up again! <verse eid="PSA 140:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 140:11"/>A man of tongues, do not let him be established in the earth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:11">a man of violence, may evil hunt him to overflowing! <verse eid="PSA 140:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 140:12"/>I know that YHWH upholds justice for the poor, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:12"><char style="add">and</char> judgment for the needy. <verse eid="PSA 140:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 140:13"/>Indeed, the righteous will give praise to Your name; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 140:13">the upright will dwell with Your face. <verse eid="PSA 140:13"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 140"/>

<chapter number="141" style="c" sid="PSA 141"/>

<para style="s">Come Quickly to Me</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 141:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 70:1–5</char></note> O YHWH, I call to You—hurry to me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:1">give ear to my voice in my calling out to You! <verse eid="PSA 141:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 141:2"/>Let my prayer be established like incense before Your face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:2"><char style="add">and</char> the lifting of my hands like the offering of the evening. <verse eid="PSA 141:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 141:3"/>Set, O YHWH, a guard for my mouth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:3">keep watch over the door of my lips. <verse eid="PSA 141:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 141:4"/>Do not make my heart bend to an evil thing, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:4">to do works in wickedness, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 141:4">with men working iniquity; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:4">never shall I eat of their delicacies! <verse eid="PSA 141:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 141:5"/>Let a righteous one strike me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:5">and let him rebuke me <char style="add">in</char> loving devotion; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 141:5"><char style="add">it is</char> oil for my head—let not my head refuse <char style="add">it</char>! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:5">For still my prayer <char style="add">is</char> against their evil deeds. <verse eid="PSA 141:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 141:6"/>Let their judges be released into the hands of the rock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:6">and let them hear my words, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:6">for they are pleasant! <verse eid="PSA 141:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 141:7"/>Like the tilling and ripping up of the land, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:7">our bones are scattered at the mouth of Sheol. <verse eid="PSA 141:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 141:8"/>Yet unto You, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:8">O Lord, <char style="add">are</char> my eyes; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 141:8">in You I take refuge—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:8">do not lay bare my soul!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">141.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">do not pour out my life</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">do not give me over to death</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 141:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 141:9"/>Keep me from the snares they have laid for me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:9">and from the lures of the workers of iniquity! <verse eid="PSA 141:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 141:10"/>Let the wicked fall into their nets together, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 141:10">until I pass over. <verse eid="PSA 141:10"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 141"/>

<chapter number="142" style="c" sid="PSA 142"/>

<para style="s">I lift My Voice to Yahweh</para>

<para style="s">A Maskil† of David, in his being in the cave. A prayer.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 142:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 57:1–11</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Samuel 22:1–5</char></note> With my voice to YHWH I cry out; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 142:1">with my voice to YHWH I plead for grace. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">142.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Maskil</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 142:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 142:2"/>I pour out before Him my complaint; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 142:2">I declare my distress before Him. <verse eid="PSA 142:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 142:3"/>With the weakening of my spirit within me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 142:3">You indeed know my path; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 142:3">on the road that I walk, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 142:3">they have hidden a snare for me. <verse eid="PSA 142:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 142:4"/>Look <char style="add">to</char> the right and see, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 142:4">and no one attends to me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 142:4">the place of refuge has perished for me; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 142:4">no one is inquiring for my soul. <verse eid="PSA 142:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 142:5"/>I cried out to You, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 142:5">I said, “You <char style="add">are</char> my refuge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 142:5">my portion in the land of the living!” <verse eid="PSA 142:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 142:6"/>Attend to my cry, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 142:6">for exceedingly I am brought low! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 142:6">Deliver me from my pursuers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 142:6">for they are stronger than I. <verse eid="PSA 142:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 142:7"/>Bring forth my soul from prison, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 142:7">for giving praise by me <char style="add">to</char> Your name! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 142:7">Let the righteous ones surround me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 142:7">for You deal bountifully with me. <verse eid="PSA 142:7"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 142"/>

<chapter number="143" style="c" sid="PSA 143"/>

<para style="s">I Stretch Out My Hands to You</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 143:1"/> O YHWH, hear my prayer; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:1">give ear to my supplications! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:1">In Your faithfulness, answer me in Your righteousness! <verse eid="PSA 143:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 143:2"/>And do not enter into judgment with Your servant, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:2">for not anyone alive is righteous before Your face. <verse eid="PSA 143:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 143:3"/>For the enemy has pursued my soul; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:3">he has crushed my life to the ground; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 143:3">he has made me dwell in darkness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:3">like the dead of old. <verse eid="PSA 143:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 143:4"/>So my spirit through me has grown weak, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:4"><char style="add">and</char> within me my heart is desolate. <verse eid="PSA 143:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 143:5"/>I remember the days of antiquity; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:5">I have meditated on all Your deeds; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:5">I muse on the work of Your hands. <verse eid="PSA 143:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 143:6"/>I spread out my hands to You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:6">my soul <char style="add">is</char> like a land exhausted for You. </para>

<para style="qs" vid="PSA 143:6">Selah <verse eid="PSA 143:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 143:7"/>Hurry to answer me, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:7">my spirit fails! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 143:7">Do not hide Your face from me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:7">or I will be likened with those going down <char style="add">to</char> the Pit. <verse eid="PSA 143:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 143:8"/>Cause me to hear Your loving devotion in the morning, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:8">for in You do I trust; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 143:8">make me to know the way in which I should walk, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:8">for to You I lift up my soul. <verse eid="PSA 143:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 143:9"/>Deliver me from my enemies, O YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:9">to You I have fled for refuge.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">143.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> LXX and one Hebrew manuscript; most Hebrew manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in You I have taken cover</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 143:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 143:10"/>Teach me to do Your will, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:10">for You <char style="add">are</char> my God; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 143:10">May Your good Spirit, lead me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:10">into the land of uprightness. <verse eid="PSA 143:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 143:11"/>For the sake of Your name, O YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:11">revive me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 143:11">in Your righteousness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:11">bring forth my soul from distress. <verse eid="PSA 143:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 143:12"/>And in Your loving devotion, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:12">may You cut off my enemies </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 143:12">and destroy all afflicting my soul! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 143:12">For I <char style="add">am</char> Your servant. <verse eid="PSA 143:12"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 143"/>

<chapter number="144" style="c" sid="PSA 144"/>

<para style="s">Blessed Be Yahweh, My Rock</para>

<para style="s">Of David.</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 144:1"/> Blessed <char style="add">be</char> YHWH, my Rock, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:1">the One training my hands for war, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:1">my fingers for battle— <verse eid="PSA 144:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 144:2"/>my steadfast One and my fortress, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:2">my tower and my deliverer—for me; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 144:2">my shield in whom I take refuge, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:2">the One subduing the peoples<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">144.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Many Hebrew manuscripts, DSS, Syriac; most Hebrew manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">my people</char></note> under me. <verse eid="PSA 144:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 144:3"/>O YHWH, what <char style="add">is</char> man that You take knowledge of him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:3">the son of man that You think of him? <verse eid="PSA 144:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 144:4"/>Man is like a breath; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:4">his days <char style="add">are</char> like a shadow passing by. <verse eid="PSA 144:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 144:5"/>O YHWH, bend Your heavens and come down! </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:5">Touch the mountains, that they may smoke! <verse eid="PSA 144:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 144:6"/>Flash lightning and scatter them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:6">send forth Your arrows and rout them! <verse eid="PSA 144:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 144:7"/>Stretch out Your hand from on high; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:7">release me and deliver me from the great waters, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:7">from the hand of sons of a foreigner, <verse eid="PSA 144:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 144:8"/>whose mouth has spoken emptiness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:8">and their right hand <char style="add">is</char> a right hand of falsehood. <verse eid="PSA 144:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 144:9"/>O God, let me sing a new song to You; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:9">on a harp of ten strings I will make music to You— <verse eid="PSA 144:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 144:10"/>the One giving salvation to kings, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:10">the One releasing David His servant from the sword of evil. <verse eid="PSA 144:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 144:11"/>May You release me and snatch me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:11">from the hand of the sons of a foreigner, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 144:11">whose mouth speaks emptiness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:11">and their right hand <char style="add">is</char> a right hand of deception. <verse eid="PSA 144:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 144:12"/>That our sons <char style="add">may be</char> as plants </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:12">grown up in their youth, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 144:12">our daughters like corner pillars, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:12">carved <char style="add">for</char> the pattern of the palace. <verse eid="PSA 144:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 144:13"/>Our granaries full, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:13">bringing out from kind to kind, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 144:13">our flocks producing thousands, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:13">being myriads in our fields, <verse eid="PSA 144:13"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 144:14"/>our oxen carrying. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 144:14">Let there be no breach, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:14">and no going forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:14">and no an outcry in our wide streets. <verse eid="PSA 144:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 144:15"/>Blessed <char style="add">are</char> the people for whom <char style="add">is</char> thus; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 144:15">blessed <char style="add">are</char> the people for whom YHWH <char style="add">is</char> God! <verse eid="PSA 144:15"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 144"/>

<chapter number="145" style="c" sid="PSA 145"/>

<para style="s">I Will Exalt You, My God and King</para>

<para style="s">A Psalm of David.†</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 145:1"/> I will lift You high, my God, the King, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:1">and I will bless Your name forever and ever! <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">145.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> This psalm is an acrostic poem, each verse beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.</char></note><verse eid="PSA 145:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 145:2"/>With every day, I will bless You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:2">and I will praise Your name, forever and ever! <verse eid="PSA 145:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 145:3"/>Great <char style="add">is</char> YHWH and to be praised greatly, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:3">and of His greatness there is no searching out. <verse eid="PSA 145:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 145:4"/>Generation to generation will commend Your works, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:4">and Your mighty acts they will declare. <verse eid="PSA 145:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 145:5"/>The splendor of the glory of Your majesty, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:5">and words of Your wonders I will put forth. <verse eid="PSA 145:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 145:6"/>And the strength of Your fearful acts they will speak, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:6">and Your greatness I will recount. <verse eid="PSA 145:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 145:7"/>The memory of the abundance of Your goodness they will pour forth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:7">and Your righteousness they will sing out. <verse eid="PSA 145:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 145:8"/>Gracious and compassionate <char style="add">is</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:8">slow to anger and great in loving devotion. <verse eid="PSA 145:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 145:9"/>Good <char style="add">is</char> YHWH to all, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:9">and His mercies <char style="add">are</char> upon all His works. <verse eid="PSA 145:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 145:10"/>O YHWH, all Your works will give You thanks, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:10">and Your holy ones will bless You. <verse eid="PSA 145:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 145:11"/>The glory of Your kingdom they will speak, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:11">and Your might they will declare, <verse eid="PSA 145:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 145:12"/>to make known to the sons of man His mighty <char style="add">deeds</char>, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:12">and the glory of the majesty of His kingdom. <verse eid="PSA 145:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 145:13"/>Your kingdom <char style="add">is</char> a kingdom of all ages, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:13">and Your dominion <char style="add">is</char> in every generation and generation.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">145.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The final two lines are supplied by one MT manuscript, LXX, Syriac, and DSS.</char></note></para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 145:13">Yahweh is faithful in all His words </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:13">and kind in all His actions. <verse eid="PSA 145:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 145:14"/>YHWH is upholding all those falling, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:14">and raising up all those bent down low. <verse eid="PSA 145:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 145:15"/>The eyes of all wait for You, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:15">and You give to them their food in its time. <verse eid="PSA 145:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 145:16"/>You open Your hand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:16">and satisfy the desire of every living thing. <verse eid="PSA 145:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 145:17"/>Righteous <char style="add">is</char> YHWH in all His ways, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:17">and kind in all His works. <verse eid="PSA 145:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 145:18"/>Near <char style="add">is</char> YHWH to all those calling on Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:18">to all who call on Him in truth. <verse eid="PSA 145:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 145:19"/>He does the desire of those who fear Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:19">and their cry for help He hears, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:19">and He saves them. <verse eid="PSA 145:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 145:20"/>YHWH is guarding all those loving Him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:20">and all the wicked He will destroy. <verse eid="PSA 145:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 145:21"/>My mouth will declare the praise of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:21">and all flesh blesses the name of His holiness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 145:21">forever and ever! <verse eid="PSA 145:21"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 145"/>

<chapter number="146" style="c" sid="PSA 146"/>

<para style="s">Praise Yahweh, O My Soul</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 146:1"/>Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">146.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 10</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 146:1">Praise, O my soul, YHWH! <verse eid="PSA 146:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 146:2"/>I will praise YHWH during my life; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 146:2">I will sing praises to my God while I exist. <verse eid="PSA 146:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 146:3"/>Do not put your⁺ trust in princes—in a son of man, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 146:3">for in him <char style="add">is</char> no deliverance. <verse eid="PSA 146:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 146:4"/>His spirit goes forth, he returns to his earth; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 146:4">on that day his plans perish. <verse eid="PSA 146:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 146:5"/>Blessed is he whose help is the God of Jacob; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 146:5">his hope <char style="add">is</char> upon YHWH his God, <verse eid="PSA 146:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 146:6"/>maker of the heavens and the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 146:6">the sea and all that <char style="add">is</char> in them, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 146:6">the One guarding truth forever, <verse eid="PSA 146:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 146:7"/>doing justice for the oppressed, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 146:7">giving bread to the hungry. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 146:7">YHWH <char style="add">is</char> the One freeing those who are bound; <verse eid="PSA 146:7"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 146:8"/>YHWH opens the eyes of the blind; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 146:8">YHWH raises up those bent down; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 146:8">YHWH loves the righteous ones; <verse eid="PSA 146:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 146:9"/>YHWH guards the sojourners; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 146:9">the fatherless and widow He sustains, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 146:9">and the way of the wicked He overturns. <verse eid="PSA 146:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 146:10"/>YHWH reigns forever—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 146:10">Your God, O Zion, from generation and generation! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 146:10">Praise YAH! <verse eid="PSA 146:10"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 146"/>

<chapter number="147" style="c" sid="PSA 147"/>

<para style="s">It Is Good to Sing Praises</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 147:1"/>Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">147.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 20</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 147:1">For <char style="add">it is</char> good to praise our God—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:1">how pleasant <char style="add">and</char> beautiful <char style="add">is</char> praise! <verse eid="PSA 147:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 147:2"/>The One building up Jerusalem <char style="add">is</char> YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:2"><char style="add">and</char> He gathers together the exiles of Israel, <verse eid="PSA 147:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 147:3"/>giving healing to the broken of heart, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:3">and binding up their wounds, <verse eid="PSA 147:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 147:4"/>Appointing the number of the stars—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:4">for all of them He calls by names. <verse eid="PSA 147:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 147:5"/>Great <char style="add">is</char> our Lord, and abundant in power; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:5">of His understanding there is no numbering! <verse eid="PSA 147:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 147:6"/>YHWH restores the humble; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:6">He casts down the wicked to the ground. <verse eid="PSA 147:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 147:7"/>Sing to YHWH with thanksgiving; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:7">make music to our God on the harp, <verse eid="PSA 147:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 147:8"/><char style="add">to</char> the One covering the heavens with clouds, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:8">the One preparing rain for the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:8">the One making grass sprout on the hills, <verse eid="PSA 147:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 147:9"/>giving to the beast its food, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:9"><char style="add">and</char> to the young of the ravens that call out. <verse eid="PSA 147:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 147:10"/>He does not delight in the strength of the horse, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:10">and not in the legs of the man does He take pleasure. <verse eid="PSA 147:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 147:11"/>YHWH is pleased with those who fear him, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:11">those hoping in His loving devotion. <verse eid="PSA 147:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 147:12"/>Exalt, O Jerusalem, YHWH; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:12">praise your God, O Zion! <verse eid="PSA 147:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 147:13"/>For He has strengthened the bars of your gates; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:13">He has blessed your sons within you. <verse eid="PSA 147:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 147:14"/>The One making peace <char style="add">for</char> your border, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:14">He satisfies you with the fat of wheat. <verse eid="PSA 147:14"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 147:15"/>The One sending forth His utterance <char style="add">to</char> the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:15">how swiftly His word runs! <verse eid="PSA 147:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 147:16"/>The One giving snow like wool, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:16">He scatters the frost like ashes, <verse eid="PSA 147:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 147:17"/>casting forth His hail like morsels;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">147.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">like crumbs</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">like pebbles</char></note> </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:17">before the face of His cold, who can stand? <verse eid="PSA 147:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 147:18"/>He sends out His word and melts them; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:18">His wind he makes blow, <char style="add">and</char> the waters flow. <verse eid="PSA 147:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 147:19"/>He declares His words to Jacob, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:19">His statutes and His judgments to Israel. <verse eid="PSA 147:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 147:20"/>He has not done so for any nation; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 147:20">and His judgments they have not known.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">147.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> MT; DSS and LXX </char><char style="fq" closed="false">His judgments He has not made known to them</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 147:20">Praise YAH! <verse eid="PSA 147:20"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 147"/>

<chapter number="148" style="c" sid="PSA 148"/>

<para style="s">Praise Yahweh from the Heavens</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 148:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 33:1–22</char></note>Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">148.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 14</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 148:1">Praise YHWH from the heavens; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:1">praise Him in the heights!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">148.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Matthew 21:9, Mark 11:10, and Luke 19:38.</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 148:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 148:2"/>Praise Him, all His angels; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:2">praise Him, all His hosts! <verse eid="PSA 148:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 148:3"/>Praise Him, O sun and moon; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:3">praise Him, all stars of light! <verse eid="PSA 148:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 148:4"/>Praise Him, O heavens of heavens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:4">and waters that <char style="add">are</char> above the heavens! <verse eid="PSA 148:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 148:5"/>Let them praise the name of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:5">for He commanded, and they were created. <verse eid="PSA 148:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 148:6"/>And He established them for ever to forever; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:6">He made a decree, and it shall not pass away. <verse eid="PSA 148:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 148:7"/>Praise YHWH from the earth, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:7">sea creatures and all the depths; <verse eid="PSA 148:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 148:8"/>fire and hail, snow and clouds, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:8">wind of storm—doing His word; <verse eid="PSA 148:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 148:9"/>mountains and all hills, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:9">trees of fruit and all cedars; <verse eid="PSA 148:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 148:10"/>the beast and all cattle, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:10">the creeping thing and bird of wing; <verse eid="PSA 148:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 148:11"/>kings of the earth and all peoples, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:11">princes and all judges of the earth; <verse eid="PSA 148:11"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 148:12"/>young men and also maidens, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:12">old with young: <verse eid="PSA 148:12"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 148:13"/>Let them praise the name of YHWH, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:13">for His name alone is exalted; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:13">His splendor above the earth and the heavens! <verse eid="PSA 148:13"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 148:14"/>For He has raised up the horn of His people, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:14">the praise from all His saints, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 148:14">from the sons of Israel, a people near to Him. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 148:14">Praise YAH! <verse eid="PSA 148:14"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 148"/>

<chapter number="149" style="c" sid="PSA 149"/>

<para style="s">Sing to Yahweh a New Song</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 149:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Isaiah 42:10–17</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Psalm 98:1–9</char></note>Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">149.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 9</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 149:1">Sing to YHWH a new song—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 149:1">His praise in the assembly of the holy ones! <verse eid="PSA 149:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 149:2"/>Let Israel rejoice in his Maker; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 149:2">let the sons of Zion rejoice in their King! <verse eid="PSA 149:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 149:3"/>Let them praise His name with dancing; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 149:3">with tambourine and harp let them make music to Him! <verse eid="PSA 149:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 149:4"/>For YHWH delights in His people; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 149:4">He adorns the humble with salvation. <verse eid="PSA 149:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 149:5"/>Let the holy ones exult in <char style="add">His</char> glory; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 149:5">let them sing for joy upon their beds. <verse eid="PSA 149:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 149:6"/>Let the high praises of God <char style="add">be</char> in their throat, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 149:6">and a two-edged sword in their hand, <verse eid="PSA 149:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 149:7"/>to execute vengeance on the nations, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 149:7">and punishments against the peoples, <verse eid="PSA 149:7"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 149:8"/>to bind their kings with chains, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 149:8">and their nobles with shackles of iron, <verse eid="PSA 149:8"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 149:9"/>to execute against them the judgment written—</para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 149:9">it <char style="add">is</char> an honor for all His holy ones. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 149:9">Praise YAH! <verse eid="PSA 149:9"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 149"/>

<chapter number="150" style="c" sid="PSA 150"/>

<para style="s">Let Everything That Has Breath Praise Yahweh</para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 150:1"/>Hallelu YAH!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">150.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hallelu YAH</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> means </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Praise YHWH</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 6</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 150:1">Praise God in His sanctuary; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 150:1">praise Him in His mighty expanse!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">150.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in His mighty heavens</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the firmament of His might</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see also Genesis 1:6–8.</char></note> <verse eid="PSA 150:1"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 150:2"/>Praise Him for His mighty acts; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 150:2">praise Him according to the abundance of His greatness! <verse eid="PSA 150:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 150:3"/>Praise Him with the blast of the shofar; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 150:3">praise Him with the harp and lyre! <verse eid="PSA 150:3"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 150:4"/>Praise Him with tambourine and dancing; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 150:4">praise Him with strings and flute! <verse eid="PSA 150:4"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 150:5"/>Praise Him with cymbals sounding; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="PSA 150:5">praise Him with cymbals shouting! <verse eid="PSA 150:5"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 150:6"/>Let everything that <char style="add">has</char> breath praise YAH! </para>

<para style="q1" vid="PSA 150:6">Praise YAH! <verse eid="PSA 150:6"/></para>

<chapter eid="PSA 150"/>

</usx>
